erge: { log: \"Zero applicable lanes -- nothing to converge. Proceeding to synthesis.\", proceed_to: phase_synthesis }\n\n  Line 431:   phase_synthesis:\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/commands/deep/assets/compiled/deep-review.contract.md:\n  Line 225: | `config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir` | N | internal flag `--fanout-lineage-artifact-dir=PATH` or marker `config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir` | none | N |\n\n  Line 277:    |-- --fanout-lineage-artifact-dir=PATH -> config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir = PATH (internal single-lineage command invocation only)\n\n  Line 386: - `config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir` when present\n\n  Line 413:   - \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir\"\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-model-benchmark-confirm.yaml:\n  Line 71:   trigger: \"At workflow START, before phase_init\"\n\n  Line 80:     if_no_context: \"Proceed to phase_init without delay\"\n\n  Line 126:   phase_init:\n\n  Line 219:   phase_synthesis:\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-agent-improvement-auto.yaml:\n  Line 65:   trigger: \"At workflow START, before phase_init\"\n\n  Line 74:     if_no_context: \"Proceed to phase_init without delay\"\n\n  Line 117:   phase_init:\n\n  Line 261:   phase_synthesis:\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-ai-council-auto.yaml:\n  Line 31:   trigger: \"At workflow START, before phase_init\"\n\n  Line 146:   phase_synthesis:\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt:\n  Line 187: Applies to both `:auto` and `:confirm`. Once `max_iterations` is resolved (the `:auto` three-tier flow, or the `:confirm` consolidated prompt above) and before `phase_init` begins, compute and present the worst-case cumulative dispatch cost for this run:\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-confirm.yaml:\n  Line 43:   trigger: \"At workflow START, before phase_init\"\n\n  Line 87:   # step_resolve_artifact_root plus the shared resolver, so root specs keep\n\n  Line 118:   step_resolve_artifact_root:\n\n  Line 121:     branch_on: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir\"\n\n  Line 124:         artifact_dir: \"{config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir}\"\n\n  Line 125:         artifact_root_dir: \"{config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir}\"\n\n  Line 127:         artifact_archive_root: \"{config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir}/_archive\"\n\n  Line 137:     description: \"Spawn fan-out lineages; skip and proceed to phase_init normally when single-executor\"\n\n  Line 142:       After all lineages complete, jump directly to phase_synthesis — skip phase_init and\n\n  Line 143:       phase_main_loop entirely (those are the single-executor path). The merge step in\n\n  Line 144:       phase_synthesis will consolidate results across all lineages.\n\n  Line 167:               config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir: {artifact_dir}/lineages/{lineage.label}\n\n  Line 176:   phase_init:\n\n  Line 280:           skip_to: phase_synthesis\n\n  Line 1332:   phase_synthesis:\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml:\n  Line 39:   config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir: \"[optional internal path] - Fan-out lineage artifact override for command-owned single-lineage execution.\"\n\n  Line 45:   trigger: \"At workflow START, before phase_init\"\n\n  Line 89:   # step_resolve_artifact_root plus the shared resolver, so root specs keep\n\n  Line 120:   step_resolve_artifact_root:\n\n  Line 123:     branch_on: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir\"\n\n  Line 126:         artifact_dir: \"{config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir}\"\n\n  Line 127:         artifact_root_dir: \"{config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir}\"\n\n  Line 129:         artifact_archive_root: \"{config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir}/_archive\"\n\n  Line 140:     branch_on: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir\"\n\n  Line 166:     description: \"Spawn fan-out lineages; skip and proceed to phase_init normally when single-executor\"\n\n  Line 176:       deep/review command surface with config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir so the LEAF\n\n  Line 179:       After all lineages complete, jump directly to phase_synthesis — skip phase_init and\n\n  Line 180:       phase_main_loop entirely (those are the single-executor path). The merge step in\n\n  Line 181:       phase_synthesis will consolidate results across all lineages.\n\n  Line 200:   phase_init:\n\n  Line 313:           skip_to: phase_synthesis\n\n  Line 909:                   skip_to: phase_synthesis\n\n  Line 912:               skip_to: phase_synthesis\n\n  Line 915:             skip_to: phase_synthesis\n\n  Line 1673:   phase_synthesis:\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-presentation.txt:\n  Line 82: | `config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir` | N | internal flag `--fanout-lineage-artifact-dir=PATH` or marker `config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir` | none | N |\n\n  Line 126:    |-- --fanout-lineage-artifact-dir=PATH -> config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir = PATH (internal single-lineage command invocation only)\n\n  Line 235: - `config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir` when present\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-confirm.yaml:\n  Line 69:   trigger: \"At workflow START, before phase_init\"\n\n  Line 113:   # step_resolve_artifact_root plus the shared resolver, so root specs keep\n\n  Line 141:   step_resolve_artifact_root:\n\n  Line 144:     branch_on: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir\"\n\n  Line 147:         artifact_dir: \"{config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir}\"\n\n  Line 148:         artifact_root_dir: \"{config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir}\"\n\n  Line 150:         artifact_archive_root: \"{config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir}/_archive\"\n\n  Line 160:     description: \"Spawn fan-out lineages; skip and proceed to phase_init normally when single-executor\"\n\n\n(Results truncated. Consider using a more specific path or pattern.)","metadata":{"matches":100,"truncated":true},"title":"phase_init|phase_main_loop|phase_synthesis|step_resolve_artifact_root|fanout_lineage_artifact_dir","time":{"start":1785758067596,"end":1785758067644}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_028da9b5cab13855016a7081732b548191b9d5d9f6da45a2ee"}},"id":"prt_fc779ab87001RN93gejxz6gcZy","sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","messageID":"msg_fc779745a001TxXig8wd9BQFim"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785758067686,"sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_PopkBp4xQ5XZX6l7TK1XmYHs","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/convergence/convergence-signals.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/convergence/convergence-signals.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: Convergence Signals Reference\n3: description: Signal definitions, scoring rules, and reports for deep-research convergence.\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"research convergence signals\"\n6:   - \"research new info ratio\"\n7:   - \"research stuck count\"\n8:   - \"mad noise floor\"\n9:   - \"question entropy\"\n10:   - \"research composite score\"\n11:   - \"convergence threshold tuning\"\n12: importance_tier: normal\n13: contextType: implementation\n14: version: 1.14.0.3\n15: ---\n16: \n17: # Convergence Signals Reference\n18: \n19: This reference defines the live deep-research convergence signals. The compact stop contract lives in `convergence.md`.\n20: \n21: ---\n22: \n23: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n24: \n25: ### Purpose\n26: \n27: Define the live convergence signals, scoring rules, threshold semantics, and reporting shape used by deep-research loops.\n28: \n29: ### When to Use\n30: \n31: Load this reference when calculating `newInfoRatio`, explaining a composite STOP vote, debugging stuck counts, or validating convergence dashboards.\n32: \n33: ### Core Principle\n34: \n35: Signals nominate STOP; legal-stop and graph gates authorize or block it.\n36: \n37: ---\n38: \n39: ## 2. SIGNAL MODEL\n40: \n41: The live model uses three weighted signals and normalizes by the weight of the signals that have enough data to run.\n42: \n43: | Signal | Weight | Requires | STOP Vote |\n44: |--------|--------|----------|-----------|\n45: | Rolling Average | `0.30` | 3 evidence iterations | Average of last 3 `newInfoRatio` values is below `convergenceThreshold` |\n46: | MAD Noise Floor | `0.35` | 4 evidence iterations | Latest `newInfoRatio` is at or below `MAD * 1.4826` |\n47: | Question Entropy | `0.35` | At least 1 key question | Evidence-backed coverage is at least `0.85` |\n48: \n49: `thought` iterations are excluded from rolling average, MAD, and stuck counting because they are analytical-only. `insight` iterations are included in convergence signals but do not count as stuck.\n50: \n51: ---\n52: \n53: ## 3. NEW INFO RATIO\n54: \n55: `newInfoRatio` measures how much an iteration added relative to accumulated research knowledge.\n56: \n57: | Ratio | Meaning |\n58: |-------|---------|\n59: | `1.0` | Mostly new findings or first broad pass |\n60: | `0.7` | Several new findings plus some refinements |\n61: | `0.5` | Mixed new and repeated material |\n62: | `0.2` | Mostly confirmation or marginal novelty |\n63: | `0.0` | No new information |\n64: \n65: Agent assessment guidance:\n66: \n67: - Fully new finding: count as `1.0`.\n68: - Refinement of known finding: count as partial novelty.\n69: - Ruled-out direction: count as valuable negative knowledge when it removes a plausible path.\n70: - Tentative single-source finding: contribute less than verified or multi-source evidence.\n71: - Simplicity bonus may add up to `0.10`, capped at `1.0`, when an iteration materially reduces the search space.\n72: \n73: Every iteration record should include `newInfoRatio` and `noveltyJustification`; see `../state/state-jsonl.md`.\n74: \n75: ---\n76: \n77: ## 4. STUCK COUNT\n78: \n79: `stuckCount` is consecutive no-progress evidence iterations.\n80: \n81: ```text\n82: for each iteration from newest to oldest:\n83:   skip status == \"thought\"\n84:   stop counting when status == \"insight\"\n85:   count if status == \"stuck\" or newInfoRatio <= noProgressThreshold\n86:   stop counting on any productive evidence iteration\n87: ```\n88: \n89: Default threshold behavior:\n90: \n91: - `stuckThreshold`: `3`\n92: - `noProgressThreshold`: implementation default aligned with the workflow's recovery check\n93: - Recovery route: `convergence-recovery.md`\n94: \n95: ---\n96: \n97: ## 5. ROLLING AVERAGE\n98: \n99: Rolling average uses the last three evidence iterations.\n100: \n101: ```text\n102: evidenceIterations = iterations where status != \"thought\"\n103: recent = last 3 evidenceIterations\n104: rollingAvg = mean(recent.newInfoRatio)\n105: rollingStop = rollingAvg < convergenceThreshold\n106: ```\n107: \n108: This signal is unavailable before three evidence iterations. The composite vote normalizes over active signals, so early runs can still use question coverage without pretending the rolling signal exists.\n109: \n110: ---\n111: \n112: ## 6. MAD NOISE FLOOR\n113: \n114: MAD compares the latest ratio against the noise floor in the accumulated evidence ratios.\n115: \n116: ```text\n117: ratios = evidenceIterations.newInfoRatio\n118: medianRatio = median(ratios)\n119: mad = median(abs(ratio - medianRatio) for ratio in ratios)\n120: noiseFloor = mad * 1.4826\n121: madStop = latestEvidenceRatio <= noiseFloor\n122: ```\n123: \n124: Interpretation:\n125: \n126: | Condition | Meaning |\n127: |-----------|---------|\n128: | Latest ratio above floor | Signal still exceeds observed noise |\n129: | Latest ratio within floor | New findings may be indistinguishable from noise |\n130: | Very high floor | Iteration quality is unstable; narrow the focus before trusting STOP |\n131: \n132: ---\n133: \n134: ## 7. QUESTION ENTROPY\n135: \n136: Question entropy is evidence-backed key-question coverage.\n137: \n138: ```text\n139: answered = count(keyQuestions with evidence-backed answers)\n140: total = count(keyQuestions)\n141: coverage = answered / total\n142: entropyStop = coverage >= 0.85\n143: ```\n144: \n145: Tentative-only findings do not satisfy evidence-backed coverage. Graph events may add extra STOP blockers when graph coverage disagrees with inline question coverage; see `convergence-graph.md`.\n146: \n147: ---\n148: \n149: ## 8. COMPOSITE SCORE\n150: \n151: ```text\n152: activeSignals = signals with enough data\n153: stopScore = sum(signal.weight for active STOP votes) / sum(active signal weights)\n154: stopCandidate = stopScore > 0.60\n155: ```\n156: \n157: The score nominates STOP only. `convergence.md` defines the legal-stop gates that decide whether the loop may exit.\n158: \n159: ---\n160: \n161: ## 9. REPORTING\n162: \n163: Every completed loop should report:\n164: \n165: ```text\n166: CONVERGENCE REPORT\n167: ------------------\n168: Stop reason: converged | maxIterationsReached | userPaused | stuckRecovery | error\n169: Iterations completed: N\n170: Questions answered: X/Y\n171: Average newInfoRatio trend: [...]\n172: Composite stop score: 0.XX\n173: Signals:\n174:   Rolling Avg (w=0.30): STOP|CONTINUE\n175:   MAD Noise (w=0.35): STOP|CONTINUE\n176:   Entropy (w=0.35): STOP|CONTINUE\n177: Legal-stop gates: pass|blocked\n178: Graph gates: pass|blocked|not_applicable\n179: ```\n180: \n181: Dashboard and registry fields derived from these signals are documented in `../state/state-reducer-registry.md`.\n182: \n183: ---\n184: \n185: ## 10. THRESHOLD TUNING\n186: \n187: | Goal | Adjustment |\n188: |------|------------|\n189: | Deeper research | Lower `convergenceThreshold`, raise `maxIterations` |\n190: | Faster completion | Raise `convergenceThreshold`, lower `maxIterations` |\n191: | More stuck recovery | Lower `stuckThreshold` cautiously |\n192: | Fewer false stops | Keep legal-stop and graph gates enabled |\n193: \n194: Optimizer-managed fields are described in `convergence-reference-only.md`. Optimizer proposals are advisory and do not override locked stop-contract fields.\n\n(End of file - total 194 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: Convergence Signals Reference\ndescription: Signal definitions, scoring rules, and reports for deep-research convergence.\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"research convergence signals\"\n  - \"research new info ratio\"\n  - \"research stuck count\"\n  - \"mad noise floor\"\n  - \"question entropy\"\n  - \"research composite score\"\n  - \"convergence threshold tuning\"\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.14.0.3\n---\n\n# Convergence Signals Reference\n\nThis reference defines the live deep-research convergence signals. The compact stop contract lives in `convergence.md`.\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/convergence/convergence-signals.md","text":"---\ntitle: Convergence Signals Reference\ndescription: Signal definitions, scoring rules, and reports for deep-research convergence.\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"research convergence signals\"\n  - \"research new info ratio\"\n  - \"research stuck count\"\n  - \"mad noise floor\"\n  - \"question entropy\"\n  - \"research composite score\"\n  - \"convergence threshold tuning\"\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.14.0.3\n---\n\n# Convergence Signals Reference\n\nThis reference defines the live deep-research convergence signals. The compact stop contract lives in `convergence.md`.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Purpose\n\nDefine the live convergence signals, scoring rules, threshold semantics, and reporting shape used by deep-research loops.\n\n### When to Use\n\nLoad this reference when calculating `newInfoRatio`, explaining a composite STOP vote, debugging stuck counts, or validating convergence dashboards.\n\n### Core Principle\n\nSignals nominate STOP; legal-stop and graph gates authorize or block it.\n\n---\n\n## 2. SIGNAL MODEL\n\nThe live model uses three weighted signals and normalizes by the weight of the signals that have enough data to run.\n\n| Signal | Weight | Requires | STOP Vote |\n|--------|--------|----------|-----------|\n| Rolling Average | `0.30` | 3 evidence iterations | Average of last 3 `newInfoRatio` values is below `convergenceThreshold` |\n| MAD Noise Floor | `0.35` | 4 evidence iterations | Latest `newInfoRatio` is at or below `MAD * 1.4826` |\n| Question Entropy | `0.35` | At least 1 key question | Evidence-backed coverage is at least `0.85` |\n\n`thought` iterations are excluded from rolling average, MAD, and stuck counting because they are analytical-only. `insight` iterations are included in convergence signals but do not count as stuck.\n\n---\n\n## 3. NEW INFO RATIO\n\n`newInfoRatio` measures how much an iteration added relative to accumulated research knowledge.\n\n| Ratio | Meaning |\n|-------|---------|\n| `1.0` | Mostly new findings or first broad pass |\n| `0.7` | Several new findings plus some refinements |\n| `0.5` | Mixed new and repeated material |\n| `0.2` | Mostly confirmation or marginal novelty |\n| `0.0` | No new information |\n\nAgent assessment guidance:\n\n- Fully new finding: count as `1.0`.\n- Refinement of known finding: count as partial novelty.\n- Ruled-out direction: count as valuable negative knowledge when it removes a plausible path.\n- Tentative single-source finding: contribute less than verified or multi-source evidence.\n- Simplicity bonus may add up to `0.10`, capped at `1.0`, when an iteration materially reduces the search space.\n\nEvery iteration record should include `newInfoRatio` and `noveltyJustification`; see `../state/state-jsonl.md`.\n\n---\n\n## 4. STUCK COUNT\n\n`stuckCount` is consecutive no-progress evidence iterations.\n\n```text\nfor each iteration from newest to oldest:\n  skip status == \"thought\"\n  stop counting when status == \"insight\"\n  count if status == \"stuck\" or newInfoRatio <= noProgressThreshold\n  stop counting on any productive evidence iteration\n```\n\nDefault threshold behavior:\n\n- `stuckThreshold`: `3`\n- `noProgressThreshold`: implementation default aligned with the workflow's recovery check\n- Recovery route: `convergence-recovery.md`\n\n---\n\n## 5. ROLLING AVERAGE\n\nRolling average uses the last three evidence iterations.\n\n```text\nevidenceIterations = iterations where status != \"thought\"\nrecent = last 3 evidenceIterations\nrollingAvg = mean(recent.newInfoRatio)\nrollingStop = rollingAvg < convergenceThreshold\n```\n\nThis signal is unavailable before three evidence iterations. The composite vote normalizes over active signals, so early runs can still use question coverage without pretending the rolling signal exists.\n\n---\n\n## 6. MAD NOISE FLOOR\n\nMAD compares the latest ratio against the noise floor in the accumulated evidence ratios.\n\n```text\nratios = evidenceIterations.newInfoRatio\nmedianRatio = median(ratios)\nmad = median(abs(ratio - medianRatio) for ratio in ratios)\nnoiseFloor = mad * 1.4826\nmadStop = latestEvidenceRatio <= noiseFloor\n```\n\nInterpretation:\n\n| Condition | Meaning |\n|-----------|---------|\n| Latest ratio above floor | Signal still exceeds observed noise |\n| Latest ratio within floor | New findings may be indistinguishable from noise |\n| Very high floor | Iteration quality is unstable; narrow the focus before trusting STOP |\n\n---\n\n## 7. QUESTION ENTROPY\n\nQuestion entropy is evidence-backed key-question coverage.\n\n```text\nanswered = count(keyQuestions with evidence-backed answers)\ntotal = count(keyQuestions)\ncoverage = answered / total\nentropyStop = coverage >= 0.85\n```\n\nTentative-only findings do not satisfy evidence-backed coverage. Graph events may add extra STOP blockers when graph coverage disagrees with inline question coverage; see `convergence-graph.md`.\n\n---\n\n## 8. COMPOSITE SCORE\n\n```text\nactiveSignals = signals with enough data\nstopScore = sum(signal.weight for active STOP votes) / sum(active signal weights)\nstopCandidate = stopScore > 0.60\n```\n\nThe score nominates STOP only. `convergence.md` defines the legal-stop gates that decide whether the loop may exit.\n\n---\n\n## 9. REPORTING\n\nEvery completed loop should report:\n\n```text\nCONVERGENCE REPORT\n------------------\nStop reason: converged | maxIterationsReached | userPaused | stuckRecovery | error\nIterations completed: N\nQuestions answered: X/Y\nAverage newInfoRatio trend: [...]\nComposite stop score: 0.XX\nSignals:\n  Rolling Avg (w=0.30): STOP|CONTINUE\n  MAD Noise (w=0.35): STOP|CONTINUE\n  Entropy (w=0.35): STOP|CONTINUE\nLegal-stop gates: pass|blocked\nGraph gates: pass|blocked|not_applicable\n```\n\nDashboard and registry fields derived from these signals are documented in `../state/state-reducer-registry.md`.\n\n---\n\n## 10. THRESHOLD TUNING\n\n| Goal | Adjustment |\n|------|------------|\n| Deeper research | Lower `convergenceThreshold`, raise `maxIterations` |\n| Faster completion | Raise `convergenceThreshold`, lower `maxIterations` |\n| More stuck recovery | Lower `stuckThreshold` cautiously |\n| Fewer false stops | Keep legal-stop and graph gates enabled |\n\nOptimizer-managed fields are described in `convergence-reference-only.md`. Optimizer proposals are advisory and do not override locked stop-contract fields.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":194,"totalLines":194,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/convergence/convergence-signals.md","time":{"start":1785758067572,"end":1785758067679}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_028da9b5cab13855016a7081732b408191815b9e3f4d07b434"}},"id":"prt_fc779ab70001nvkPDkFo168GxK","sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","messageID":"msg_fc779745a001TxXig8wd9BQFim"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785758067707,"sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_N9St1gz2o1WAw22kLGNC1DTs","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/state/state-reducer-registry.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/state/state-reducer-registry.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: Deep Research Reducer And Registry Reference\n3: description: Reducer ownership, findings registry schema, validation, fault tolerance, and reconstruction rules.\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"research reducer registry\"\n6:   - \"research findings registry\"\n7:   - \"reducer ownership contract\"\n8:   - \"research registry fingerprint\"\n9:   - \"reducer fault tolerance\"\n10:   - \"research dashboard derivation\"\n11: importance_tier: normal\n12: contextType: implementation\n13: version: 1.14.0.2\n14: ---\n15: \n16: # Deep Research Reducer And Registry Reference\n17: \n18: The reducer turns append-only iteration state into synchronized strategy, registry, dashboard, and synthesis metadata. It is the source of truth for derived packet state.\n19: \n20: ---\n21: \n22: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n23: \n24: ### Purpose\n25: \n26: Define reducer ownership, findings registry shape, validation behavior, fault tolerance, file protection, dashboard derivation, and legacy aliases.\n27: \n28: ### When to Use\n29: \n30: Load this reference when rebuilding derived state, validating registry/dashboard outputs, or deciding whether a file is agent-owned or reducer-owned.\n31: \n32: ### Core Principle\n33: \n34: The reducer owns derived state. Manual edits to reducer-managed outputs are temporary and may be overwritten.\n35: \n36: ---\n37: \n38: ## 2. REDUCER CONTRACT\n39: \n40: The workflow reducer:\n41: \n42: - reads `deep-research-state.jsonl`, per-iteration deltas, strategy, and iteration markdown;\n43: - reads `inbox.jsonl` as immutable question input;\n44: - reads the prior registry as canonical question state when present;\n45: - validates required iteration artifacts;\n46: - updates machine-owned strategy sections;\n47: - regenerates the findings registry;\n48: - regenerates the dashboard;\n49: - records convergence and blocked-stop summaries.\n50: \n51: It must fail closed before writing derived files when JSONL corruption is detected in strict mode.\n52: \n53: ---\n54: \n55: ## 3. FINDINGS REGISTRY\n56: \n57: The canonical registry stores open/resolved questions, findings, ruled-out directions, convergence state, and blocked-stop history.\n58: \n59: ```json\n60: {\n61:   \"openQuestions\": [],\n62:   \"resolvedQuestions\": [],\n63:   \"keyFindings\": [],\n64:   \"ruledOutDirections\": [],\n65:   \"coverageBySources\": {},\n66:   \"convergenceScore\": 0.42,\n67:   \"blockedStopHistory\": [],\n68:   \"graphConvergenceScore\": null,\n69:   \"graphDecision\": null,\n70:   \"graphBlockers\": [],\n71:   \"lastUpdated\": \"2026-05-24T00:00:00Z\"\n72: }\n73: ```\n74: \n75: Question ownership:\n76: \n77: - `inbox.jsonl` is append-only input for external questions.\n78: - The registry is the canonical owner of promoted question text, provenance, and operator decisions.\n79: - The strategy `key-questions` block is a generated projection and is rewritten from registry state on every reduce step.\n80: \n81: When an inbox row targets an existing registry question by promoted question id or inbox id but carries different text, the reducer records a conflict instead of overwriting markdown. Conflict records use `operatorDecision` values of `accepted`, `rejected`, `superseded`, or `needs_decision`; the default unresolved decision is `needs_decision`. The emitted `question_conflict` JSONL event includes both `inboxValue` and `registryValue`.\n82: \n83: The reducer writes the registry to `findings-registry.json`; this is the canonical live name. `deep-research-findings-registry.json` is a legacy read-fallback path only -- the reducer checks it when `findings-registry.json` is absent but never writes to it. New docs should reference `findings-registry.json` and mention the legacy name only when explaining read-compatibility.\n84: \n85: ---\n86: \n87: ## 4. VALIDATION RULES\n88: \n89: Blocking validation:\n90: \n91: - config, state log, and strategy exist before a resume;\n92: - every dispatched iteration produces a non-empty iteration markdown file;\n93: - every dispatched iteration appends a JSONL delta record with required fields;\n94: - JSONL records parse in strict mode;\n95: - reducer-owned outputs refresh after iteration evaluation;\n96: - convergence STOP candidates record gate evidence.\n97: \n98: Post-dispatch failure codes include:\n99: \n100: | Code | Meaning |\n101: |------|---------|\n102: | `iteration_file_missing` | Expected iteration markdown file was not created |\n103: | `iteration_file_empty` | Iteration markdown exists but is empty |\n104: | `jsonl_not_appended` | JSONL state did not receive the iteration record |\n105: | `jsonl_missing_fields` | Required JSONL fields are absent |\n106: | `jsonl_parse_error` | JSONL line is malformed |\n107: \n108: Three consecutive failures route to stuck recovery or escalation.\n109: \n110: ---\n111: \n112: ## 5. FAULT TOLERANCE\n113: \n114: Fault-tolerant reads may skip malformed JSONL lines only in lenient recovery mode. Strict mode stops before derived writes.\n115: \n116: Safe recovery order:\n117: \n118: 1. Preserve the corrupted state file.\n119: 2. Read valid JSONL records.\n120: 3. Reconstruct missing iteration summaries from `iterations/iteration-NNN.md`.\n121: 4. Append explicit reconstructed records.\n122: 5. Regenerate registry and dashboard.\n123: 6. Record the recovery in JSONL.\n124: \n125: Example reconstructed record:\n126: \n127: ```json\n128: {\"type\":\"iteration\",\"run\":3,\"status\":\"reconstructed\",\"focus\":\"extracted focus\",\"findingsCount\":0,\"newInfoRatio\":0.0}\n129: ```\n130: \n131: ---\n132: \n133: ## 6. FILE PROTECTION MAP\n134: \n135: The config may include:\n136: \n137: ```json\n138: {\n139:   \"fileProtection\": {\n140:     \"deep-research-config.json\": \"immutable\",\n141:     \"deep-research-state.jsonl\": \"append-only\",\n142:     \"deep-research-strategy.md\": \"mutable\",\n143:     \"deep-research-dashboard.md\": \"auto-generated\",\n144:     \"findings-registry.json\": \"auto-generated\",\n145:     \"iteration-*.md\": \"write-once\",\n146:     \"research/research.md\": \"mutable\"\n147:   }\n148: }\n149: ```\n150: \n151: Protection is a workflow contract. It documents ownership and supports validation; it is not a substitute for command-level checks.\n152: \n153: ---\n154: \n155: ## 7. DASHBOARD DERIVATION\n156: \n157: Dashboard values are derived from raw state:\n158: \n159: | Dashboard Field | Source |\n160: |-----------------|--------|\n161: | iteration count | JSONL iteration records |\n162: | current status | latest lifecycle or synthesis event |\n163: | convergence trend | `convergenceSignals` |\n164: | blocked stops | registry `blockedStopHistory` |\n165: | graph convergence | registry graph fields |\n166: | next focus | strategy |\n167: \n168: `synthesis_complete` events are authoritative for terminal status when present.\n169: \n170: ---\n171: \n172: ## 8. LEGACY ALIASES\n173: \n174: The workflow may dual-read older names during migration windows, but new writes use canonical `deep-research-*` artifacts. Migration reads should append a migration event that records `legacyPath`, `canonicalPath`, and timestamp.\n\n(End of file - total 174 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: Deep Research Reducer And Registry Reference\ndescription: Reducer ownership, findings registry schema, validation, fault tolerance, and reconstruction rules.\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"research reducer registry\"\n  - \"research findings registry\"\n  - \"reducer ownership contract\"\n  - \"research registry fingerprint\"\n  - \"reducer fault tolerance\"\n  - \"research dashboard derivation\"\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.14.0.2\n---\n\n# Deep Research Reducer And Registry Reference\n\nThe reducer turns append-only iteration state into synchronized strategy, registry, dashboard, and synthesis metadata. It is the source of truth for derived packet state.\n\n---","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/state/state-reducer-registry.md","text":"---\ntitle: Deep Research Reducer And Registry Reference\ndescription: Reducer ownership, findings registry schema, validation, fault tolerance, and reconstruction rules.\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"research reducer registry\"\n  - \"research findings registry\"\n  - \"reducer ownership contract\"\n  - \"research registry fingerprint\"\n  - \"reducer fault tolerance\"\n  - \"research dashboard derivation\"\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.14.0.2\n---\n\n# Deep Research Reducer And Registry Reference\n\nThe reducer turns append-only iteration state into synchronized strategy, registry, dashboard, and synthesis metadata. It is the source of truth for derived packet state.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Purpose\n\nDefine reducer ownership, findings registry shape, validation behavior, fault tolerance, file protection, dashboard derivation, and legacy aliases.\n\n### When to Use\n\nLoad this reference when rebuilding derived state, validating registry/dashboard outputs, or deciding whether a file is agent-owned or reducer-owned.\n\n### Core Principle\n\nThe reducer owns derived state. Manual edits to reducer-managed outputs are temporary and may be overwritten.\n\n---\n\n## 2. REDUCER CONTRACT\n\nThe workflow reducer:\n\n- reads `deep-research-state.jsonl`, per-iteration deltas, strategy, and iteration markdown;\n- reads `inbox.jsonl` as immutable question input;\n- reads the prior registry as canonical question state when present;\n- validates required iteration artifacts;\n- updates machine-owned strategy sections;\n- regenerates the findings registry;\n- regenerates the dashboard;\n- records convergence and blocked-stop summaries.\n\nIt must fail closed before writing derived files when JSONL corruption is detected in strict mode.\n\n---\n\n## 3. FINDINGS REGISTRY\n\nThe canonical registry stores open/resolved questions, findings, ruled-out directions, convergence state, and blocked-stop history.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"openQuestions\": [],\n  \"resolvedQuestions\": [],\n  \"keyFindings\": [],\n  \"ruledOutDirections\": [],\n  \"coverageBySources\": {},\n  \"convergenceScore\": 0.42,\n  \"blockedStopHistory\": [],\n  \"graphConvergenceScore\": null,\n  \"graphDecision\": null,\n  \"graphBlockers\": [],\n  \"lastUpdated\": \"2026-05-24T00:00:00Z\"\n}\n```\n\nQuestion ownership:\n\n- `inbox.jsonl` is append-only input for external questions.\n- The registry is the canonical owner of promoted question text, provenance, and operator decisions.\n- The strategy `key-questions` block is a generated projection and is rewritten from registry state on every reduce step.\n\nWhen an inbox row targets an existing registry question by promoted question id or inbox id but carries different text, the reducer records a conflict instead of overwriting markdown. Conflict records use `operatorDecision` values of `accepted`, `rejected`, `superseded`, or `needs_decision`; the default unresolved decision is `needs_decision`. The emitted `question_conflict` JSONL event includes both `inboxValue` and `registryValue`.\n\nThe reducer writes the registry to `findings-registry.json`; this is the canonical live name. `deep-research-findings-registry.json` is a legacy read-fallback path only -- the reducer checks it when `findings-registry.json` is absent but never writes to it. New docs should reference `findings-registry.json` and mention the legacy name only when explaining read-compatibility.\n\n---\n\n## 4. VALIDATION RULES\n\nBlocking validation:\n\n- config, state log, and strategy exist before a resume;\n- every dispatched iteration produces a non-empty iteration markdown file;\n- every dispatched iteration appends a JSONL delta record with required fields;\n- JSONL records parse in strict mode;\n- reducer-owned outputs refresh after iteration evaluation;\n- convergence STOP candidates record gate evidence.\n\nPost-dispatch failure codes include:\n\n| Code | Meaning |\n|------|---------|\n| `iteration_file_missing` | Expected iteration markdown file was not created |\n| `iteration_file_empty` | Iteration markdown exists but is empty |\n| `jsonl_not_appended` | JSONL state did not receive the iteration record |\n| `jsonl_missing_fields` | Required JSONL fields are absent |\n| `jsonl_parse_error` | JSONL line is malformed |\n\nThree consecutive failures route to stuck recovery or escalation.\n\n---\n\n## 5. FAULT TOLERANCE\n\nFault-tolerant reads may skip malformed JSONL lines only in lenient recovery mode. Strict mode stops before derived writes.\n\nSafe recovery order:\n\n1. Preserve the corrupted state file.\n2. Read valid JSONL records.\n3. Reconstruct missing iteration summaries from `iterations/iteration-NNN.md`.\n4. Append explicit reconstructed records.\n5. Regenerate registry and dashboard.\n6. Record the recovery in JSONL.\n\nExample reconstructed record:\n\n```json\n{\"type\":\"iteration\",\"run\":3,\"status\":\"reconstructed\",\"focus\":\"extracted focus\",\"findingsCount\":0,\"newInfoRatio\":0.0}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 6. FILE PROTECTION MAP\n\nThe config may include:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"fileProtection\": {\n    \"deep-research-config.json\": \"immutable\",\n    \"deep-research-state.jsonl\": \"append-only\",\n    \"deep-research-strategy.md\": \"mutable\",\n    \"deep-research-dashboard.md\": \"auto-generated\",\n    \"findings-registry.json\": \"auto-generated\",\n    \"iteration-*.md\": \"write-once\",\n    \"research/research.md\": \"mutable\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\nProtection is a workflow contract. It documents ownership and supports validation; it is not a substitute for command-level checks.\n\n---\n\n## 7. DASHBOARD DERIVATION\n\nDashboard values are derived from raw state:\n\n| Dashboard Field | Source |\n|-----------------|--------|\n| iteration count | JSONL iteration records |\n| current status | latest lifecycle or synthesis event |\n| convergence trend | `convergenceSignals` |\n| blocked stops | registry `blockedStopHistory` |\n| graph convergence | registry graph fields |\n| next focus | strategy |\n\n`synthesis_complete` events are authoritative for terminal status when present.\n\n---\n\n## 8. LEGACY ALIASES\n\nThe workflow may dual-read older names during migration windows, but new writes use canonical `deep-research-*` artifacts. Migration reads should append a migration event that records `legacyPath`, `canonicalPath`, and timestamp.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":174,"totalLines":174,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/state/state-reducer-registry.md","time":{"start":1785758067564,"end":1785758067705}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_028da9b5cab13855016a7081732b34819194fc3b5f22b4c29f"}},"id":"prt_fc779ab68001K1onNe0VYulAjF","sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","messageID":"msg_fc779745a001TxXig8wd9BQFim"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785758067762,"sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_wUR0kT5QboDv2GxYYzQEQOjM","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/protocol/context-snapshot.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/protocol/context-snapshot.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: Codebase Context Snapshot Reference\n3: description: Bounded, pointer-based context snapshot captured during deep-research initialization for codebase-scoped targets.\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"research context snapshot\"\n6:   - \"research known context capture\"\n7:   - \"research codebase pointers\"\n8:   - \"bounded context snapshot\"\n9: importance_tier: normal\n10: contextType: implementation\n11: version: 1.14.0.0\n12: ---\n13: \n14: # Codebase Context Snapshot Reference\n15: \n16: Bounded context capture rules for the `Known Context` section of `deep-research-strategy.md` when the research target is codebase-scoped.\n17: \n18: ---\n19: \n20: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n21: \n22: ### Purpose\n23: \n24: Define what a codebase-scoped initialization must capture in `Known Context` before the loop starts, and how that capture stays bounded rather than becoming a second research pass.\n25: \n26: ### When to Use\n27: \n28: Load this reference during INIT when the research topic targets an existing codebase, feature, or system rather than an external/unknown domain.\n29: \n30: ### Core Principle\n31: \n32: The snapshot is pointer-based, not a full context dump: it orients the first iteration without duplicating discovery work the loop itself should do.\n33: \n34: ---\n35: \n36: ## 2. SNAPSHOT CONTENTS\n37: \n38: During initialization, capture a bounded, pointer-based context snapshot in `deep-research-strategy.md` `Known Context` when the target is codebase-scoped. The snapshot must include:\n39: \n40: - Relevant source paths or symbols, cited as pointers rather than full file bodies.\n41: - Known integration points and likely reuse candidates.\n42: - Existing conventions or constraints that should shape the first iteration.\n43: - Gaps or unavailable context sources, including stale code graph or memory retrieval.\n44: \n45: ---\n46: \n47: ## 3. NON-GOALS AND ROUTING\n48: \n49: The snapshot must not create a separate context report loop:\n50: \n51: - If a quick lookup is all that is needed, route the user to `@context` instead of running deep-research.\n52: - If planning is the real goal, route to `/speckit:plan` after the snapshot is available rather than continuing to iterate.\n53: \n54: This keeps the bounded snapshot scoped to orienting the first iteration, not substituting for `@context` or `/speckit:plan`.\n\n(End of file - total 54 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: Codebase Context Snapshot Reference\ndescription: Bounded, pointer-based context snapshot captured during deep-research initialization for codebase-scoped targets.\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"research context snapshot\"\n  - \"research known context capture\"\n  - \"research codebase pointers\"\n  - \"bounded context snapshot\"\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.14.0.0\n---\n\n# Codebase Context Snapshot Reference\n\nBounded context capture rules for the `Known Context` section of `deep-research-strategy.md` when the research target is codebase-scoped.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/protocol/context-snapshot.md","text":"---\ntitle: Codebase Context Snapshot Reference\ndescription: Bounded, pointer-based context snapshot captured during deep-research initialization for codebase-scoped targets.\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"research context snapshot\"\n  - \"research known context capture\"\n  - \"research codebase pointers\"\n  - \"bounded context snapshot\"\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.14.0.0\n---\n\n# Codebase Context Snapshot Reference\n\nBounded context capture rules for the `Known Context` section of `deep-research-strategy.md` when the research target is codebase-scoped.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Purpose\n\nDefine what a codebase-scoped initialization must capture in `Known Context` before the loop starts, and how that capture stays bounded rather than becoming a second research pass.\n\n### When to Use\n\nLoad this reference during INIT when the research topic targets an existing codebase, feature, or system rather than an external/unknown domain.\n\n### Core Principle\n\nThe snapshot is pointer-based, not a full context dump: it orients the first iteration without duplicating discovery work the loop itself should do.\n\n---\n\n## 2. SNAPSHOT CONTENTS\n\nDuring initialization, capture a bounded, pointer-based context snapshot in `deep-research-strategy.md` `Known Context` when the target is codebase-scoped. The snapshot must include:\n\n- Relevant source paths or symbols, cited as pointers rather than full file bodies.\n- Known integration points and likely reuse candidates.\n- Existing conventions or constraints that should shape the first iteration.\n- Gaps or unavailable context sources, including stale code graph or memory retrieval.\n\n---\n\n## 3. NON-GOALS AND ROUTING\n\nThe snapshot must not create a separate context report loop:\n\n- If a quick lookup is all that is needed, route the user to `@context` instead of running deep-research.\n- If planning is the real goal, route to `/speckit:plan` after the snapshot is available rather than continuing to iterate.\n\nThis keeps the bounded snapshot scoped to orienting the first iteration, not substituting for `@context` or `/speckit:plan`.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":54,"totalLines":54,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/protocol/context-snapshot.md","time":{"start":1785758067581,"end":1785758067734}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_028da9b5cab13855016a7081732b448191b43f80d1b2d435e8"}},"id":"prt_fc779ab7a0011anrjuKKnGe2WQ","sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","messageID":"msg_fc779745a001TxXig8wd9BQFim"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785758067898,"sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"glob","callID":"call_cjvj43bYhX84TeRdmqntNtzA","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/**/*deep*research*"},"output":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-research-reducers/deep-research-projection-types.ts\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-research-reducers/deep-research-projection-schema.ts\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-research-reducers/deep-research-reducer.ts\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-research-sealed-artifacts/deep-research-sealed-artifacts.ts\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-research-sealed-artifacts/deep-research-artifact-material.ts\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-research-sealed-artifacts/deep-research-sealed-artifact-types.ts\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-research-ledger-schema/deep-research-ledger-schema.ts\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-research-ledger-schema/deep-research-ledger-types.ts\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-research-resume-adapter/deep-research-resume-adapter.ts\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-research-certificates/deep-research-certificate-validation.ts\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-research-certificates/deep-research-certificates.ts\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-research-certificates/deep-research-certificate-types.ts\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/deep-research-novelty-inertness.vitest.ts\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/deep-research-resume-adapter.vitest.ts\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/deep-research-ledger-schema.vitest.ts\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/deep-research-shadow-parity.vitest.ts\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/deep-research-certificates.vitest.ts\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/deep-research-convergence-floor.vitest.ts\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/deep-research-reduce-state.vitest.ts\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/deep-research-memory-upsert-yaml.vitest.ts\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/deep-research-sealed-artifacts.vitest.ts\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/deep-research-rollback-gate.vitest.ts\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/deep-research-reducers.vitest.ts","metadata":{"count":23,"truncated":false},"title":"","time":{"start":1785758067589,"end":1785758067895}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_028da9b5cab13855016a7081732b4c8191a42873b7dbcf0232"}},"id":"prt_fc779ab80001wh4DjDuHMgIUgf","sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","messageID":"msg_fc779745a001TxXig8wd9BQFim"}}
