{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785758296660,"sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_xxWS5t2xtxsySHMhCgKP9xeO","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Webflow MCP Action Reference (Remote Surface, 2026-08-03)\"\n3: description: \"Complete official action reference for the Webflow MCP remote surface: 31 tools, 220 actions, required parameters, read/write flags, and frozen risk classes.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"webflow action reference\"\n6:   - \"webflow mcp actions\"\n7:   - \"webflow tool parameters\"\n8: importance_tier: important\n9: contextType: implementation\n10: version: 1.1.0.0\n11: ---\n12: # Webflow MCP Action Reference (Remote Surface)\n13: \n14: Complete action inventory for the remote Webflow MCP surface.\n15: \n16: ---\n17: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n18: \n19: Source: official Webflow MCP tool documentation (developers.webflow.com/mcp/tools/*, fetched\n20: 2026-08-03) — the **remote deployed surface** (`com.webflow/mcp` 2.0.0): **31 tools / 220\n21: actions**. The local OSS server (`webflow-mcp-server` npm) exposes the smaller 18-module baseline\n22: in `tool-surface.md`. Always re-discover the pinned version's live surface per session. Class =\n23: frozen risk class applied by action-name semantics (RO/DW/DS/PB/DP); read/write flags are the\n24: official tool-level flags.\n25: \n26: ### Global Parameters\n27: \n28: Every action on the page-building tools (`data_element_tool`, `data_element_settings_tool`,\n29: `data_component_tool`, `data_component_props_tool`, `data_component_variants_tool`,\n30: `data_element_builder`, `data_component_builder`, `data_whtml_builder`, `data_style_tool`,\n31: `data_variable_tool`) requires `siteId` and `pageId` in addition to the parameters listed;\n32: Designer-canvas actions (`designer_tool`, `element_snapshot_tool`) require `siteId`. Actions\n33: without required parameters are marked `—`.\n34: \n35: ---\n36: ## 2. AGENT INSTRUCTIONS\n37: \n38: ### `data_agent_instructions_tool` — read, write\n39: \n40: | Action                | Required parameters               | Class |\n41: | -----------------------| -----------------------------------| -------|\n42: | `search_instructions` | `site_id`                         | RO    |\n43: | `read_instruction`    | `site_id, path`                   | RO    |\n44: | `create_instruction`  | `site_id, kind, path, markdown`   | DW    |\n45: | `update_instruction`  | `site_id, kind, path`             | DW    |\n46: | `delete_instruction`  | `site_id, kind, path`             | DS    |\n47: | `move_instruction`    | `site_id, kind, fromPath, toPath` | DW    |\n48: \n49: \n50: ---\n51: ## 3. ANALYZE (ADD-ON)\n52: \n53: ### `data_analyze_tool` — read\n54: \n55: | Action | Required parameters | Class |\n56: |--------|---------------------|-------|\n57: | `get_query_guide` | `—` | RO |\n58: | `get_resolve_event_element_guide` | `—` | RO |\n59: | `get_time_on_page_report` | `site_id, startTime, endTime, metricScope` | RO |\n60: | `get_top_dimensions_report` | `site_id, startTime, endTime, dimension, metricScope, limit` | RO |\n61: | `get_top_events_report` | `site_id, startTime, endTime` | RO |\n62: | `get_top_pages_report` | `site_id, startTime, endTime, limit` | RO |\n63: | `get_traffic_report` | `site_id, startTime, endTime, metricScope, bucketTimeZone` | RO |\n64: \n65: \n66: ---\n67: ## 4. ASSETS\n68: \n69: ### `data_assets_tool` — read, write\n70: \n71: | Action | Required parameters | Class |\n72: |--------|---------------------|-------|\n73: | `compress_assets` | `site_id, asset_ids[], format` | DW |\n74: | `create_asset` | `site_id, file_name, file_hash` | DW |\n75: | `create_asset_folder` | `site_id, display_name` | DW |\n76: | `delete_asset` | `asset_id` | DS |\n77: | `get_asset` | `asset_id` | RO |\n78: | `get_asset_folder` | `folder_id` | RO |\n79: | `get_compression_task` | `site_id, task_id` | RO |\n80: | `list_asset_folders` | `site_id` | RO |\n81: | `list_assets` | `site_id` | RO |\n82: | `list_compression_tasks` | `site_id` | RO |\n83: | `update_asset` | `asset_id` | DW |\n84: | `update_asset_folder` | `folder_id` | DW |\n85: \n86: ### `asset_tool` — write\n87: \n88: | Action | Required parameters | Class |\n89: |--------|---------------------|-------|\n90: | `upload_image_by_url` | `url` | DW |\n91: \n92: ### `get_asset_preview` — read\n93: \n94: | Action | Required parameters | Class |\n95: |--------|---------------------|-------|\n96: | `get_asset_preview` | `asset_id` | RO |\n97: \n98: \n99: ---\n100: ## 5. CMS\n101: \n102: ### `data_cms_tool` — read, write\n103: \n104: | Action | Required parameters | Class |\n105: |--------|---------------------|-------|\n106: | `create_collection` | `siteId, request{displayName, singularName}` | DW |\n107: | `create_collection_items` | `collection_id, request{fieldData}` | DW |\n108: | `create_collection_option_field` | `collection_id, request{type=Option, displayName, metadata}` | DW |\n109: | `create_collection_reference_field` | `collection_id, request{type, displayName, metadata{collectionId}}` | DW |\n110: | `create_collection_static_field` | `collection_id, request{type, displayName}` | DW |\n111: | `delete_collection_field` | `collection_id, field_id` | DS |\n112: | `delete_collection_items` | `collection_id, request{items[].id}` | DS |\n113: | `get_collection_details` | `collection_id` | RO |\n114: | `get_collection_list` | `siteId` | RO |\n115: | `list_collection_items` | `collection_id` | RO |\n116: | `publish_collection_items` | `collection_id, request{itemIds}` | PB |\n117: | `unpublish_collection_items` | `collection_id, request{items[].id}` | PB |\n118: | `update_collection_field` | `collection_id, field_id, request` | DW |\n119: | `update_collection_items` | `collection_id, request{items[].id, fieldData}` | DW |\n120: \n121: \n122: ---\n123: ## 6. COMMENTS\n124: \n125: ### `data_comments_tool` — read, write\n126: \n127: | Action | Required parameters | Class |\n128: |--------|---------------------|-------|\n129: | `create_reply` | `site_id, comment_thread_id, content` | DW |\n130: | `get_comment_thread` | `site_id, comment_thread_id` | RO |\n131: | `list_comment_replies` | `site_id, comment_thread_id` | RO |\n132: | `list_comment_threads` | `site_id` | RO |\n133: | `search_comment_user_by_email` | `site_id, email` | RO |\n134: \n135: \n136: ---\n137: ## 7. COMPONENTS\n138: \n139: ### `data_component_tool` — read, write *(+ siteId, pageId global)*\n140: \n141: | Action | Required parameters | Class |\n142: |--------|---------------------|-------|\n143: | `create_blank_component` | `name` | DW |\n144: | `duplicate_component` | `source_component_id, name` | DW |\n145: | `get_all_components` | `—` | RO |\n146: | `get_component` | `component_id, name` | RO |\n147: | `get_parent_component` | `id {component, element}` | RO |\n148: | `insert_component_instance` | `parent_element_id, component_id, creation_position` | DW |\n149: | `query_components` | `queries[]` | RO |\n150: | `set_component_metadata` | `component_id` | DW |\n151: | `transform_element_to_component` | `id {component, element}, name` | DW |\n152: | `unlink_component_instance` | `component_instance_id` | DW |\n153: | `unregister_component` | `component_id` | DS |\n154: \n155: ### `data_component_builder` — write *(+ siteId, pageId global)*\n156: \n157: | Action | Required parameters | Class |\n158: |--------|---------------------|-------|\n159: | `insert_in_element` | `build_label, parent_element_id, creation_position, component_schema{name}` | DW |\n160: | `insert_in_slot` | `build_label, parent_element_id, creation_position, component_schema{name}, slot_name` | DW |\n161: \n162: ### `data_component_props_tool` — read, write *(+ siteId, pageId global)*\n163: \n164: | Action | Required parameters | Class |\n165: |--------|---------------------|-------|\n166: | `create_prop` | `component_id, props[]` | DW |\n167: | `get_component_instance_props` | `element_id {component, element}` | RO |\n168: | `remove_prop` | `component_id, prop_ids` | DS |\n169: | `reset_all_props_value` | `element_id {component, element}` | DW |\n170: | `set_component_instance_prop_values` | `element_id, values[]` | DW |\n171: | `update_prop` | `component_id, props[].prop_id` | DW |\n172: \n173: ### `data_component_variants_tool` — read, write *(+ siteId, pageId global)*\n174: \n175: | Action | Required parameters | Class |\n176: |--------|---------------------|-------|\n177: | `create_variant` | `component_id, name` | DW |\n178: | `delete_variant` | `component_id, variant_id` | DS |\n179: | `duplicate_variant` | `component_id, source_variant_id` | DW |\n180: | `get_variant_settings` | `component_id, variant_id` | RO |\n181: | `get_variant_styles` | `variant_id, style_name` | RO |\n182: | `reorder_variants` | `component_id, variant_ids` | DW |\n183: | `set_variant_name` | `component_id, variant_id, name` | DW |\n184: | `set_variant_styles` | `variant_id, style_name` | DW |\n185: \n186: \n187: ---\n188: ## 8. ELEMENTS\n189: \n190: ### `data_element_tool` — read, write *(+ siteId, pageId global)*\n191: \n192: | Action | Required parameters | Class |\n193: |--------|---------------------|-------|\n194: | `get_all_elements` | `pageId, siteId` | RO |\n195: | `get_attributes` | `id {component, element}` | RO |\n196: | `get_display_name` | `element_id {component, element}` | RO |\n197: | `move_element` | `id, anchor_element_id, creation_position` | DW |\n198: | `query_elements` | `queries[]` | RO |\n199: | `remove_attribute` | `id, attribute_names` | DS |\n200: | `remove_element` | `id {component, element}` | DS |\n201: | `set_attributes` | `id, attributes[]` | DW |\n202: | `set_display_name` | `element_id, display_name` | DW |\n203: | `set_heading_level` | `id, heading_level` | DW |\n204: | `set_image_asset` | `id, image_asset_id` | DW |\n205: | `set_link` | `id, linkType, link` | DW |\n206: | `set_style` | `id, style_names` | DW |\n207: | `set_text` | `id, text` | DW |\n208: \n209: ### `data_element_settings_tool` — read, write *(+ siteId, pageId global)*\n210: \n211: | Action | Required parameters | Class |\n212: |--------|---------------------|-------|\n213: | `get_bindable_sources` | `queries[]` | RO |\n214: | `get_settings` | `type, element_id` | RO |\n215: | `set_dom_id` | `element_id` | DW |\n216: | `set_settings` | `operations[]` | DW |\n217: | `set_tag` | `element_id` | DW |\n218: | `set_visibility` | `element_id` | DW |\n219: \n220: ### `data_element_builder` — write *(+ siteId, pageId global)*\n221: \n222: | Action | Required parameters | Class |\n223: |--------|---------------------|-------|\n224: | `create_element` | `build_label, parent_element_id, creation_position, element_schema{type}` | DW |\n225: \n226: \n227: ---\n228: ## 9. ENTERPRISE\n229: \n230: ### `data_enterprise_tool` — read, write\n231: \n232: | Action | Required parameters | Class |\n233: |--------|---------------------|-------|\n234: | `add_well_known_file` | `site_id, fileName, fileData, contentType` | DW |\n235: | `create_301_redirect` | `site_id, fromUrl, toUrl` | DW |\n236: | `delete_301_redirect` | `site_id, redirect_id` | DS |\n237: | `delete_robots_txt` | `site_id` | DS |\n238: | `get_robots_txt` | `site_id` | RO |\n239: | `list_301_redirects` | `site_id` | RO |\n240: | `list_site_activity_logs` | `site_id` | RO |\n241: | `remove_well_known_files` | `site_id, fileNames` | DS |\n242: | `replace_robots_txt` | `site_id` | DW |\n243: | `update_301_redirect` | `site_id, redirect_id, fromUrl, toUrl` | DW |\n244: | `update_robots_txt` | `site_id` | DW |\n245: \n246: \n247: ---\n248: ## 10. FONTS\n249: \n250: ### `data_fonts_tool` — read, write\n251: \n252: | Action | Required parameters | Class |\n253: |--------|---------------------|-------|\n254: | `batch_delete_fonts` | `site_id, items[]` | DS |\n255: | `create_font` | `site_id, file_name, file_hash, font_family, weight, italic, font_display` | DW |\n256: | `delete_font` | `site_id, font_id` | DS |\n257: | `get_font` | `site_id, font_id` | RO |\n258: | `list_fonts` | `site_id` | RO |\n259: | `replace_font_file` | `site_id, font_id, file_name, file_hash` | DW |\n260: | `update_font` | `site_id, font_id` | DW |\n261: \n262: \n263: ---\n264: ## 11. FORMS\n265: \n266: ### `data_forms_tool` — read, write\n267: \n268: | Action | Required parameters | Class |\n269: |--------|---------------------|-------|\n270: | `delete_form_submission` | `site_id, form_submission_id` | DS |\n271: | `get_form` | `form_id` | RO |\n272: | `get_form_submission` | `site_id, form_submission_id` | RO |\n273: | `list_form_submissions` | `site_id, form_id` | RO |\n274: | `list_forms` | `site_id` | RO |\n275: | `list_site_form_submissions` | `site_id` | RO |\n276: | `update_form_submission` | `site_id, form_submission_id, form_submission_data` | DW |\n277: \n278: \n279: ---\n280: ## 12. LOCALIZATION\n281: \n282: ### `data_localization_tool` — read, write\n283: \n284: | Action | Required parameters | Class |\n285: |--------|---------------------|-------|\n286: | `get_component_content` | `site_id, component_id` | RO |\n287: | `get_component_properties` | `site_id, component_id` | RO |\n288: | `get_page_content` | `page_id` | RO |\n289: | `list_components` | `site_id` | RO |\n290: | `update_component_content` | `site_id, component_id, localeId, nodes` | DW |\n291: | `update_component_properties` | `site_id, component_id, localeId, properties` | DW |\n292: | `update_static_content` | `page_id, localeId, nodes` | DW |\n293: \n294: \n295: ---\n296: ## 13. PAGES\n297: \n298: ### `data_pages_tool` — read, write\n299: \n300: | Action | Required parameters | Class |\n301: |--------|---------------------|-------|\n302: | `bulk_update_pages` | `site_id, pages[]` | DW |\n303: | `bulk_update_pages_schema_markup` | `site_id, pages[]` | DW |\n304: | `create_branch` | `site_id, page_id` | DW |\n305: | `create_page` | `site_id, title, slug` | DW |\n306: | `delete_branch` | `site_id, branch_id` | DS |\n307: | `get_branch_details` | `site_id, branch_id` | RO |\n308: | `get_page_metadata` | `page_id` | RO |\n309: | `list_branches` | `site_id` | RO |\n310: | `list_pages` | `site_id` | RO |\n311: | `query_pages_schema_markup` | `site_id, pages[]` | RO |\n312: | `update_page_settings` | `page_id` | DW |\n313: \n314: \n315: ---\n316: ## 14. SCRIPTS\n317: \n318: ### `data_scripts_tool` — read, write\n319: \n320: | Action | Required parameters | Class |\n321: |--------|---------------------|-------|\n322: | `add_page_script` | `page_id, script_id, location, version` | DW |\n323: | `add_site_script` | `site_id, script_id, location, version` | DW |\n324: | `clear_page_scripts` | `page_id` | DS |\n325: | `clear_site_scripts` | `site_id` | DS |\n326: | `delete_registered_script` | `site_id, script_id` | DS |\n327: | `get_page_freeform_code` | `page_id` | RO |\n328: | `get_page_scripts` | `page_id` | RO |\n329: | `get_registered_script` | `site_id, script_id` | RO |\n330: | `get_registered_scripts` | `site_id` | RO |\n331: | `get_site_freeform_code` | `site_id` | RO |\n332: | `get_site_scripts` | `site_id` | RO |\n333: | `register_hosted_script` | `site_id, hosted_location, integrity_hash, version, display_name` | DW |\n334: | `register_inline_script` | `site_id, source_code, version, display_name` | DW |\n335: | `remove_page_script` | `page_id, script_id` | DS |\n336: | `remove_site_script` | `site_id, script_id` | DS |\n337: | `set_page_freeform_code` | `page_id, location, content` | DW |\n338: | `set_page_scripts` | `page_id, scripts` | DW |\n339: | `set_site_freeform_code` | `site_id, location, content` | DW |\n340: | `set_site_scripts` | `site_id, scripts` | DW |\n341: | `update_registered_script` | `site_id, script_id` | DW |\n342: \n343: \n344: ---\n345: ## 15. SITEMAP\n346: \n347: ### `data_sitemap_tool` — read, write\n348: \n349: | Action | Required parameters | Class |\n350: |--------|---------------------|-------|\n351: | `bulk_update_items_sitemap_status` | `collection_id, items[]` | DW |\n352: | `bulk_update_pages_sitemap_status` | `site_id, pages[]` | DW |\n353: | `get_item_sitemap_status` | `collection_id, item_id` | RO |\n354: | `get_page_sitemap_status` | `page_id` | RO |\n355: | `list_items_sitemap_status` | `collection_id` | RO |\n356: | `list_pages_sitemap_status` | `site_id` | RO |\n357: | `update_item_sitemap_status` | `collection_id, item_id, includeInSitemap` | DW |\n358: | `update_page_sitemap_status` | `page_id, includeInSitemap` | DW |\n359: \n360: \n361: ---\n362: ## 16. SITES\n363: \n364: ### `data_sites_tool` — read, write\n365: \n366: | Action | Required parameters | Class |\n367: |--------|---------------------|-------|\n368: | `get_site` | `site_id` | RO |\n369: | `list_sites` | `—` | RO |\n370: | `publish_site` | `site_id` | PB |\n371: \n372: \n373: ---\n374: ## 17. STYLE\n375: \n376: ### `data_style_tool` — read, write *(+ siteId, pageId global)*\n377: \n378: | Action | Required parameters | Class |\n379: |--------|---------------------|-------|\n380: | `create_style` | `name, properties[]` | DW |\n381: | `get_style_variable_modes` | `style_name` | RO |\n382: | `get_styles` | `query` | RO |\n383: | `query_styles` | `queries[]` | RO |\n384: | `remove_all_style_variable_modes` | `style_name` | DS |\n385: | `remove_style` | `style_name` | DS |\n386: | `remove_style_variable_mode` | `style_name, variable_collection_id` | DS |\n387: | `rename_style` | `style_name, new_name` | DW |\n388: | `set_style_variable_mode` | `style_name, variable_collection_id, mode_id` | DW |\n389: | `update_style` | `style_name` | DW |\n390: \n391: \n392: ---\n393: ## 18. VARIABLES\n394: \n395: ### `data_variable_tool` — read, write *(+ siteId, pageId global)*\n396: \n397: | Action | Required parameters | Class |\n398: |--------|---------------------|-------|\n399: | `create_color_variable` | `variable_collection_id, variable_name, value` | DW |\n400: | `create_font_family_variable` | `variable_collection_id, variable_name, value` | DW |\n401: | `create_number_variable` | `variable_collection_id, variable_name, value` | DW |\n402: | `create_percentage_variable` | `variable_collection_id, variable_name, value` | DW |\n403: | `create_size_variable` | `variable_collection_id, variable_name, value` | DW |\n404: | `create_variable_collection` | `name` | DW |\n405: | `create_variable_mode` | `variable_collection_id, name` | DW |\n406: | `delete_variable` | `variable_collection_id, variable_id` | DS |\n407: | `get_variable_collections` | `query` | RO |\n408: | `get_variables` | `variable_collection_id` | RO |\n409: | `query_variables` | `queries[]` | RO |\n410: | `rename_variable` | `variable_collection_id, variable_id, new_name` | DW |\n411: | `reorder_variable_collection` | `collection_id, anchor_collection_id, position` | DW |\n412: | `update_color_variable` | `variable_collection_id, variable_id, value` | DW |\n413: | `update_font_family_variable` | `variable_collection_id, variable_id, value` | DW |\n414: | `update_number_variable` | `variable_collection_id, variable_id, value` | DW |\n415: | `update_percentage_variable` | `variable_collection_id, variable_id, value` | DW |\n416: | `update_size_variable` | `variable_collection_id, variable_id, value` | DW |\n417: \n418: \n419: ---\n420: ## 19. WEBHOOKS\n421: \n422: ### `data_webhook_tool` — read, write\n423: \n424: | Action | Required parameters | Class |\n425: |--------|---------------------|-------|\n426: | `create_webhook` | `site_id, trigger_type, url` | DW |\n427: | `delete_webhook` | `webhook_id` | DS |\n428: | `get_webhook` | `webhook_id` | RO |\n429: | `list_webhooks` | `site_id` | RO |\n430: \n431: \n432: ---\n433: ## 20. WHTML\n434: \n435: ### `data_whtml_builder` — write *(+ siteId, pageId global)*\n436: \n437: | Action | Required parameters | Class |\n438: |--------|---------------------|-------|\n439: | `insert_whtml` | `build_label, parent_element_id, creation_position, html` | DW |\n440: \n441: \n442: ---\n443: ## 21. DESIGNER CANVAS\n444: \n445: ### `designer_tool` — read, write *(+ siteId)*\n446: \n447: | Action | Required parameters | Class |\n448: |--------|---------------------|-------|\n449: | `check_if_inside_component_view` | `—` | RO |\n450: | `close_component_view` | `—` | DW |\n451: | `create_page_folder` | `page_folder_name` | DW |\n452: | `get_all_breakpoints` | `—` | RO |\n453: | `get_branch_parent_page_id` | `—` | RO |\n454: | `get_current_branch_id` | `—` | RO |\n455: | `get_current_component` | `—` | RO |\n456: | `get_current_mode` | `—` | RO |\n457: | `get_current_page` | `—` | RO |\n458: | `get_selected_element` | `—` | RO |\n459: | `list_branches` | `page_id` | RO |\n460: | `open_canvas` | `component_id, page_id` | DW |\n461: | `open_component_view` | `component_instance_id {component, element}` | DW |\n462: | `select_element` | `id {component, element}` | DW |\n463: | `switch_page` | `page_id` | DW |\n464: \n465: ### `element_snapshot_tool` — read *(+ siteId)*\n466: \n467: | Action | Required parameters | Class |\n468: |--------|---------------------|-------|\n469: | `get_element_snapshot` | `id {component, element}` | RO |\n470: \n471: \n472: ---\n473: ## 22. UTILITY\n474: \n475: ### `ask_webflow_ai` — read\n476: \n477: | Action | Required parameters | Class |\n478: |--------|---------------------|-------|\n479: | `ask_webflow_ai` | `message` | RO |\n480: \n481: ### `webflow_guide_tool` — read\n482: \n483: | Action | Required parameters | Class |\n484: |--------|---------------------|-------|\n485: | `get_guidelines` | `—` | RO |\n486: \n487: ### `get_more_tools` — read\n488: \n489: | Action | Required parameters | Class |\n490: |--------|---------------------|-------|\n491: | `get_more_tools` | `brief, category, context` | RO |\n492: \n493: ---\n494: ## 23. RELATED RESOURCES\n495: \n496: - [`tool-surface.md`](tool-surface.md) — local OSS baseline (18 modules)\n497: - [`mcp-wiring.md`](mcp-wiring.md) — wiring, auth, scope model\n498: - [`../SKILL.md`](../SKILL.md) — frozen classes and gates\n\n(End of file - total 498 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: \"Webflow MCP Action Reference (Remote Surface, 2026-08-03)\"\ndescription: \"Complete official action reference for the Webflow MCP remote surface: 31 tools, 220 actions, required parameters, read/write flags, and frozen risk classes.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"webflow action reference\"\n  - \"webflow mcp actions\"\n  - \"webflow tool parameters\"\nimportance_tier: important\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.1.0.0\n---\n# Webflow MCP Action Reference (Remote Surface)\n\nComplete action inventory for the remote Webflow MCP surface.\n\n---\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nSource: official Webflow MCP tool documentation (developers.webflow.com/mcp/tools/*, fetched\n2026-08-03) — the **remote deployed surface** (`com.webflow/mcp` 2.0.0): **31 tools / 220","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md","text":"---\ntitle: \"Webflow MCP Action Reference (Remote Surface, 2026-08-03)\"\ndescription: \"Complete official action reference for the Webflow MCP remote surface: 31 tools, 220 actions, required parameters, read/write flags, and frozen risk classes.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"webflow action reference\"\n  - \"webflow mcp actions\"\n  - \"webflow tool parameters\"\nimportance_tier: important\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.1.0.0\n---\n# Webflow MCP Action Reference (Remote Surface)\n\nComplete action inventory for the remote Webflow MCP surface.\n\n---\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nSource: official Webflow MCP tool documentation (developers.webflow.com/mcp/tools/*, fetched\n2026-08-03) — the **remote deployed surface** (`com.webflow/mcp` 2.0.0): **31 tools / 220\nactions**. The local OSS server (`webflow-mcp-server` npm) exposes the smaller 18-module baseline\nin `tool-surface.md`. Always re-discover the pinned version's live surface per session. Class =\nfrozen risk class applied by action-name semantics (RO/DW/DS/PB/DP); read/write flags are the\nofficial tool-level flags.\n\n### Global Parameters\n\nEvery action on the page-building tools (`data_element_tool`, `data_element_settings_tool`,\n`data_component_tool`, `data_component_props_tool`, `data_component_variants_tool`,\n`data_element_builder`, `data_component_builder`, `data_whtml_builder`, `data_style_tool`,\n`data_variable_tool`) requires `siteId` and `pageId` in addition to the parameters listed;\nDesigner-canvas actions (`designer_tool`, `element_snapshot_tool`) require `siteId`. Actions\nwithout required parameters are marked `—`.\n\n---\n## 2. AGENT INSTRUCTIONS\n\n### `data_agent_instructions_tool` — read, write\n\n| Action                | Required parameters               | Class |\n| -----------------------| -----------------------------------| -------|\n| `search_instructions` | `site_id`                         | RO    |\n| `read_instruction`    | `site_id, path`                   | RO    |\n| `create_instruction`  | `site_id, kind, path, markdown`   | DW    |\n| `update_instruction`  | `site_id, kind, path`             | DW    |\n| `delete_instruction`  | `site_id, kind, path`             | DS    |\n| `move_instruction`    | `site_id, kind, fromPath, toPath` | DW    |\n\n\n---\n## 3. ANALYZE (ADD-ON)\n\n### `data_analyze_tool` — read\n\n| Action | Required parameters | Class |\n|--------|---------------------|-------|\n| `get_query_guide` | `—` | RO |\n| `get_resolve_event_element_guide` | `—` | RO |\n| `get_time_on_page_report` | `site_id, startTime, endTime, metricScope` | RO |\n| `get_top_dimensions_report` | `site_id, startTime, endTime, dimension, metricScope, limit` | RO |\n| `get_top_events_report` | `site_id, startTime, endTime` | RO |\n| `get_top_pages_report` | `site_id, startTime, endTime, limit` | RO |\n| `get_traffic_report` | `site_id, startTime, endTime, metricScope, bucketTimeZone` | RO |\n\n\n---\n## 4. ASSETS\n\n### `data_assets_tool` — read, write\n\n| Action | Required parameters | Class |\n|--------|---------------------|-------|\n| `compress_assets` | `site_id, asset_ids[], format` | DW |\n| `create_asset` | `site_id, file_name, file_hash` | DW |\n| `create_asset_folder` | `site_id, display_name` | DW |\n| `delete_asset` | `asset_id` | DS |\n| `get_asset` | `asset_id` | RO |\n| `get_asset_folder` | `folder_id` | RO |\n| `get_compression_task` | `site_id, task_id` | RO |\n| `list_asset_folders` | `site_id` | RO |\n| `list_assets` | `site_id` | RO |\n| `list_compression_tasks` | `site_id` | RO |\n| `update_asset` | `asset_id` | DW |\n| `update_asset_folder` | `folder_id` | DW |\n\n### `asset_tool` — write\n\n| Action | Required parameters | Class |\n|--------|---------------------|-------|\n| `upload_image_by_url` | `url` | DW |\n\n### `get_asset_preview` — read\n\n| Action | Required parameters | Class |\n|--------|---------------------|-------|\n| `get_asset_preview` | `asset_id` | RO |\n\n\n---\n## 5. CMS\n\n### `data_cms_tool` — read, write\n\n| Action | Required parameters | Class |\n|--------|---------------------|-------|\n| `create_collection` | `siteId, request{displayName, singularName}` | DW |\n| `create_collection_items` | `collection_id, request{fieldData}` | DW |\n| `create_collection_option_field` | `collection_id, request{type=Option, displayName, metadata}` | DW |\n| `create_collection_reference_field` | `collection_id, request{type, displayName, metadata{collectionId}}` | DW |\n| `create_collection_static_field` | `collection_id, request{type, displayName}` | DW |\n| `delete_collection_field` | `collection_id, field_id` | DS |\n| `delete_collection_items` | `collection_id, request{items[].id}` | DS |\n| `get_collection_details` | `collection_id` | RO |\n| `get_collection_list` | `siteId` | RO |\n| `list_collection_items` | `collection_id` | RO |\n| `publish_collection_items` | `collection_id, request{itemIds}` | PB |\n| `unpublish_collection_items` | `collection_id, request{items[].id}` | PB |\n| `update_collection_field` | `collection_id, field_id, request` | DW |\n| `update_collection_items` | `collection_id, request{items[].id, fieldData}` | DW |\n\n\n---\n## 6. COMMENTS\n\n### `data_comments_tool` — read, write\n\n| Action | Required parameters | Class |\n|--------|---------------------|-------|\n| `create_reply` | `site_id, comment_thread_id, content` | DW |\n| `get_comment_thread` | `site_id, comment_thread_id` | RO |\n| `list_comment_replies` | `site_id, comment_thread_id` | RO |\n| `list_comment_threads` | `site_id` | RO |\n| `search_comment_user_by_email` | `site_id, email` | RO |\n\n\n---\n## 7. COMPONENTS\n\n### `data_component_tool` — read, write *(+ siteId, pageId global)*\n\n| Action | Required parameters | Class |\n|--------|---------------------|-------|\n| `create_blank_component` | `name` | DW |\n| `duplicate_component` | `source_component_id, name` | DW |\n| `get_all_components` | `—` | RO |\n| `get_component` | `component_id, name` | RO |\n| `get_parent_component` | `id {component, element}` | RO |\n| `insert_component_instance` | `parent_element_id, component_id, creation_position` | DW |\n| `query_components` | `queries[]` | RO |\n| `set_component_metadata` | `component_id` | DW |\n| `transform_element_to_component` | `id {component, element}, name` | DW |\n| `unlink_component_instance` | `component_instance_id` | DW |\n| `unregister_component` | `component_id` | DS |\n\n### `data_component_builder` — write *(+ siteId, pageId global)*\n\n| Action | Required parameters | Class |\n|--------|---------------------|-------|\n| `insert_in_element` | `build_label, parent_element_id, creation_position, component_schema{name}` | DW |\n| `insert_in_slot` | `build_label, parent_element_id, creation_position, component_schema{name}, slot_name` | DW |\n\n### `data_component_props_tool` — read, write *(+ siteId, pageId global)*\n\n| Action | Required parameters | Class |\n|--------|---------------------|-------|\n| `create_prop` | `component_id, props[]` | DW |\n| `get_component_instance_props` | `element_id {component, element}` | RO |\n| `remove_prop` | `component_id, prop_ids` | DS |\n| `reset_all_props_value` | `element_id {component, element}` | DW |\n| `set_component_instance_prop_values` | `element_id, values[]` | DW |\n| `update_prop` | `component_id, props[].prop_id` | DW |\n\n### `data_component_variants_tool` — read, write *(+ siteId, pageId global)*\n\n| Action | Required parameters | Class |\n|--------|---------------------|-------|\n| `create_variant` | `component_id, name` | DW |\n| `delete_variant` | `component_id, variant_id` | DS |\n| `duplicate_variant` | `component_id, source_variant_id` | DW |\n| `get_variant_settings` | `component_id, variant_id` | RO |\n| `get_variant_styles` | `variant_id, style_name` | RO |\n| `reorder_variants` | `component_id, variant_ids` | DW |\n| `set_variant_name` | `component_id, variant_id, name` | DW |\n| `set_variant_styles` | `variant_id, style_name` | DW |\n\n\n---\n## 8. ELEMENTS\n\n### `data_element_tool` — read, write *(+ siteId, pageId global)*\n\n| Action | Required parameters | Class |\n|--------|---------------------|-------|\n| `get_all_elements` | `pageId, siteId` | RO |\n| `get_attributes` | `id {component, element}` | RO |\n| `get_display_name` | `element_id {component, element}` | RO |\n| `move_element` | `id, anchor_element_id, creation_position` | DW |\n| `query_elements` | `queries[]` | RO |\n| `remove_attribute` | `id, attribute_names` | DS |\n| `remove_element` | `id {component, element}` | DS |\n| `set_attributes` | `id, attributes[]` | DW |\n| `set_display_name` | `element_id, display_name` | DW |\n| `set_heading_level` | `id, heading_level` | DW |\n| `set_image_asset` | `id, image_asset_id` | DW |\n| `set_link` | `id, linkType, link` | DW |\n| `set_style` | `id, style_names` | DW |\n| `set_text` | `id, text` | DW |\n\n### `data_element_settings_tool` — read, write *(+ siteId, pageId global)*\n\n| Action | Required parameters | Class |\n|--------|---------------------|-------|\n| `get_bindable_sources` | `queries[]` | RO |\n| `get_settings` | `type, element_id` | RO |\n| `set_dom_id` | `element_id` | DW |\n| `set_settings` | `operations[]` | DW |\n| `set_tag` | `element_id` | DW |\n| `set_visibility` | `element_id` | DW |\n\n### `data_element_builder` — write *(+ siteId, pageId global)*\n\n| Action | Required parameters | Class |\n|--------|---------------------|-------|\n| `create_element` | `build_label, parent_element_id, creation_position, element_schema{type}` | DW |\n\n\n---\n## 9. ENTERPRISE\n\n### `data_enterprise_tool` — read, write\n\n| Action | Required parameters | Class |\n|--------|---------------------|-------|\n| `add_well_known_file` | `site_id, fileName, fileData, contentType` | DW |\n| `create_301_redirect` | `site_id, fromUrl, toUrl` | DW |\n| `delete_301_redirect` | `site_id, redirect_id` | DS |\n| `delete_robots_txt` | `site_id` | DS |\n| `get_robots_txt` | `site_id` | RO |\n| `list_301_redirects` | `site_id` | RO |\n| `list_site_activity_logs` | `site_id` | RO |\n| `remove_well_known_files` | `site_id, fileNames` | DS |\n| `replace_robots_txt` | `site_id` | DW |\n| `update_301_redirect` | `site_id, redirect_id, fromUrl, toUrl` | DW |\n| `update_robots_txt` | `site_id` | DW |\n\n\n---\n## 10. FONTS\n\n### `data_fonts_tool` — read, write\n\n| Action | Required parameters | Class |\n|--------|---------------------|-------|\n| `batch_delete_fonts` | `site_id, items[]` | DS |\n| `create_font` | `site_id, file_name, file_hash, font_family, weight, italic, font_display` | DW |\n| `delete_font` | `site_id, font_id` | DS |\n| `get_font` | `site_id, font_id` | RO |\n| `list_fonts` | `site_id` | RO |\n| `replace_font_file` | `site_id, font_id, file_name, file_hash` | DW |\n| `update_font` | `site_id, font_id` | DW |\n\n\n---\n## 11. FORMS\n\n### `data_forms_tool` — read, write\n\n| Action | Required parameters | Class |\n|--------|---------------------|-------|\n| `delete_form_submission` | `site_id, form_submission_id` | DS |\n| `get_form` | `form_id` | RO |\n| `get_form_submission` | `site_id, form_submission_id` | RO |\n| `list_form_submissions` | `site_id, form_id` | RO |\n| `list_forms` | `site_id` | RO |\n| `list_site_form_submissions` | `site_id` | RO |\n| `update_form_submission` | `site_id, form_submission_id, form_submission_data` | DW |\n\n\n---\n## 12. LOCALIZATION\n\n### `data_localization_tool` — read, write\n\n| Action | Required parameters | Class |\n|--------|---------------------|-------|\n| `get_component_content` | `site_id, component_id` | RO |\n| `get_component_properties` | `site_id, component_id` | RO |\n| `get_page_content` | `page_id` | RO |\n| `list_components` | `site_id` | RO |\n| `update_component_content` | `site_id, component_id, localeId, nodes` | DW |\n| `update_component_properties` | `site_id, component_id, localeId, properties` | DW |\n| `update_static_content` | `page_id, localeId, nodes` | DW |\n\n\n---\n## 13. PAGES\n\n### `data_pages_tool` — read, write\n\n| Action | Required parameters | Class |\n|--------|---------------------|-------|\n| `bulk_update_pages` | `site_id, pages[]` | DW |\n| `bulk_update_pages_schema_markup` | `site_id, pages[]` | DW |\n| `create_branch` | `site_id, page_id` | DW |\n| `create_page` | `site_id, title, slug` | DW |\n| `delete_branch` | `site_id, branch_id` | DS |\n| `get_branch_details` | `site_id, branch_id` | RO |\n| `get_page_metadata` | `page_id` | RO |\n| `list_branches` | `site_id` | RO |\n| `list_pages` | `site_id` | RO |\n| `query_pages_schema_markup` | `site_id, pages[]` | RO |\n| `update_page_settings` | `page_id` | DW |\n\n\n---\n## 14. SCRIPTS\n\n### `data_scripts_tool` — read, write\n\n| Action | Required parameters | Class |\n|--------|---------------------|-------|\n| `add_page_script` | `page_id, script_id, location, version` | DW |\n| `add_site_script` | `site_id, script_id, location, version` | DW |\n| `clear_page_scripts` | `page_id` | DS |\n| `clear_site_scripts` | `site_id` | DS |\n| `delete_registered_script` | `site_id, script_id` | DS |\n| `get_page_freeform_code` | `page_id` | RO |\n| `get_page_scripts` | `page_id` | RO |\n| `get_registered_script` | `site_id, script_id` | RO |\n| `get_registered_scripts` | `site_id` | RO |\n| `get_site_freeform_code` | `site_id` | RO |\n| `get_site_scripts` | `site_id` | RO |\n| `register_hosted_script` | `site_id, hosted_location, integrity_hash, version, display_name` | DW |\n| `register_inline_script` | `site_id, source_code, version, display_name` | DW |\n| `remove_page_script` | `page_id, script_id` | DS |\n| `remove_site_script` | `site_id, script_id` | DS |\n| `set_page_freeform_code` | `page_id, location, content` | DW |\n| `set_page_scripts` | `page_id, scripts` | DW |\n| `set_site_freeform_code` | `site_id, location, content` | DW |\n| `set_site_scripts` | `site_id, scripts` | DW |\n| `update_registered_script` | `site_id, script_id` | DW |\n\n\n---\n## 15. SITEMAP\n\n### `data_sitemap_tool` — read, write\n\n| Action | Required parameters | Class |\n|--------|---------------------|-------|\n| `bulk_update_items_sitemap_status` | `collection_id, items[]` | DW |\n| `bulk_update_pages_sitemap_status` | `site_id, pages[]` | DW |\n| `get_item_sitemap_status` | `collection_id, item_id` | RO |\n| `get_page_sitemap_status` | `page_id` | RO |\n| `list_items_sitemap_status` | `collection_id` | RO |\n| `list_pages_sitemap_status` | `site_id` | RO |\n| `update_item_sitemap_status` | `collection_id, item_id, includeInSitemap` | DW |\n| `update_page_sitemap_status` | `page_id, includeInSitemap` | DW |\n\n\n---\n## 16. SITES\n\n### `data_sites_tool` — read, write\n\n| Action | Required parameters | Class |\n|--------|---------------------|-------|\n| `get_site` | `site_id` | RO |\n| `list_sites` | `—` | RO |\n| `publish_site` | `site_id` | PB |\n\n\n---\n## 17. STYLE\n\n### `data_style_tool` — read, write *(+ siteId, pageId global)*\n\n| Action | Required parameters | Class |\n|--------|---------------------|-------|\n| `create_style` | `name, properties[]` | DW |\n| `get_style_variable_modes` | `style_name` | RO |\n| `get_styles` | `query` | RO |\n| `query_styles` | `queries[]` | RO |\n| `remove_all_style_variable_modes` | `style_name` | DS |\n| `remove_style` | `style_name` | DS |\n| `remove_style_variable_mode` | `style_name, variable_collection_id` | DS |\n| `rename_style` | `style_name, new_name` | DW |\n| `set_style_variable_mode` | `style_name, variable_collection_id, mode_id` | DW |\n| `update_style` | `style_name` | DW |\n\n\n---\n## 18. VARIABLES\n\n### `data_variable_tool` — read, write *(+ siteId, pageId global)*\n\n| Action | Required parameters | Class |\n|--------|---------------------|-------|\n| `create_color_variable` | `variable_collection_id, variable_name, value` | DW |\n| `create_font_family_variable` | `variable_collection_id, variable_name, value` | DW |\n| `create_number_variable` | `variable_collection_id, variable_name, value` | DW |\n| `create_percentage_variable` | `variable_collection_id, variable_name, value` | DW |\n| `create_size_variable` | `variable_collection_id, variable_name, value` | DW |\n| `create_variable_collection` | `name` | DW |\n| `create_variable_mode` | `variable_collection_id, name` | DW |\n| `delete_variable` | `variable_collection_id, variable_id` | DS |\n| `get_variable_collections` | `query` | RO |\n| `get_variables` | `variable_collection_id` | RO |\n| `query_variables` | `queries[]` | RO |\n| `rename_variable` | `variable_collection_id, variable_id, new_name` | DW |\n| `reorder_variable_collection` | `collection_id, anchor_collection_id, position` | DW |\n| `update_color_variable` | `variable_collection_id, variable_id, value` | DW |\n| `update_font_family_variable` | `variable_collection_id, variable_id, value` | DW |\n| `update_number_variable` | `variable_collection_id, variable_id, value` | DW |\n| `update_percentage_variable` | `variable_collection_id, variable_id, value` | DW |\n| `update_size_variable` | `variable_collection_id, variable_id, value` | DW |\n\n\n---\n## 19. WEBHOOKS\n\n### `data_webhook_tool` — read, write\n\n| Action | Required parameters | Class |\n|--------|---------------------|-------|\n| `create_webhook` | `site_id, trigger_type, url` | DW |\n| `delete_webhook` | `webhook_id` | DS |\n| `get_webhook` | `webhook_id` | RO |\n| `list_webhooks` | `site_id` | RO |\n\n\n---\n## 20. WHTML\n\n### `data_whtml_builder` — write *(+ siteId, pageId global)*\n\n| Action | Required parameters | Class |\n|--------|---------------------|-------|\n| `insert_whtml` | `build_label, parent_element_id, creation_position, html` | DW |\n\n\n---\n## 21. DESIGNER CANVAS\n\n### `designer_tool` — read, write *(+ siteId)*\n\n| Action | Required parameters | Class |\n|--------|---------------------|-------|\n| `check_if_inside_component_view` | `—` | RO |\n| `close_component_view` | `—` | DW |\n| `create_page_folder` | `page_folder_name` | DW |\n| `get_all_breakpoints` | `—` | RO |\n| `get_branch_parent_page_id` | `—` | RO |\n| `get_current_branch_id` | `—` | RO |\n| `get_current_component` | `—` | RO |\n| `get_current_mode` | `—` | RO |\n| `get_current_page` | `—` | RO |\n| `get_selected_element` | `—` | RO |\n| `list_branches` | `page_id` | RO |\n| `open_canvas` | `component_id, page_id` | DW |\n| `open_component_view` | `component_instance_id {component, element}` | DW |\n| `select_element` | `id {component, element}` | DW |\n| `switch_page` | `page_id` | DW |\n\n### `element_snapshot_tool` — read *(+ siteId)*\n\n| Action | Required parameters | Class |\n|--------|---------------------|-------|\n| `get_element_snapshot` | `id {component, element}` | RO |\n\n\n---\n## 22. UTILITY\n\n### `ask_webflow_ai` — read\n\n| Action | Required parameters | Class |\n|--------|---------------------|-------|\n| `ask_webflow_ai` | `message` | RO |\n\n### `webflow_guide_tool` — read\n\n| Action | Required parameters | Class |\n|--------|---------------------|-------|\n| `get_guidelines` | `—` | RO |\n\n### `get_more_tools` — read\n\n| Action | Required parameters | Class |\n|--------|---------------------|-------|\n| `get_more_tools` | `brief, category, context` | RO |\n\n---\n## 23. RELATED RESOURCES\n\n- [`tool-surface.md`](tool-surface.md) — local OSS baseline (18 modules)\n- [`mcp-wiring.md`](mcp-wiring.md) — wiring, auth, scope model\n- [`../SKILL.md`](../SKILL.md) — frozen classes and gates","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":498,"totalLines":498,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md","time":{"start":1785758296652,"end":1785758296659}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0988c57a5556d0f9016a7082580498819196d21b95903719a0"}},"id":"prt_fc77d298d0010wnHpFdxXXgrCd","sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","messageID":"msg_fc77cf028001ZMthqLhmQIiwqU"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785758296757,"sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_nc8H400LvwTFT3UH8eLKRWgu","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/designer-capabilities.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/designer-capabilities.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Webflow Designer Capabilities\"\n3: description: \"How the Webflow MCP 2.0 Designer surface works: canvas model, Bridge App boundary, selection-driven edit loop, element tree, styles and variable modes, components with props/variants/slots, breakpoints, assets, and pages — all draft-only until publish.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"webflow designer capabilities\"\n6:   - \"webflow designer logic\"\n7:   - \"webflow canvas model\"\n8:   - \"webflow element tree\"\n9:   - \"webflow design tokens\"\n10:   - \"webflow component variants\"\n11:   - \"webflow breakpoints\"\n12: importance_tier: important\n13: contextType: implementation\n14: version: 1.0.0.0\n15: ---\n16: \n17: # Webflow Designer Capabilities - Canvas Model and Edit Logic\n18: \n19: The operational logic of the Webflow MCP 2.0 Designer surface: what the canvas state is, which operations need the Bridge App, and how element, style, variable, component, and breakpoint edits compose into safe design workflows.\n20: \n21: ---\n22: \n23: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n24: \n25: The Designer surface is the flagship of Webflow MCP 2.0: it operates on the live site tree and the open Designer canvas rather than on content records only. It splits into two planes with different connection requirements:\n26: \n27: - **Data-API designer modules** — elements, components, styles, variables, assets, and pages. These target the site tree through the Data API and work without the canvas open; the Bridge App is optional for them.\n28: - **Canvas-bound operations** — current page / mode / branch / component view / selection, canvas navigation, visual snapshots, and breakpoint reads. These read live Designer state and **require the Bridge App open in the Designer** (remote OAuth installs it automatically; local stdio mode needs the Bridge App Designer extension).\n29: \n30: Every Designer edit is a **draft on the site tree** — nothing appears on the live site until a separate, gated `publish_site` runs. All Designer-family operations pair with `sk-design`: the transport executes, never decides taste.\n31: \n32: ---\n33: \n34: ## 2. CANVAS MODEL AND BRIDGE BOUNDARY\n35: \n36: The live canvas exposes five pieces of state that shape every Designer workflow:\n37: \n38: | State | Read action | Notes |\n39: |---|---|---|\n40: | Current page | `get_current_page` | Which page is open in the Designer |\n41: | Current mode | `get_current_mode` | Design / preview / editing context |\n42: | Current branch | `get_current_branch_id`, `list_branches`, `get_branch_parent_page_id` | Branch-scoped edit contexts |\n43: | Component view | `get_current_component`, `check_if_inside_component_view` | When inside a component, mutations are scoped to the component |\n44: | Current selection | `get_selected_element` | The element the operator is looking at |\n45: \n46: Navigation actions: `open_canvas` (`component_id`, `page_id`), `switch_page` (`page_id`), `open_component_view` (component instance), `close_component_view`, `select_element` (`id {component, element}`).\n47: \n48: All of these are **canvas-bound**: they read or move the live Designer state, so they fail when the Bridge App is not connected. `create_page_folder` and `open_canvas` are the only two draft-write actions in this group; everything else is read-only or canvas navigation. The bridge boundary is a failure mode, not a design limitation: a data-only session (CMS, content, publish) must never assume canvas state exists, and a Designer session must confirm the canvas is open before the edit loop starts.\n49: \n50: ---\n51: \n52: ## 3. SELECTION-DRIVEN EDIT LOOP\n53: \n54: The canonical Designer workflow is a five-step loop, always starting from what is true on the canvas rather than from assumptions about the tree:\n55: \n56: 1. **Snapshot** — `get_element_snapshot` (`id {component, element}`, RO) captures the element's rendered state before any change.\n57: 2. **Discover** — `query_elements` (`queries[]`, RO) or `get_all_elements` (`pageId`, `siteId`, RO) locates the target in the tree.\n58: 3. **Focus** — `select_element` or `open_canvas` puts the target in view so the operator and the agent agree on what is about to change.\n59: 4. **Mutate** — a draft-write (DW) action from the element/style/variable/component sets (§4–§6), with the target id and a write preview.\n60: 5. **Verify** — snapshot or query read-back confirms the postcondition; a DS action inside the loop requires operator confirmation plus a rollback statement (version-history restore) before it runs.\n61: \n62: The loop is the contract for `sk-design` pairing: the design judgment step (what to change) happens before step 4, and the agent only executes. Every mutation step is individually confirmable, so a multi-edit design pass is a sequence of confirmable steps rather than one bulk write.\n63: \n64: ---\n65: \n66: ## 4. ELEMENT TREE SEMANTICS\n67: \n68: Elements are addressed by `id {component, element}`: an element can be a plain node in the page tree or an instance inside a component. Positions are expressed as `parent_element_id` + `creation_position`; builder-style mutations add a `build_label` (the human-readable label of the build step) to `create_element` and the two component insertion actions.\n69: \n70: | Aspect | Actions | Class |\n71: |---|---|---|\n72: | Read | `get_all_elements`, `query_elements`, `get_display_name`, `get_attributes` | RO |\n73: | Structure | `create_element` (`element_schema{type}`), `move_element` (`anchor_element_id`), `set_display_name` | DW |\n74: | Content | `set_text`, `set_link` (`linkType`, `link`), `set_heading_level`, `set_image_asset`, `set_style` (`style_names`), `set_attributes` | DW |\n75: | Settings | `get_settings`, `set_settings` (`operations[]`), `set_dom_id`, `set_tag`, `set_visibility`, `get_bindable_sources` | RO / DW |\n76: | Destructive | `remove_element`, `remove_attribute` (`attribute_names`), `remove_style` | DS |\n77: \n78: Semantics that matter:\n79: \n80: - `set_style` references styles by `style_names` — the element points at named styles, it does not inline raw CSS. Styling an element therefore means first ensuring the style exists (§5).\n81: - `remove_element` accepts `{component, element}` ids: removing a component instance vs. a plain element are the same action but different rollback surfaces (component instances can be re-inserted; plain element removal relies on version history).\n82: - `set_visibility` and `set_dom_id` are per-element settings that affect interaction targets (CMS bindings, custom code) — a DW gate with a scope check.\n83: \n84: ---\n85: \n86: ## 5. STYLE AND DESIGN TOKENS\n87: \n88: Styles are named, reusable property sets; design tokens are typed variables collected into collections with modes. The two compose: styles can be bound to variable modes so a theme switch re-skins every element using the style.\n89: \n90: **Style lifecycle** (`data_style_tool`): `create_style` (`name`, `properties[]`, DW), `update_style`, `rename_style`, `remove_style` (DS), reads `query_styles` / `get_styles`. Mode bindings: `set_style_variable_mode` (`style_name`, `variable_collection_id`, `mode_id`, DW), `get_style_variable_modes`, `remove_style_variable_mode` / `remove_all_style_variable_modes` (DS).\n91: \n92: **Token lifecycle** (`data_variable_tool`): collections `create_variable_collection` / `reorder_variable_collection` (DW); modes `create_variable_mode` (DW); typed variables — color, font family, number, percentage, size — each with `create_*` / `update_*` (DW) and `delete_variable` (DS); reads `get_variable_collections`, `get_variables`, `query_variables`.\n93: \n94: Tokenization logic: create collection → create mode (e.g. \"Light\") → create typed variables → `set_style_variable_mode` to bind a style → apply the style to elements. A second mode (\"Dark\") then re-skins the same style without touching elements. Renames ripple through every binding; deletes are DS because they break every bound style.\n95: \n96: ---\n97: \n98: ## 6. COMPONENTS: BUILDER, PROPS, VARIANTS, SLOTS\n99: \n100: Components are the highest-leverage Designer capability: reusable trees with instance-level props, variants, slots, and metadata.\n101: \n102: | Aspect | Actions | Class |\n103: |---|---|---|\n104: | Lifecycle | `create_blank_component`, `duplicate_component`, `transform_element_to_component`, `set_component_metadata` | DW |\n105: | | `unregister_component` | DS |\n106: | Instances | `insert_component_instance` (`parent_element_id`, `component_id`, `creation_position`), `unlink_component_instance`, `get_parent_component` | DW / RO |\n107: | Builder | `insert_in_element` / `insert_in_slot` (`component_schema{name}`, `slot_name`, `build_label`) | DW |\n108: | Props | `create_prop`, `update_prop`, `set_component_instance_prop_values`, `reset_all_props_value`, `get_component_instance_props` | DW / RO |\n109: | | `remove_prop` | DS |\n110: | Variants | `create_variant`, `duplicate_variant`, `set_variant_name`, `reorder_variants`, `set_variant_styles`, `get_variant_settings`, `get_variant_styles` | DW / RO |\n111: | | `delete_variant` | DS |\n112: | View scoping | `open_component_view`, `close_component_view`, `get_current_component`, `check_if_inside_component_view` | DW / RO |\n113: \n114: Component logic:\n115: \n116: - **Props are the API of the component**: instances are customized with `set_component_instance_prop_values`, never by editing the master tree. `reset_all_props_value` returns an instance to defaults (DW, preview the values first).\n117: - **Slots are extension points**: `insert_in_slot` builds inside a component slot, so a card component can accept arbitrary children. Slot targets need the `slot_name` plus the component schema.\n118: - **Variants are style layers**: `set_variant_styles` (`variant_id`, `style_name`) binds named styles to a variant; `get_variant_styles` / `get_variant_settings` read the current layer before changing it. Variant name/set/reorder are cheap; `delete_variant` is DS.\n119: - **Editing inside the component view** scopes element mutations to the component master; `check_if_inside_component_view` decides whether a proposed element edit targets the component or the page.\n120: \n121: ---\n122: \n123: ## 7. BREAKPOINTS AND RESPONSIVE LOGIC\n124: \n125: Breakpoints are **canvas-bound** state: `get_all_breakpoints` reads the live Designer breakpoint set and requires the Bridge App. Responsive logic is indirect but deliberate:\n126: \n127: - Styles carry `style_names` and are defined once; per-breakpoint behavior comes from the style system inside the Designer (a style's properties resolve per breakpoint in the canvas).\n128: - An element's responsive behavior is therefore changed by editing which styles apply (`set_style`) and what those styles contain (`create_style` / `update_style`), not by a dedicated responsive action.\n129: - Snapshot verification is breakpoint-aware: `get_element_snapshot` reflects the current canvas mode, so a responsive change should be verified at the target breakpoint with the canvas on that breakpoint.\n130: \n131: ---\n132: \n133: ## 8. ASSETS AND PAGES IN DESIGNER CONTEXT\n134: \n135: **Assets** feed the visual layer: `list_assets`, `get_asset`, `get_asset_preview`, `create_asset` (`file_name`, `file_hash`), `create_asset_folder`, `update_asset`, `update_asset_folder`, `upload_image_by_url` (DW), `compress_assets` (`format` — WebP/AVIF pipeline, DW), `list_compression_tasks` / `get_compression_task`, and `delete_asset` (DS). Elements bind to assets with `set_image_asset` (`image_asset_id`); the edit loop for an image swap is: upload → list to confirm the asset id → `set_image_asset` → snapshot verify.\n136: \n137: **Pages** are the canvas context and the branch vehicle: `create_page` (`siteId`, `title`, `slug`), `create_page_folder`, `update_page_settings`, `switch_page` (canvas-bound), plus branches `create_branch`, `get_branch_details`, `list_branches`, `get_branch_parent_page_id`, `get_current_branch_id` (all RO/DW) and `delete_branch` (DS). Branches are parallel edit contexts: switching the canvas to a branch isolates Designer edits from the main page until the branch merges — a natural staging pattern for design work.\n138: \n139: ---\n140: \n141: ## 9. OPERATION CLASSES AND GATES\n142: \n143: | Class | Examples | Gate |\n144: |---|---|---|\n145: | **RO** read-only | snapshot, query elements/styles/variables/components, canvas state reads, asset/pages reads, breakpoints | none |\n146: | **DW** draft-write | create/update elements, styles, variables, components, props, variants, assets, pages | scope check + target id + write preview; `sk-design` pairing for all Designer mutations |\n147: | **DS** destructive | `remove_element`, `remove_style`, `remove_style_variable_mode`, `remove_all_style_variable_modes`, `delete_variable`, `unregister_component`, `remove_prop`, `delete_variant`, `delete_asset`, `delete_branch` | operator confirmation with exact target + rollback statement (version-history restore) |\n148: | **Publish** | `publish_site` (separate surface) | fresh confirmation naming site/page scope + domains |\n149: \n150: Two rules dominate: Designer edits are **draft-only until publish** (the Designer gate is upstream of the publish gate), and **taste never comes from the transport** — any layout/style/component decision loads `sk-design` first.\n151: \n152: ---\n153: \n154: ## 10. WORKED FLOWS\n155: \n156: ### Flow A — Tokenized restyle (light theme)\n157: \n158: 1. `create_variable_collection` \"Brand\" (DW) → `create_variable_mode` \"Light\" (DW) → `create_color_variable` \"brand-primary\" (DW)\n159: 2. `create_style` \"Button Primary\" with `properties[]` (DW) → `set_style_variable_mode` binding the mode (DW)\n160: 3. `query_elements` → `set_style` `[\"Button Primary\"]` on the target (DW)\n161: 4. `get_element_snapshot` verify (RO)\n162: \n163: ### Flow B — Component with variants\n164: \n165: 1. `transform_element_to_component` (DW) or `create_blank_component` (DW)\n166: 2. `create_prop` \"label\" (DW) → `set_component_instance_prop_values` on the inserted instance (DW)\n167: 3. `create_variant` \"Hover\" (DW) → `set_variant_styles` binding a hover style (DW)\n168: 4. `open_component_view` → element edits inside the view (DW, scoped) → `close_component_view`\n169: 5. `get_element_snapshot` verify (RO)\n170: \n171: ### Flow C — Image swap\n172: \n173: 1. `upload_image_by_url` (DW) → `list_assets` to confirm the id (RO)\n174: 2. `set_image_asset` on the element (DW)\n175: 3. `get_asset_preview` / `get_element_snapshot` verify (RO)\n176: \n177: ---\n178: \n179: ## 11. RELATED RESOURCES\n180: \n181: - [`action-reference.md`](action-reference.md) — exact required parameters per Designer action\n182: - [`tool-surface.md`](tool-surface.md) — local OSS baseline and module layout\n183: - [`mcp-wiring.md`](mcp-wiring.md) — transport, auth, and Bridge App connection details\n184: - [`troubleshooting.md`](troubleshooting.md) — Bridge App / canvas failure triage\n185: - [`../feature-catalog/design/designer.md`](../feature-catalog/design/designer.md) — capability card\n186: - [`../feature-catalog/design/component-variants.md`](../feature-catalog/design/component-variants.md) — variant capability card\n\n(End of file - total 186 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: \"Webflow Designer Capabilities\"\ndescription: \"How the Webflow MCP 2.0 Designer surface works: canvas model, Bridge App boundary, selection-driven edit loop, element tree, styles and variable modes, components with props/variants/slots, breakpoints, assets, and pages — all draft-only until publish.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"webflow designer capabilities\"\n  - \"webflow designer logic\"\n  - \"webflow canvas model\"\n  - \"webflow element tree\"\n  - \"webflow design tokens\"\n  - \"webflow component variants\"\n  - \"webflow breakpoints\"\nimportance_tier: important\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.0.0.0\n---\n\n# Webflow Designer Capabilities - Canvas Model and Edit Logic\n\nThe operational logic of the Webflow MCP 2.0 Designer surface: what the canvas state is, which operations need the Bridge App, and how element, style, variable, component, and breakpoint edits compose into safe design workflows.\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/designer-capabilities.md","text":"---\ntitle: \"Webflow Designer Capabilities\"\ndescription: \"How the Webflow MCP 2.0 Designer surface works: canvas model, Bridge App boundary, selection-driven edit loop, element tree, styles and variable modes, components with props/variants/slots, breakpoints, assets, and pages — all draft-only until publish.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"webflow designer capabilities\"\n  - \"webflow designer logic\"\n  - \"webflow canvas model\"\n  - \"webflow element tree\"\n  - \"webflow design tokens\"\n  - \"webflow component variants\"\n  - \"webflow breakpoints\"\nimportance_tier: important\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.0.0.0\n---\n\n# Webflow Designer Capabilities - Canvas Model and Edit Logic\n\nThe operational logic of the Webflow MCP 2.0 Designer surface: what the canvas state is, which operations need the Bridge App, and how element, style, variable, component, and breakpoint edits compose into safe design workflows.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nThe Designer surface is the flagship of Webflow MCP 2.0: it operates on the live site tree and the open Designer canvas rather than on content records only. It splits into two planes with different connection requirements:\n\n- **Data-API designer modules** — elements, components, styles, variables, assets, and pages. These target the site tree through the Data API and work without the canvas open; the Bridge App is optional for them.\n- **Canvas-bound operations** — current page / mode / branch / component view / selection, canvas navigation, visual snapshots, and breakpoint reads. These read live Designer state and **require the Bridge App open in the Designer** (remote OAuth installs it automatically; local stdio mode needs the Bridge App Designer extension).\n\nEvery Designer edit is a **draft on the site tree** — nothing appears on the live site until a separate, gated `publish_site` runs. All Designer-family operations pair with `sk-design`: the transport executes, never decides taste.\n\n---\n\n## 2. CANVAS MODEL AND BRIDGE BOUNDARY\n\nThe live canvas exposes five pieces of state that shape every Designer workflow:\n\n| State | Read action | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| Current page | `get_current_page` | Which page is open in the Designer |\n| Current mode | `get_current_mode` | Design / preview / editing context |\n| Current branch | `get_current_branch_id`, `list_branches`, `get_branch_parent_page_id` | Branch-scoped edit contexts |\n| Component view | `get_current_component`, `check_if_inside_component_view` | When inside a component, mutations are scoped to the component |\n| Current selection | `get_selected_element` | The element the operator is looking at |\n\nNavigation actions: `open_canvas` (`component_id`, `page_id`), `switch_page` (`page_id`), `open_component_view` (component instance), `close_component_view`, `select_element` (`id {component, element}`).\n\nAll of these are **canvas-bound**: they read or move the live Designer state, so they fail when the Bridge App is not connected. `create_page_folder` and `open_canvas` are the only two draft-write actions in this group; everything else is read-only or canvas navigation. The bridge boundary is a failure mode, not a design limitation: a data-only session (CMS, content, publish) must never assume canvas state exists, and a Designer session must confirm the canvas is open before the edit loop starts.\n\n---\n\n## 3. SELECTION-DRIVEN EDIT LOOP\n\nThe canonical Designer workflow is a five-step loop, always starting from what is true on the canvas rather than from assumptions about the tree:\n\n1. **Snapshot** — `get_element_snapshot` (`id {component, element}`, RO) captures the element's rendered state before any change.\n2. **Discover** — `query_elements` (`queries[]`, RO) or `get_all_elements` (`pageId`, `siteId`, RO) locates the target in the tree.\n3. **Focus** — `select_element` or `open_canvas` puts the target in view so the operator and the agent agree on what is about to change.\n4. **Mutate** — a draft-write (DW) action from the element/style/variable/component sets (§4–§6), with the target id and a write preview.\n5. **Verify** — snapshot or query read-back confirms the postcondition; a DS action inside the loop requires operator confirmation plus a rollback statement (version-history restore) before it runs.\n\nThe loop is the contract for `sk-design` pairing: the design judgment step (what to change) happens before step 4, and the agent only executes. Every mutation step is individually confirmable, so a multi-edit design pass is a sequence of confirmable steps rather than one bulk write.\n\n---\n\n## 4. ELEMENT TREE SEMANTICS\n\nElements are addressed by `id {component, element}`: an element can be a plain node in the page tree or an instance inside a component. Positions are expressed as `parent_element_id` + `creation_position`; builder-style mutations add a `build_label` (the human-readable label of the build step) to `create_element` and the two component insertion actions.\n\n| Aspect | Actions | Class |\n|---|---|---|\n| Read | `get_all_elements`, `query_elements`, `get_display_name`, `get_attributes` | RO |\n| Structure | `create_element` (`element_schema{type}`), `move_element` (`anchor_element_id`), `set_display_name` | DW |\n| Content | `set_text`, `set_link` (`linkType`, `link`), `set_heading_level`, `set_image_asset`, `set_style` (`style_names`), `set_attributes` | DW |\n| Settings | `get_settings`, `set_settings` (`operations[]`), `set_dom_id`, `set_tag`, `set_visibility`, `get_bindable_sources` | RO / DW |\n| Destructive | `remove_element`, `remove_attribute` (`attribute_names`), `remove_style` | DS |\n\nSemantics that matter:\n\n- `set_style` references styles by `style_names` — the element points at named styles, it does not inline raw CSS. Styling an element therefore means first ensuring the style exists (§5).\n- `remove_element` accepts `{component, element}` ids: removing a component instance vs. a plain element are the same action but different rollback surfaces (component instances can be re-inserted; plain element removal relies on version history).\n- `set_visibility` and `set_dom_id` are per-element settings that affect interaction targets (CMS bindings, custom code) — a DW gate with a scope check.\n\n---\n\n## 5. STYLE AND DESIGN TOKENS\n\nStyles are named, reusable property sets; design tokens are typed variables collected into collections with modes. The two compose: styles can be bound to variable modes so a theme switch re-skins every element using the style.\n\n**Style lifecycle** (`data_style_tool`): `create_style` (`name`, `properties[]`, DW), `update_style`, `rename_style`, `remove_style` (DS), reads `query_styles` / `get_styles`. Mode bindings: `set_style_variable_mode` (`style_name`, `variable_collection_id`, `mode_id`, DW), `get_style_variable_modes`, `remove_style_variable_mode` / `remove_all_style_variable_modes` (DS).\n\n**Token lifecycle** (`data_variable_tool`): collections `create_variable_collection` / `reorder_variable_collection` (DW); modes `create_variable_mode` (DW); typed variables — color, font family, number, percentage, size — each with `create_*` / `update_*` (DW) and `delete_variable` (DS); reads `get_variable_collections`, `get_variables`, `query_variables`.\n\nTokenization logic: create collection → create mode (e.g. \"Light\") → create typed variables → `set_style_variable_mode` to bind a style → apply the style to elements. A second mode (\"Dark\") then re-skins the same style without touching elements. Renames ripple through every binding; deletes are DS because they break every bound style.\n\n---\n\n## 6. COMPONENTS: BUILDER, PROPS, VARIANTS, SLOTS\n\nComponents are the highest-leverage Designer capability: reusable trees with instance-level props, variants, slots, and metadata.\n\n| Aspect | Actions | Class |\n|---|---|---|\n| Lifecycle | `create_blank_component`, `duplicate_component`, `transform_element_to_component`, `set_component_metadata` | DW |\n| | `unregister_component` | DS |\n| Instances | `insert_component_instance` (`parent_element_id`, `component_id`, `creation_position`), `unlink_component_instance`, `get_parent_component` | DW / RO |\n| Builder | `insert_in_element` / `insert_in_slot` (`component_schema{name}`, `slot_name`, `build_label`) | DW |\n| Props | `create_prop`, `update_prop`, `set_component_instance_prop_values`, `reset_all_props_value`, `get_component_instance_props` | DW / RO |\n| | `remove_prop` | DS |\n| Variants | `create_variant`, `duplicate_variant`, `set_variant_name`, `reorder_variants`, `set_variant_styles`, `get_variant_settings`, `get_variant_styles` | DW / RO |\n| | `delete_variant` | DS |\n| View scoping | `open_component_view`, `close_component_view`, `get_current_component`, `check_if_inside_component_view` | DW / RO |\n\nComponent logic:\n\n- **Props are the API of the component**: instances are customized with `set_component_instance_prop_values`, never by editing the master tree. `reset_all_props_value` returns an instance to defaults (DW, preview the values first).\n- **Slots are extension points**: `insert_in_slot` builds inside a component slot, so a card component can accept arbitrary children. Slot targets need the `slot_name` plus the component schema.\n- **Variants are style layers**: `set_variant_styles` (`variant_id`, `style_name`) binds named styles to a variant; `get_variant_styles` / `get_variant_settings` read the current layer before changing it. Variant name/set/reorder are cheap; `delete_variant` is DS.\n- **Editing inside the component view** scopes element mutations to the component master; `check_if_inside_component_view` decides whether a proposed element edit targets the component or the page.\n\n---\n\n## 7. BREAKPOINTS AND RESPONSIVE LOGIC\n\nBreakpoints are **canvas-bound** state: `get_all_breakpoints` reads the live Designer breakpoint set and requires the Bridge App. Responsive logic is indirect but deliberate:\n\n- Styles carry `style_names` and are defined once; per-breakpoint behavior comes from the style system inside the Designer (a style's properties resolve per breakpoint in the canvas).\n- An element's responsive behavior is therefore changed by editing which styles apply (`set_style`) and what those styles contain (`create_style` / `update_style`), not by a dedicated responsive action.\n- Snapshot verification is breakpoint-aware: `get_element_snapshot` reflects the current canvas mode, so a responsive change should be verified at the target breakpoint with the canvas on that breakpoint.\n\n---\n\n## 8. ASSETS AND PAGES IN DESIGNER CONTEXT\n\n**Assets** feed the visual layer: `list_assets`, `get_asset`, `get_asset_preview`, `create_asset` (`file_name`, `file_hash`), `create_asset_folder`, `update_asset`, `update_asset_folder`, `upload_image_by_url` (DW), `compress_assets` (`format` — WebP/AVIF pipeline, DW), `list_compression_tasks` / `get_compression_task`, and `delete_asset` (DS). Elements bind to assets with `set_image_asset` (`image_asset_id`); the edit loop for an image swap is: upload → list to confirm the asset id → `set_image_asset` → snapshot verify.\n\n**Pages** are the canvas context and the branch vehicle: `create_page` (`siteId`, `title`, `slug`), `create_page_folder`, `update_page_settings`, `switch_page` (canvas-bound), plus branches `create_branch`, `get_branch_details`, `list_branches`, `get_branch_parent_page_id`, `get_current_branch_id` (all RO/DW) and `delete_branch` (DS). Branches are parallel edit contexts: switching the canvas to a branch isolates Designer edits from the main page until the branch merges — a natural staging pattern for design work.\n\n---\n\n## 9. OPERATION CLASSES AND GATES\n\n| Class | Examples | Gate |\n|---|---|---|\n| **RO** read-only | snapshot, query elements/styles/variables/components, canvas state reads, asset/pages reads, breakpoints | none |\n| **DW** draft-write | create/update elements, styles, variables, components, props, variants, assets, pages | scope check + target id + write preview; `sk-design` pairing for all Designer mutations |\n| **DS** destructive | `remove_element`, `remove_style`, `remove_style_variable_mode`, `remove_all_style_variable_modes`, `delete_variable`, `unregister_component`, `remove_prop`, `delete_variant`, `delete_asset`, `delete_branch` | operator confirmation with exact target + rollback statement (version-history restore) |\n| **Publish** | `publish_site` (separate surface) | fresh confirmation naming site/page scope + domains |\n\nTwo rules dominate: Designer edits are **draft-only until publish** (the Designer gate is upstream of the publish gate), and **taste never comes from the transport** — any layout/style/component decision loads `sk-design` first.\n\n---\n\n## 10. WORKED FLOWS\n\n### Flow A — Tokenized restyle (light theme)\n\n1. `create_variable_collection` \"Brand\" (DW) → `create_variable_mode` \"Light\" (DW) → `create_color_variable` \"brand-primary\" (DW)\n2. `create_style` \"Button Primary\" with `properties[]` (DW) → `set_style_variable_mode` binding the mode (DW)\n3. `query_elements` → `set_style` `[\"Button Primary\"]` on the target (DW)\n4. `get_element_snapshot` verify (RO)\n\n### Flow B — Component with variants\n\n1. `transform_element_to_component` (DW) or `create_blank_component` (DW)\n2. `create_prop` \"label\" (DW) → `set_component_instance_prop_values` on the inserted instance (DW)\n3. `create_variant` \"Hover\" (DW) → `set_variant_styles` binding a hover style (DW)\n4. `open_component_view` → element edits inside the view (DW, scoped) → `close_component_view`\n5. `get_element_snapshot` verify (RO)\n\n### Flow C — Image swap\n\n1. `upload_image_by_url` (DW) → `list_assets` to confirm the id (RO)\n2. `set_image_asset` on the element (DW)\n3. `get_asset_preview` / `get_element_snapshot` verify (RO)\n\n---\n\n## 11. RELATED RESOURCES\n\n- [`action-reference.md`](action-reference.md) — exact required parameters per Designer action\n- [`tool-surface.md`](tool-surface.md) — local OSS baseline and module layout\n- [`mcp-wiring.md`](mcp-wiring.md) — transport, auth, and Bridge App connection details\n- [`troubleshooting.md`](troubleshooting.md) — Bridge App / canvas failure triage\n- [`../feature-catalog/design/designer.md`](../feature-catalog/design/designer.md) — capability card\n- [`../feature-catalog/design/component-variants.md`](../feature-catalog/design/component-variants.md) — variant capability card","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":186,"totalLines":186,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/designer-capabilities.md","time":{"start":1785758296748,"end":1785758296754}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0988c57a5556d0f9016a70825804ac81919ec3380e043dd414"}},"id":"prt_fc77d2a5600100h1LBTl6bUmy0","sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","messageID":"msg_fc77cf028001ZMthqLhmQIiwqU"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785758296848,"sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_aWReIt5yf5JU0V8ohOPhRnaf","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/tool-surface.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/tool-surface.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Webflow MCP Tool Surface (Research Baseline)\"\n3: description: \"Research-time inventory of the local OSS webflow-mcp-server 18-module surface with risk classes; the remote surface lives in action-reference.md.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"webflow tool surface\"\n6:   - \"webflow mcp tools\"\n7:   - \"webflow tool inventory\"\n8:   - \"webflow actions\"\n9: importance_tier: important\n10: contextType: implementation\n11: version: 1.1.0.0\n12: ---\n13: # Webflow MCP Tool Surface (Local OSS Baseline)\n14: \n15: Research-time inventory of the local 18-module server surface.\n16: \n17: ---\n18: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n19: \n20: **Two surfaces.** The remote deployed surface (`com.webflow/mcp` 2.0.0) is documented at **31\n21: tools / 220 actions** in `action-reference.md` (official docs, 2026-08-03). This file is the\n22: **local OSS server baseline** (18 modules, research-time 2026-08-02). Baseline only: live\n23: discovery (`list_tools`) per session is the only trustworthy inventory; the pinned server\n24: version's actual surface must be recorded here after the first authenticated session.\n25: \n26: ---\n27: ## 2. Combined-Tool Pattern\n28: \n29: Each of the 18 modules registers **one MCP tool** whose input schema is an `actions` array of\n30: optional per-action objects; each action maps 1:1 to a Webflow Data API v2 endpoint\n31: (GET/POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE per the server source). Tool-level `readOnlyHint` exists but is not\n32: per-action — per-action class derives from the HTTP method + payload semantics.\n33: \n34: ---\n35: ## 3. Module Inventory (18 Modules, Official Repo `Src/Tools/`)\n36: \n37: | Module | Surface | Key actions (class) |\n38: |--------|---------|---------------------|\n39: | **sites** | site-level lifecycle | `list_sites` (RO), `get_site` (RO), `publish_site` (PB — POST /v2/sites/:id/publish; body must carry `customDomains` OR `publishToWebflowSubdomain`; optional `pageId`; 1/min queue) |\n40: | **pages** | page metadata/content/settings | `list_pages` (RO), `get_page_metadata` (RO), `get_page_content` (RO), `update_page_settings` (DW; schema also carries publishing status → PB when flipping to published), `update_static_content` (DW; secondary-locale DOM nodes) |\n41: | **cms** | collections + items | `get_collection_list` (RO), `get_collection_details` (RO), `list_collection_items` (RO), `create_collection*` (DW), `update_collection_field` (DW), `create_collection_items` (DW), `update_collection_items` (DW — bulk draft writes), `publish_collection_items` (PB), `delete_collection_items` (DS — permanent) |\n42: | **components** | site components | `list_components` (RO), `get_component_content` (RO), `get_component_properties` (RO), `update_component_content` (DW), `update_component_properties` (DW) |\n43: | **scripts** | custom code | `list_registered_scripts` (RO), `list_applied_scripts` (RO), `get_page_script` (RO), `add_inline_site_script` (DW), `upsert_page_script` (DW — ships with publish), `delete_all_site_scripts` (DS), `delete_all_page_scripts` (DS) |\n44: | **workflows** | workflow automation | `list_workflows` (RO), `list_workflow_runs` (RO), `get_workflow_run` (RO), `run_workflow` (DP — executes a pre-approved automation; blast radius depends on the workflow definition) |\n45: | **webhooks** | integration config | `list_webhooks` (RO), `get_webhook` (RO), `create_webhook` (DW), `delete_webhook` (DS — integration config, not site content) |\n46: | **enterprise** | Enterprise-gated (plan check) | `list_301_redirects` (RO), `get_robots_txt` (RO), `list_site_activity_logs` (RO), `create_301_redirect` (DW), `update_301_redirect` (DW), `update_robots_txt` (DW), `replace_robots_txt` (DW), `add_well_known_file` (DW), `delete_301_redirect` (DS), `delete_robots_txt` (DS), `remove_well_known_files` (DS) |\n47: | **aiChat** | AI Q&A | `ask_webflow_ai` (RO — Webflow AI over API knowledge; `readOnlyHint: true`) |\n48: | **comments** | comment threads | `list_comment_threads` (RO), `get_comment_thread` (RO), `list_comment_replies` (RO) |\n49: | **rules** | guidance | `webflow_guide_tool` (RO — best-practice guidance text, no side effects) |\n50: | **dePages** | Designer pages | `create_page` (DW), `create_page_folder` (DW), `switch_page` (DW) — Designer session required |\n51: | **deElement** | Designer elements | `query_elements` (RO), `get_selected_element` (RO), snapshot (RO), `select_element` (DW), `set_text` (DW), `set_style` (DW), `set_link` (DW), `set_heading_level` (DW), `set_image_asset` (DW), `add_or_update_attribute` (DW), `update_id_attribute` (DW), `remove_element` (DS), `remove_attribute` (DS), `remove_style` (DS), `remove_properties` (DS) |\n52: | **deStyle** | Designer styles | style read/get (RO), style create/update (DW), `remove_style` (DS) |\n53: | **deVariable** | Designer variables | `get_variable_collections` (RO), `get_variables` (RO), `query_variables` (RO), `create_variable_collection` (DW), `create_variable_mode` (DW), `create/update_*_variable` (DW), `rename_variable` (DW), `delete_variable` (DS) |\n54: | **deComponents** | Designer components | component read/get (RO), component builder (DW), `unregister_component` (DS) |\n55: | **deAsset** | Designer assets | asset read/list (RO), asset upload (DW), asset delete (DS) |\n56: | **localDeMCPConnection** | OSS-local only | `get_designer_app_connection_info` (RO — bridge-app connection state) |\n57: \n58: ---\n59: ## 4. Read-Only Surface (Safe, No Mutation)\n60: \n61: `ask_webflow_ai`, comments (list/get/replies), `webflow_guide_tool`, `get_designer_app_connection_info`,\n62: `list_sites`, `get_site`, `list_pages`, `get_page_metadata`, `get_page_content`, cms list/get,\n63: components list/get, scripts list/get, webhooks list/get, workflows list/get, enterprise\n64: list/get/robots/activity, plus the `de*` getters and `query_*` family.\n65: \n66: ---\n67: ## 5. Publish/Deploy Surface (Never Implicit)\n68: \n69: - `publish_site` — the single site-level deploy action (POST /v2/sites/:id/publish).\n70: - `publish_collection_items` — deploys CMS item drafts to live.\n71: - `run_workflow` — executes a pre-approved automation.\n72: - Script registration ships with site publish (publish-adjacent).\n73: - There is no other deploy path — every other mutation is draft/staging-scoped.\n74: \n75: ---\n76: ## 6. Destructive Surface (No Trash/Revert Via Mcp)\n77: \n78: CMS item deletion (permanent), script deletion (site/page), webhook deletion, enterprise redirect/\n79: robots/well-known deletion, `remove_element`/`remove_attribute`/`remove_style`/`remove_properties`,\n80: `delete_variable`, `unregister_component`, asset deletion. None expose an undo endpoint; rollback\n81: must be re-applied state or version-history snapshot re-publish. API-level site restore does not\n82: exist in the Data API v2 surface → treated as unsupported.\n83: \n84: ---\n85: ## 7. Cross-Cutting Facts\n86: \n87: - CMS mutations are NOT implicitly draft-safe — the client chooses live vs queued/drafted target.\n88: - Nothing auto-publishes; one publish queue per minute.\n89: - Rate limits: plan-based 60/120 rpm; 429 + `Retry-After` (~60s); SDK backoff default.\n90: - `custom_code` scopes are Data-Client-app-only (not site tokens).\n91: - Unknown modules default to RO/DW until discovery evidence proves a higher class (fail closed).\n92: - Enterprise module is gated to Enterprise plans; capability varies by workspace tier.\n93: \n94: ---\n95: ## 8. RELATED RESOURCES\n96: \n97: - [`action-reference.md`](action-reference.md) — remote surface (31 tools / 220 actions)\n98: - [`../SKILL.md`](../SKILL.md) — frozen classes and gates\n\n(End of file - total 98 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: \"Webflow MCP Tool Surface (Research Baseline)\"\ndescription: \"Research-time inventory of the local OSS webflow-mcp-server 18-module surface with risk classes; the remote surface lives in action-reference.md.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"webflow tool surface\"\n  - \"webflow mcp tools\"\n  - \"webflow tool inventory\"\n  - \"webflow actions\"\nimportance_tier: important\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.1.0.0\n---\n# Webflow MCP Tool Surface (Local OSS Baseline)\n\nResearch-time inventory of the local 18-module server surface.\n\n---\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n**Two surfaces.** The remote deployed surface (`com.webflow/mcp` 2.0.0) is documented at **31","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/tool-surface.md","text":"---\ntitle: \"Webflow MCP Tool Surface (Research Baseline)\"\ndescription: \"Research-time inventory of the local OSS webflow-mcp-server 18-module surface with risk classes; the remote surface lives in action-reference.md.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"webflow tool surface\"\n  - \"webflow mcp tools\"\n  - \"webflow tool inventory\"\n  - \"webflow actions\"\nimportance_tier: important\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.1.0.0\n---\n# Webflow MCP Tool Surface (Local OSS Baseline)\n\nResearch-time inventory of the local 18-module server surface.\n\n---\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n**Two surfaces.** The remote deployed surface (`com.webflow/mcp` 2.0.0) is documented at **31\ntools / 220 actions** in `action-reference.md` (official docs, 2026-08-03). This file is the\n**local OSS server baseline** (18 modules, research-time 2026-08-02). Baseline only: live\ndiscovery (`list_tools`) per session is the only trustworthy inventory; the pinned server\nversion's actual surface must be recorded here after the first authenticated session.\n\n---\n## 2. Combined-Tool Pattern\n\nEach of the 18 modules registers **one MCP tool** whose input schema is an `actions` array of\noptional per-action objects; each action maps 1:1 to a Webflow Data API v2 endpoint\n(GET/POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE per the server source). Tool-level `readOnlyHint` exists but is not\nper-action — per-action class derives from the HTTP method + payload semantics.\n\n---\n## 3. Module Inventory (18 Modules, Official Repo `Src/Tools/`)\n\n| Module | Surface | Key actions (class) |\n|--------|---------|---------------------|\n| **sites** | site-level lifecycle | `list_sites` (RO), `get_site` (RO), `publish_site` (PB — POST /v2/sites/:id/publish; body must carry `customDomains` OR `publishToWebflowSubdomain`; optional `pageId`; 1/min queue) |\n| **pages** | page metadata/content/settings | `list_pages` (RO), `get_page_metadata` (RO), `get_page_content` (RO), `update_page_settings` (DW; schema also carries publishing status → PB when flipping to published), `update_static_content` (DW; secondary-locale DOM nodes) |\n| **cms** | collections + items | `get_collection_list` (RO), `get_collection_details` (RO), `list_collection_items` (RO), `create_collection*` (DW), `update_collection_field` (DW), `create_collection_items` (DW), `update_collection_items` (DW — bulk draft writes), `publish_collection_items` (PB), `delete_collection_items` (DS — permanent) |\n| **components** | site components | `list_components` (RO), `get_component_content` (RO), `get_component_properties` (RO), `update_component_content` (DW), `update_component_properties` (DW) |\n| **scripts** | custom code | `list_registered_scripts` (RO), `list_applied_scripts` (RO), `get_page_script` (RO), `add_inline_site_script` (DW), `upsert_page_script` (DW — ships with publish), `delete_all_site_scripts` (DS), `delete_all_page_scripts` (DS) |\n| **workflows** | workflow automation | `list_workflows` (RO), `list_workflow_runs` (RO), `get_workflow_run` (RO), `run_workflow` (DP — executes a pre-approved automation; blast radius depends on the workflow definition) |\n| **webhooks** | integration config | `list_webhooks` (RO), `get_webhook` (RO), `create_webhook` (DW), `delete_webhook` (DS — integration config, not site content) |\n| **enterprise** | Enterprise-gated (plan check) | `list_301_redirects` (RO), `get_robots_txt` (RO), `list_site_activity_logs` (RO), `create_301_redirect` (DW), `update_301_redirect` (DW), `update_robots_txt` (DW), `replace_robots_txt` (DW), `add_well_known_file` (DW), `delete_301_redirect` (DS), `delete_robots_txt` (DS), `remove_well_known_files` (DS) |\n| **aiChat** | AI Q&A | `ask_webflow_ai` (RO — Webflow AI over API knowledge; `readOnlyHint: true`) |\n| **comments** | comment threads | `list_comment_threads` (RO), `get_comment_thread` (RO), `list_comment_replies` (RO) |\n| **rules** | guidance | `webflow_guide_tool` (RO — best-practice guidance text, no side effects) |\n| **dePages** | Designer pages | `create_page` (DW), `create_page_folder` (DW), `switch_page` (DW) — Designer session required |\n| **deElement** | Designer elements | `query_elements` (RO), `get_selected_element` (RO), snapshot (RO), `select_element` (DW), `set_text` (DW), `set_style` (DW), `set_link` (DW), `set_heading_level` (DW), `set_image_asset` (DW), `add_or_update_attribute` (DW), `update_id_attribute` (DW), `remove_element` (DS), `remove_attribute` (DS), `remove_style` (DS), `remove_properties` (DS) |\n| **deStyle** | Designer styles | style read/get (RO), style create/update (DW), `remove_style` (DS) |\n| **deVariable** | Designer variables | `get_variable_collections` (RO), `get_variables` (RO), `query_variables` (RO), `create_variable_collection` (DW), `create_variable_mode` (DW), `create/update_*_variable` (DW), `rename_variable` (DW), `delete_variable` (DS) |\n| **deComponents** | Designer components | component read/get (RO), component builder (DW), `unregister_component` (DS) |\n| **deAsset** | Designer assets | asset read/list (RO), asset upload (DW), asset delete (DS) |\n| **localDeMCPConnection** | OSS-local only | `get_designer_app_connection_info` (RO — bridge-app connection state) |\n\n---\n## 4. Read-Only Surface (Safe, No Mutation)\n\n`ask_webflow_ai`, comments (list/get/replies), `webflow_guide_tool`, `get_designer_app_connection_info`,\n`list_sites`, `get_site`, `list_pages`, `get_page_metadata`, `get_page_content`, cms list/get,\ncomponents list/get, scripts list/get, webhooks list/get, workflows list/get, enterprise\nlist/get/robots/activity, plus the `de*` getters and `query_*` family.\n\n---\n## 5. Publish/Deploy Surface (Never Implicit)\n\n- `publish_site` — the single site-level deploy action (POST /v2/sites/:id/publish).\n- `publish_collection_items` — deploys CMS item drafts to live.\n- `run_workflow` — executes a pre-approved automation.\n- Script registration ships with site publish (publish-adjacent).\n- There is no other deploy path — every other mutation is draft/staging-scoped.\n\n---\n## 6. Destructive Surface (No Trash/Revert Via Mcp)\n\nCMS item deletion (permanent), script deletion (site/page), webhook deletion, enterprise redirect/\nrobots/well-known deletion, `remove_element`/`remove_attribute`/`remove_style`/`remove_properties`,\n`delete_variable`, `unregister_component`, asset deletion. None expose an undo endpoint; rollback\nmust be re-applied state or version-history snapshot re-publish. API-level site restore does not\nexist in the Data API v2 surface → treated as unsupported.\n\n---\n## 7. Cross-Cutting Facts\n\n- CMS mutations are NOT implicitly draft-safe — the client chooses live vs queued/drafted target.\n- Nothing auto-publishes; one publish queue per minute.\n- Rate limits: plan-based 60/120 rpm; 429 + `Retry-After` (~60s); SDK backoff default.\n- `custom_code` scopes are Data-Client-app-only (not site tokens).\n- Unknown modules default to RO/DW until discovery evidence proves a higher class (fail closed).\n- Enterprise module is gated to Enterprise plans; capability varies by workspace tier.\n\n---\n## 8. RELATED RESOURCES\n\n- [`action-reference.md`](action-reference.md) — remote surface (31 tools / 220 actions)\n- [`../SKILL.md`](../SKILL.md) — frozen classes and gates","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":98,"totalLines":98,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/tool-surface.md","time":{"start":1785758296833,"end":1785758296843}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0988c57a5556d0f9016a70825804b48191a795ff87cd70e76d"}},"id":"prt_fc77d2ab5001WeD59FoejXTGxN","sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","messageID":"msg_fc77cf028001ZMthqLhmQIiwqU"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785758297015,"sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_O3S7irOgL2EV3rQSwFEntx3w","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/mcp-wiring.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/mcp-wiring.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Webflow MCP Wiring (via Code Mode)\"\n3: description: \"How the official Webflow MCP 2.0 transport is wired through Code Mode: registered manual, local stdio + WEBFLOW_TOKEN, the remote OAuth alternative, scope model, rate limits, Bridge App boundary, and surface reconciliation.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"webflow mcp wiring\"\n6:   - \"webflow utcp manual\"\n7:   - \"webflow code mode\"\n8:   - \"webflow token\"\n9:   - \"webflow oauth\"\n10:   - \"webflow bridge app\"\n11: importance_tier: important\n12: contextType: implementation\n13: version: 1.2.0.0\n14: ---\n15: \n16: # Webflow MCP Wiring (via Code Mode)\n17: \n18: How the official Webflow MCP 2.0 transport is wired through Code Mode, with the full auth and rate-limit contract.\n19: \n20: ---\n21: \n22: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n23: \n24: Transport identity (frozen): official `webflow-mcp-server` (npm), local stdio registration with\n25: `WEBFLOW_TOKEN` as the deterministic automation default; remote OAuth (`https://mcp.webflow.com/mcp`\n26: per hosted docs; `/sse` per the repo README — see §6) as the operator-preference alternative.\n27: Version pinning and the README-vs-hosted surface reconciliation are mandatory before first live\n28: use.\n29: \n30: Webflow MCP 2.0 exposes Webflow's Data API v2 and Designer API as a bounded combined-tool surface\n31: (18 tool modules, one MCP tool per module with an `actions` array). This skill reaches it through\n32: the repo's **Code Mode** transport. Code Mode consumes stdio; the official server ships as a Node\n33: CLI (`npx -y webflow-mcp-server@latest`), so the registered `webflow` manual is a plain stdio\n34: registration — no bridge needed for the local path. The remote OAuth surface speaks remote HTTP\n35: and requires the `mcp-remote` bridge (§5).\n36: \n37: Claims below are tagged **[CONFIRMED]** (read from this repo's config or cited official docs at\n38: research time), **[INFERRED]** (supported but not exercised end-to-end), or **[UNKNOWN]**\n39: (requires an authenticated session or a provisioned test site).\n40: \n41: ---\n42: ## 2. THE REGISTERED `webflow` MANUAL\n43: \n44: Registered in `.utcp_config.json` (manual call template, type `mcp`):\n45: \n46: ```json\n47: {\n48:   \"name\": \"webflow\",\n49:   \"call_template_type\": \"mcp\",\n50:   \"config\": {\n51:     \"mcpServers\": {\n52:       \"webflow\": {\n53:         \"transport\": \"stdio\",\n54:         \"command\": \"npx\",\n55:         \"args\": [\"-y\", \"webflow-mcp-server@latest\"],\n56:         \"env\": { \"WEBFLOW_TOKEN\": \"${WEBFLOW_TOKEN}\" }\n57:       }\n58:     }\n59:   }\n60: }\n61: ```\n62: \n63: **Validated as-is: verify, never re-add, never edit the entry.** The env placeholder resolves from\n64: the operator's environment (`.env.example` documents the namespaced `webflow_WEBFLOW_TOKEN`).\n65: Server prerequisites: Node.js 22.3.0+ **[CONFIRMED]**.\n66: \n67: ---\n68: ## 3. AUTHENTICATION (least privilege)\n69: \n70: ### Token kinds\n71: \n72: | Kind | Scope | Use |\n73: |------|-------|-----|\n74: | **Site Token** | single site; full scope model | automation baseline (deterministic) |\n75: | **Workspace Token** | all sites in workspace; **no `site` scope** | read-only monitoring/auditing only |\n76: | **OAuth token** | multi-site, user-specific | public apps / interactive remote flow |\n77: \n78: ### Scope model (site-level)\n79: \n80: `assets:read/write`, `authorized_user:read`, `cms:read/write`, `comments:read/write`,\n81: `components:read/write`, `custom_code:read/write` (**Data Client apps only** — site tokens cannot\n82: access custom-code endpoints), `ecommerce:read/write`, `forms:read/write`, `pages:read/write`,\n83: `sites:read/write`, `site_activity:read`, `site_config:read/write`, `users:read/write`, `webhooks`\n84: (per trigger type), `workspace:read/write`.\n85: \n86: ### Frozen baseline (automation)\n87: \n88: - Read-only baseline scopes: `cms:read`, `pages:read`, `sites:read`, `assets:read`,\n89:   `components:read`, `forms:read`, `authorized_user:read`.\n90: - Escalate to `sites:write` only for the staging-subdomain publish test.\n91: - Official best practice: minimal scopes; mint a new token when new scopes are needed.\n92: - Role gate: only site owners/admins can authorize the MCP server/app.\n93: - Token values live only in the operator environment; the repo carries names and placeholders.\n94: \n95: ---\n96: ## 4. DISCOVERY-FIRST CONTRACT\n97: \n98: Before invoking any Webflow tool:\n99: \n100: ```ts\n101: const tools = await list_tools();            // live discovery per session\n102: const webflow = tools.filter(t => t.name.startsWith(\"webflow.webflow.\"));\n103: ```\n104: \n105: Expected callable names follow the Code Mode convention `{manual}.{manual}_{tool}` (registry\n106: `webflow.webflow.<tool>` / TypeScript `webflow.webflow_<tool>`) — **UNVERIFIED** until\n107: authenticated discovery (mobbin precedent: `mobbin.mobbin.search_screens` /\n108: `mobbin.mobbin_search_screens`). The research-time inventory (18 modules) is the baseline in\n109: `tool-surface.md`; **always re-discover per session** — never call from memory, and fail closed on\n110: drift.\n111: \n112: ---\n113: ## 5. REMOTE OAUTH ALTERNATIVE\n114: \n115: - Endpoint per hosted docs: `https://mcp.webflow.com/mcp` (Streamable HTTP; registry\n116:   `com.webflow/mcp` 2.0.0) — Claude Code: `claude mcp add --transport http webflow\n117:   https://mcp.webflow.com/mcp`; Cursor: URL in MCP config.\n118: - Reached via the same bridge pattern as `refero`: `npx -y mcp-remote https://mcp.webflow.com/mcp`\n119:   as a stdio manual, browser OAuth consent per site/workspace, auth state under `~/.mcp-auth/`.\n120: - The remote transport (`mcp-remote`) is **experimental** — pin the version.\n121: - The Bridge App installs automatically during remote OAuth authorization; local mode needs the\n122:   Bridge App Designer extension for Designer tools (§7).\n123: - Not registered by default; operator decision required (interactive consent is not\n124:   automation-friendly).\n125: \n126: ---\n127: ## 6. VERSION-SURFACE CONTRADICTION (reconcile per session)\n128: \n129: | Surface | Documents | Evidence |\n130: |---------|-----------|----------|\n131: | Remote (hosted) | Streamable HTTP `https://mcp.webflow.com/mcp`; resources + Agent Instructions; setup guides for Claude/Cursor/Postman/Windsurf | developers.webflow.com/mcp/* **[CONFIRMED]** |\n132: | Remote (repo README) | `https://mcp.webflow.com/sse`; no `prompts`/`resources` | github.com/webflow/mcp-server README **[CONFIRMED]** |\n133: | Local OSS | stdio + `WEBFLOW_TOKEN`; `dist/index.js` entry; separate from remote path | repo package.json/src/index.ts **[CONFIRMED]** |\n134: \n135: Treat the deployed remote surface and the OSS snapshot as **different surfaces** until a\n136: version-specific reconciliation lands; the local stdio server is the deterministic baseline for\n137: automation. Record the tested endpoint + version in `mcp-servers/webflow-mcp/README.md` after the\n138: first authenticated session.\n139: \n140: ---\n141: ## 7. DESIGNER BRIDGE APP BOUNDARY\n142: \n143: - Data API tools work with Webflow closed **[CONFIRMED]**.\n144: - Designer API tools (`de*` families: deAsset, deComponents, deElement, dePages, deStyle,\n145:   deVariable) require the **Bridge App** open in the Designer (auto-installs to authorized sites\n146:   after OAuth; local mode needs a registered/published Bridge App Designer extension).\n147: - Designer edits are draft operations inside the Designer; they become visible only via\n148:   `publish_site`.\n149: - All Designer-family operations must load `sk-design` first (cross-hub pairing).\n150: \n151: ---\n152: ## 8. RATE LIMITS AND ERROR SEMANTICS\n153: \n154: - Plan-based general limits: Starter/Basic 60 req/min; CMS/eCommerce/Business 120 req/min;\n155:   Enterprise custom. Headers: `X-RateLimit-Limit` / `X-RateLimit-Remaining`.\n156: - 429 responses carry `Retry-After` (~60s) — honor it; never blind-replay ambiguous\n157:   non-idempotent writes after errors.\n158: - Site publish: **one successful publish per minute**.\n159: - The official SDK (used by the server) has built-in exponential backoff.\n160: \n161: ---\n162: ## 9. DIAGNOSTIC FLOW\n163: \n164: 1. `scripts/doctor.sh` — node/npx versions, manual presence (verify, never re-add), token\n165:    presence (boolean only), config parse.\n166: 2. If discovery fails: check the manual env resolution (`${WEBFLOW_TOKEN}` from the operator\n167:    environment), token scopes (read-only baseline cannot call write actions), 429/`Retry-After`\n168:    backoff, and the pinned server version vs `tool-surface.md`.\n169: 3. Designer tools failing → Bridge App not open/authorized; confirm Designer session + pairing.\n170: 4. On any drift between live `list_tools` and the baseline inventory → record the drift, fail\n171:    closed on mismatched tools, and update `tool-surface.md` with the dated fixture.\n172: \n173: ---\n174: ## 10. SAFETY BOUNDARY (summary)\n175: \n176: - Read-only and draft-safe mutations pass without a gate (scope check only).\n177: - Destructive (`delete_*`, `remove_*`), publish (`publish_site`, `publish_collection_items`,\n178:   publish-status changes), and deploy (`run_workflow`, script registration) classes **require\n179:   operator confirmation** and rollback evidence.\n180: - Publish from smoke/test flows to `publishToWebflowSubdomain` only — never `customDomains`;\n181:   single `pageId` limits blast radius.\n182: - Nothing auto-publishes; CMS mutations are not implicitly draft-safe.\n183: - Workspace tokens are read-only; `custom_code` scopes are Data-Client-app-only.\n184: - API-level site backup/restore does not exist in the Data API v2 surface — DS class carries the\n185:   strongest confirmations.\n186: \n187: ---\n188: ## 11. RELATED RESOURCES\n189: \n190: - [`action-reference.md`](action-reference.md) — remote surface (31 tools / 220 actions)\n191: - [`tool-surface.md`](tool-surface.md) — local OSS baseline\n192: - [`troubleshooting.md`](troubleshooting.md) — failure modes\n193: - [`../SKILL.md`](../SKILL.md) — frozen classes and gates\n\n(End of file - total 193 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: \"Webflow MCP Wiring (via Code Mode)\"\ndescription: \"How the official Webflow MCP 2.0 transport is wired through Code Mode: registered manual, local stdio + WEBFLOW_TOKEN, the remote OAuth alternative, scope model, rate limits, Bridge App boundary, and surface reconciliation.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"webflow mcp wiring\"\n  - \"webflow utcp manual\"\n  - \"webflow code mode\"\n  - \"webflow token\"\n  - \"webflow oauth\"\n  - \"webflow bridge app\"\nimportance_tier: important\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.2.0.0\n---\n\n# Webflow MCP Wiring (via Code Mode)\n\nHow the official Webflow MCP 2.0 transport is wired through Code Mode, with the full auth and rate-limit contract.\n\n---","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/mcp-wiring.md","text":"---\ntitle: \"Webflow MCP Wiring (via Code Mode)\"\ndescription: \"How the official Webflow MCP 2.0 transport is wired through Code Mode: registered manual, local stdio + WEBFLOW_TOKEN, the remote OAuth alternative, scope model, rate limits, Bridge App boundary, and surface reconciliation.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"webflow mcp wiring\"\n  - \"webflow utcp manual\"\n  - \"webflow code mode\"\n  - \"webflow token\"\n  - \"webflow oauth\"\n  - \"webflow bridge app\"\nimportance_tier: important\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.2.0.0\n---\n\n# Webflow MCP Wiring (via Code Mode)\n\nHow the official Webflow MCP 2.0 transport is wired through Code Mode, with the full auth and rate-limit contract.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nTransport identity (frozen): official `webflow-mcp-server` (npm), local stdio registration with\n`WEBFLOW_TOKEN` as the deterministic automation default; remote OAuth (`https://mcp.webflow.com/mcp`\nper hosted docs; `/sse` per the repo README — see §6) as the operator-preference alternative.\nVersion pinning and the README-vs-hosted surface reconciliation are mandatory before first live\nuse.\n\nWebflow MCP 2.0 exposes Webflow's Data API v2 and Designer API as a bounded combined-tool surface\n(18 tool modules, one MCP tool per module with an `actions` array). This skill reaches it through\nthe repo's **Code Mode** transport. Code Mode consumes stdio; the official server ships as a Node\nCLI (`npx -y webflow-mcp-server@latest`), so the registered `webflow` manual is a plain stdio\nregistration — no bridge needed for the local path. The remote OAuth surface speaks remote HTTP\nand requires the `mcp-remote` bridge (§5).\n\nClaims below are tagged **[CONFIRMED]** (read from this repo's config or cited official docs at\nresearch time), **[INFERRED]** (supported but not exercised end-to-end), or **[UNKNOWN]**\n(requires an authenticated session or a provisioned test site).\n\n---\n## 2. THE REGISTERED `webflow` MANUAL\n\nRegistered in `.utcp_config.json` (manual call template, type `mcp`):\n\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"webflow\",\n  \"call_template_type\": \"mcp\",\n  \"config\": {\n    \"mcpServers\": {\n      \"webflow\": {\n        \"transport\": \"stdio\",\n        \"command\": \"npx\",\n        \"args\": [\"-y\", \"webflow-mcp-server@latest\"],\n        \"env\": { \"WEBFLOW_TOKEN\": \"${WEBFLOW_TOKEN}\" }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Validated as-is: verify, never re-add, never edit the entry.** The env placeholder resolves from\nthe operator's environment (`.env.example` documents the namespaced `webflow_WEBFLOW_TOKEN`).\nServer prerequisites: Node.js 22.3.0+ **[CONFIRMED]**.\n\n---\n## 3. AUTHENTICATION (least privilege)\n\n### Token kinds\n\n| Kind | Scope | Use |\n|------|-------|-----|\n| **Site Token** | single site; full scope model | automation baseline (deterministic) |\n| **Workspace Token** | all sites in workspace; **no `site` scope** | read-only monitoring/auditing only |\n| **OAuth token** | multi-site, user-specific | public apps / interactive remote flow |\n\n### Scope model (site-level)\n\n`assets:read/write`, `authorized_user:read`, `cms:read/write`, `comments:read/write`,\n`components:read/write`, `custom_code:read/write` (**Data Client apps only** — site tokens cannot\naccess custom-code endpoints), `ecommerce:read/write`, `forms:read/write`, `pages:read/write`,\n`sites:read/write`, `site_activity:read`, `site_config:read/write`, `users:read/write`, `webhooks`\n(per trigger type), `workspace:read/write`.\n\n### Frozen baseline (automation)\n\n- Read-only baseline scopes: `cms:read`, `pages:read`, `sites:read`, `assets:read`,\n  `components:read`, `forms:read`, `authorized_user:read`.\n- Escalate to `sites:write` only for the staging-subdomain publish test.\n- Official best practice: minimal scopes; mint a new token when new scopes are needed.\n- Role gate: only site owners/admins can authorize the MCP server/app.\n- Token values live only in the operator environment; the repo carries names and placeholders.\n\n---\n## 4. DISCOVERY-FIRST CONTRACT\n\nBefore invoking any Webflow tool:\n\n```ts\nconst tools = await list_tools();            // live discovery per session\nconst webflow = tools.filter(t => t.name.startsWith(\"webflow.webflow.\"));\n```\n\nExpected callable names follow the Code Mode convention `{manual}.{manual}_{tool}` (registry\n`webflow.webflow.<tool>` / TypeScript `webflow.webflow_<tool>`) — **UNVERIFIED** until\nauthenticated discovery (mobbin precedent: `mobbin.mobbin.search_screens` /\n`mobbin.mobbin_search_screens`). The research-time inventory (18 modules) is the baseline in\n`tool-surface.md`; **always re-discover per session** — never call from memory, and fail closed on\ndrift.\n\n---\n## 5. REMOTE OAUTH ALTERNATIVE\n\n- Endpoint per hosted docs: `https://mcp.webflow.com/mcp` (Streamable HTTP; registry\n  `com.webflow/mcp` 2.0.0) — Claude Code: `claude mcp add --transport http webflow\n  https://mcp.webflow.com/mcp`; Cursor: URL in MCP config.\n- Reached via the same bridge pattern as `refero`: `npx -y mcp-remote https://mcp.webflow.com/mcp`\n  as a stdio manual, browser OAuth consent per site/workspace, auth state under `~/.mcp-auth/`.\n- The remote transport (`mcp-remote`) is **experimental** — pin the version.\n- The Bridge App installs automatically during remote OAuth authorization; local mode needs the\n  Bridge App Designer extension for Designer tools (§7).\n- Not registered by default; operator decision required (interactive consent is not\n  automation-friendly).\n\n---\n## 6. VERSION-SURFACE CONTRADICTION (reconcile per session)\n\n| Surface | Documents | Evidence |\n|---------|-----------|----------|\n| Remote (hosted) | Streamable HTTP `https://mcp.webflow.com/mcp`; resources + Agent Instructions; setup guides for Claude/Cursor/Postman/Windsurf | developers.webflow.com/mcp/* **[CONFIRMED]** |\n| Remote (repo README) | `https://mcp.webflow.com/sse`; no `prompts`/`resources` | github.com/webflow/mcp-server README **[CONFIRMED]** |\n| Local OSS | stdio + `WEBFLOW_TOKEN`; `dist/index.js` entry; separate from remote path | repo package.json/src/index.ts **[CONFIRMED]** |\n\nTreat the deployed remote surface and the OSS snapshot as **different surfaces** until a\nversion-specific reconciliation lands; the local stdio server is the deterministic baseline for\nautomation. Record the tested endpoint + version in `mcp-servers/webflow-mcp/README.md` after the\nfirst authenticated session.\n\n---\n## 7. DESIGNER BRIDGE APP BOUNDARY\n\n- Data API tools work with Webflow closed **[CONFIRMED]**.\n- Designer API tools (`de*` families: deAsset, deComponents, deElement, dePages, deStyle,\n  deVariable) require the **Bridge App** open in the Designer (auto-installs to authorized sites\n  after OAuth; local mode needs a registered/published Bridge App Designer extension).\n- Designer edits are draft operations inside the Designer; they become visible only via\n  `publish_site`.\n- All Designer-family operations must load `sk-design` first (cross-hub pairing).\n\n---\n## 8. RATE LIMITS AND ERROR SEMANTICS\n\n- Plan-based general limits: Starter/Basic 60 req/min; CMS/eCommerce/Business 120 req/min;\n  Enterprise custom. Headers: `X-RateLimit-Limit` / `X-RateLimit-Remaining`.\n- 429 responses carry `Retry-After` (~60s) — honor it; never blind-replay ambiguous\n  non-idempotent writes after errors.\n- Site publish: **one successful publish per minute**.\n- The official SDK (used by the server) has built-in exponential backoff.\n\n---\n## 9. DIAGNOSTIC FLOW\n\n1. `scripts/doctor.sh` — node/npx versions, manual presence (verify, never re-add), token\n   presence (boolean only), config parse.\n2. If discovery fails: check the manual env resolution (`${WEBFLOW_TOKEN}` from the operator\n   environment), token scopes (read-only baseline cannot call write actions), 429/`Retry-After`\n   backoff, and the pinned server version vs `tool-surface.md`.\n3. Designer tools failing → Bridge App not open/authorized; confirm Designer session + pairing.\n4. On any drift between live `list_tools` and the baseline inventory → record the drift, fail\n   closed on mismatched tools, and update `tool-surface.md` with the dated fixture.\n\n---\n## 10. SAFETY BOUNDARY (summary)\n\n- Read-only and draft-safe mutations pass without a gate (scope check only).\n- Destructive (`delete_*`, `remove_*`), publish (`publish_site`, `publish_collection_items`,\n  publish-status changes), and deploy (`run_workflow`, script registration) classes **require\n  operator confirmation** and rollback evidence.\n- Publish from smoke/test flows to `publishToWebflowSubdomain` only — never `customDomains`;\n  single `pageId` limits blast radius.\n- Nothing auto-publishes; CMS mutations are not implicitly draft-safe.\n- Workspace tokens are read-only; `custom_code` scopes are Data-Client-app-only.\n- API-level site backup/restore does not exist in the Data API v2 surface — DS class carries the\n  strongest confirmations.\n\n---\n## 11. RELATED RESOURCES\n\n- [`action-reference.md`](action-reference.md) — remote surface (31 tools / 220 actions)\n- [`tool-surface.md`](tool-surface.md) — local OSS baseline\n- [`troubleshooting.md`](troubleshooting.md) — failure modes\n- [`../SKILL.md`](../SKILL.md) — frozen classes and gates","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":193,"totalLines":193,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/mcp-wiring.md","time":{"start":1785758297006,"end":1785758297013}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0988c57a5556d0f9016a70825804bc819191b349dab9e3c1be"}},"id":"prt_fc77d2b04001tz06bl7DoUwS56","sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","messageID":"msg_fc77cf028001ZMthqLhmQIiwqU"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785758297176,"sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_NLchhBmREChtBGlbUgvoQCDQ","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/troubleshooting.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/troubleshooting.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Webflow MCP Troubleshooting\"\n3: description: \"Common failure modes for the webflow Code Mode manual: token and scope issues, discovery failures, rate limits, publish queue, Designer Bridge App, version-surface contradictions, and redaction rules.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"webflow troubleshooting\"\n6:   - \"webflow mcp not working\"\n7:   - \"webflow token error\"\n8:   - \"webflow 429\"\n9:   - \"webflow bridge app\"\n10: importance_tier: normal\n11: contextType: implementation\n12: version: 1.1.0.0\n13: ---\n14: # Webflow MCP Troubleshooting\n15: \n16: Common failure modes for the webflow Code Mode manual and their fixes.\n17: \n18: ---\n19: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n20: \n21: This reference covers discovery failures, auth/scope errors, rate limiting, publish-queue issues,\n22: Designer Bridge App failures, surface drift, and redaction rules. Run `../scripts/doctor.sh`\n23: (verify-only) first.\n24: \n25: ---\n26: \n27: \n28: ---\n29: ## 2. Discovery Fails (No `Webflow.Webflow.*` Tools In `List_Tools`)\n30: \n31: 1. Confirm the operator environment exports `WEBFLOW_TOKEN` (namespaced\n32:    `webflow_WEBFLOW_TOKEN` in `.env.example`); the Code Mode manual resolves `${WEBFLOW_TOKEN}`\n33:    from the environment. Check `scripts/doctor.sh` (boolean token check — never prints values).\n34: 2. Confirm npx can fetch `webflow-mcp-server` (offline cache, registry access). If the pinned\n35:    version is unreachable, restore the recorded pinned version from\n36:    `../mcp-servers/webflow-mcp/README.md`.\n37: 3. Confirm Node >= 22.3.0 (the server's documented runtime requirement).\n38: 4. Re-run discovery per session; never call from memory.\n39: \n40: ---\n41: ## 3. Tool Calls Fail With Auth Errors (401/403)\n42: \n43: | Symptom | Cause | Fix |\n44: |---------|-------|-----|\n45: | 401 on everything | missing/expired `WEBFLOW_TOKEN` | export a valid token; restart the manual |\n46: | 403 on a specific action | token scopes insufficient for the action's class | check the action's required scope (`tool-surface.md`); mint a least-privilege token with the needed scope |\n47: | 403 on site-level calls | workspace token (no `site` scope) | use a Site Token for site-level operations |\n48: | 403 on custom-code endpoints | `custom_code` scopes are Data-Client-app-only | use a Data Client app token or drop the call |\n49: | 403 on authorize | role below owner/admin | only site owners/admins can authorize the MCP server |\n50: \n51: ---\n52: ## 4. Rate Limiting (429)\n53: \n54: - Honor `Retry-After` (~60s); the official SDK applies exponential backoff by default.\n55: - Publishing is limited to one successful queue per minute — batch or wait.\n56: - Plan-based general limits: Starter/Basic 60 rpm; CMS/eCommerce/Business 120 rpm.\n57: - Never blind-replay ambiguous non-idempotent writes after a 429/error.\n58: \n59: ---\n60: ## 5. Publish Failures\n61: \n62: - \"Publish queue busy\": one publish per minute — wait and retry once, verify before retry.\n63: - Staging vs production: the publish body requires `customDomains` OR `publishToWebflowSubdomain`.\n64:   Smoke flows must pass only the staging flag (optionally scoped to a single `pageId`).\n65: - Published drafts didn't appear: CMS items may have been written to the draft queue — publishing\n66:   is a separate explicit action (`publish_collection_items`).\n67: \n68: ---\n69: ## 6. Designer / Bridge App Failures (`De*` Tools)\n70: \n71: - Designer tools fail when Webflow is closed or the Designer session has no authorized site —\n72:   Designer API tools require the Bridge App open in the Designer.\n73: - Bridge App not installed: it auto-installs to authorized sites after remote OAuth; local mode\n74:   needs a registered/published MCP Bridge App Designer extension.\n75: - `get_designer_app_connection_info` (RO) reports connection state — check it before Designer work.\n76: - Designer edits are draft-only; they appear on the live site only after `publish_site`.\n77: \n78: ---\n79: ## 7. Suspicious Or Missing Tools\n80: \n81: - The public `webflow/mcp-server` README and the hosted docs disagree on the surface (`/sse` vs\n82:   `/mcp`, resources presence). Treat the **pinned server version's live discovery** as\n83:   authoritative; record dated fixtures in `tool-surface.md`.\n84: - Unknown tool modules default to read-only/draft-write until discovery proves otherwise\n85:   (fail closed) — never grant destructive/publish/deploy classes by default.\n86: - Tool named differently than the baseline: record the drift and update the fixture; do not\n87:   guess.\n88: \n89: ---\n90: ## 8. WORKFLOW AND WEBHOOK ISSUES\n91: \n92: - `run_workflow` fails: confirm the workflow id and required inputs (`flows`/`workflows` list is\n93:   RO); the blast radius depends on the workflow definition — state it in the confirmation.\n94: - Webhook create/delete: integration config, not site content; `delete_webhook` is destructive\n95:   class.\n96: \n97: ---\n98: ## 9. REDACTION RULES\n99: \n100: - Never commit or log token values; redact tool output containing them.\n101: - Never print the resolved `${WEBFLOW_TOKEN}` value (doctor.sh reports presence only).\n102: - Never record account identifiers in fixtures.\n103: \n104: ---\n105: ## 10. RELATED RESOURCES\n106: \n107: - [`mcp-wiring.md`](mcp-wiring.md) — wiring and auth details\n108: - [`action-reference.md`](action-reference.md) — action inventory\n109: - [`../SKILL.md`](../SKILL.md) — frozen classes and gates\n\n(End of file - total 109 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: \"Webflow MCP Troubleshooting\"\ndescription: \"Common failure modes for the webflow Code Mode manual: token and scope issues, discovery failures, rate limits, publish queue, Designer Bridge App, version-surface contradictions, and redaction rules.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"webflow troubleshooting\"\n  - \"webflow mcp not working\"\n  - \"webflow token error\"\n  - \"webflow 429\"\n  - \"webflow bridge app\"\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.1.0.0\n---\n# Webflow MCP Troubleshooting\n\nCommon failure modes for the webflow Code Mode manual and their fixes.\n\n---\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/troubleshooting.md","text":"---\ntitle: \"Webflow MCP Troubleshooting\"\ndescription: \"Common failure modes for the webflow Code Mode manual: token and scope issues, discovery failures, rate limits, publish queue, Designer Bridge App, version-surface contradictions, and redaction rules.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"webflow troubleshooting\"\n  - \"webflow mcp not working\"\n  - \"webflow token error\"\n  - \"webflow 429\"\n  - \"webflow bridge app\"\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.1.0.0\n---\n# Webflow MCP Troubleshooting\n\nCommon failure modes for the webflow Code Mode manual and their fixes.\n\n---\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nThis reference covers discovery failures, auth/scope errors, rate limiting, publish-queue issues,\nDesigner Bridge App failures, surface drift, and redaction rules. Run `../scripts/doctor.sh`\n(verify-only) first.\n\n---\n\n\n---\n## 2. Discovery Fails (No `Webflow.Webflow.*` Tools In `List_Tools`)\n\n1. Confirm the operator environment exports `WEBFLOW_TOKEN` (namespaced\n   `webflow_WEBFLOW_TOKEN` in `.env.example`); the Code Mode manual resolves `${WEBFLOW_TOKEN}`\n   from the environment. Check `scripts/doctor.sh` (boolean token check — never prints values).\n2. Confirm npx can fetch `webflow-mcp-server` (offline cache, registry access). If the pinned\n   version is unreachable, restore the recorded pinned version from\n   `../mcp-servers/webflow-mcp/README.md`.\n3. Confirm Node >= 22.3.0 (the server's documented runtime requirement).\n4. Re-run discovery per session; never call from memory.\n\n---\n## 3. Tool Calls Fail With Auth Errors (401/403)\n\n| Symptom | Cause | Fix |\n|---------|-------|-----|\n| 401 on everything | missing/expired `WEBFLOW_TOKEN` | export a valid token; restart the manual |\n| 403 on a specific action | token scopes insufficient for the action's class | check the action's required scope (`tool-surface.md`); mint a least-privilege token with the needed scope |\n| 403 on site-level calls | workspace token (no `site` scope) | use a Site Token for site-level operations |\n| 403 on custom-code endpoints | `custom_code` scopes are Data-Client-app-only | use a Data Client app token or drop the call |\n| 403 on authorize | role below owner/admin | only site owners/admins can authorize the MCP server |\n\n---\n## 4. Rate Limiting (429)\n\n- Honor `Retry-After` (~60s); the official SDK applies exponential backoff by default.\n- Publishing is limited to one successful queue per minute — batch or wait.\n- Plan-based general limits: Starter/Basic 60 rpm; CMS/eCommerce/Business 120 rpm.\n- Never blind-replay ambiguous non-idempotent writes after a 429/error.\n\n---\n## 5. Publish Failures\n\n- \"Publish queue busy\": one publish per minute — wait and retry once, verify before retry.\n- Staging vs production: the publish body requires `customDomains` OR `publishToWebflowSubdomain`.\n  Smoke flows must pass only the staging flag (optionally scoped to a single `pageId`).\n- Published drafts didn't appear: CMS items may have been written to the draft queue — publishing\n  is a separate explicit action (`publish_collection_items`).\n\n---\n## 6. Designer / Bridge App Failures (`De*` Tools)\n\n- Designer tools fail when Webflow is closed or the Designer session has no authorized site —\n  Designer API tools require the Bridge App open in the Designer.\n- Bridge App not installed: it auto-installs to authorized sites after remote OAuth; local mode\n  needs a registered/published MCP Bridge App Designer extension.\n- `get_designer_app_connection_info` (RO) reports connection state — check it before Designer work.\n- Designer edits are draft-only; they appear on the live site only after `publish_site`.\n\n---\n## 7. Suspicious Or Missing Tools\n\n- The public `webflow/mcp-server` README and the hosted docs disagree on the surface (`/sse` vs\n  `/mcp`, resources presence). Treat the **pinned server version's live discovery** as\n  authoritative; record dated fixtures in `tool-surface.md`.\n- Unknown tool modules default to read-only/draft-write until discovery proves otherwise\n  (fail closed) — never grant destructive/publish/deploy classes by default.\n- Tool named differently than the baseline: record the drift and update the fixture; do not\n  guess.\n\n---\n## 8. WORKFLOW AND WEBHOOK ISSUES\n\n- `run_workflow` fails: confirm the workflow id and required inputs (`flows`/`workflows` list is\n  RO); the blast radius depends on the workflow definition — state it in the confirmation.\n- Webhook create/delete: integration config, not site content; `delete_webhook` is destructive\n  class.\n\n---\n## 9. REDACTION RULES\n\n- Never commit or log token values; redact tool output containing them.\n- Never print the resolved `${WEBFLOW_TOKEN}` value (doctor.sh reports presence only).\n- Never record account identifiers in fixtures.\n\n---\n## 10. RELATED RESOURCES\n\n- [`mcp-wiring.md`](mcp-wiring.md) — wiring and auth details\n- [`action-reference.md`](action-reference.md) — action inventory\n- [`../SKILL.md`](../SKILL.md) — frozen classes and gates","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":109,"totalLines":109,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/troubleshooting.md","time":{"start":1785758297169,"end":1785758297174}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0988c57a5556d0f9016a70825804c8819192a20ab12ec9be31"}},"id":"prt_fc77d2be6001h36apDDJHJ0ha4","sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","messageID":"msg_fc77cf028001ZMthqLhmQIiwqU"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785758297235,"sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_M3yqVg2D1jhaUuufjHYwZN4O","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/utcp-manual-reference.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/utcp-manual-reference.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Webflow MCP Registered Manual Reference\"\n3: description: \"Reference shape of the registered webflow Code Mode manual in .utcp_config.json — verify, never re-add, never edit.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"webflow manual reference\"\n6:   - \"webflow utcp manual\"\n7:   - \"webflow manual shape\"\n8: importance_tier: normal\n9: contextType: implementation\n10: version: 1.1.0.0\n11: ---\n12: \n13: # Webflow MCP Registered Manual Reference - Reference Shape\n14: \n15: Reference shape of the `webflow` Code Mode manual registered in `.utcp_config.json`.\n16: \n17: ---\n18: \n19: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n20: \n21: ### Purpose\n22: \n23: Provide the canonical reference shape of the registered `webflow` manual so operators can verify\n24: the live entry without re-adding or editing it. The live config is authoritative; this asset\n25: documents what the entry should look like and why each field is fixed.\n26: \n27: ### Usage\n28: \n29: - Compare the live `webflow` entry in `.utcp_config.json` against the reference shape below.\n30: - On drift, record it and verify the intended change with the operator — never silently re-add or\n31:   edit the entry.\n32: - The env placeholder resolves from the operator's environment; `.env.example` documents the\n33:   namespaced `webflow_WEBFLOW_TOKEN` name only.\n34: \n35: ---\n36: \n37: ## 2. REFERENCE SHAPE\n38: \n39: ```json\n40: {\n41:   \"name\": \"webflow\",\n42:   \"call_template_type\": \"mcp\",\n43:   \"config\": {\n44:     \"mcpServers\": {\n45:       \"webflow\": {\n46:         \"transport\": \"stdio\",\n47:         \"command\": \"npx\",\n48:         \"args\": [\"-y\", \"webflow-mcp-server@latest\"],\n49:         \"env\": { \"WEBFLOW_TOKEN\": \"${WEBFLOW_TOKEN}\" }\n50:       }\n51:     }\n52:   }\n53: }\n54: ```\n55: \n56: ---\n57: \n58: ## 3. FIELD GUIDELINES\n59: \n60: **`transport`**:\n61: - Fixed to `stdio` — Code Mode consumes stdio; the official server ships as a Node CLI.\n62: \n63: **`command` / `args`**:\n64: - `npx` resolving `webflow-mcp-server@latest` — pin the exact version after the first verified\n65:   session and record it in `../mcp-servers/webflow-mcp/README.md`.\n66: \n67: **`env`**:\n68: - `WEBFLOW_TOKEN` bound from the operator environment — the value never lives in the repository.\n69: \n70: **Server runtime**:\n71: - Node 22.3.0+ (verified by `../scripts/doctor.sh`).\n72: \n73: ---\n74: \n75: ## 4. RELATED RESOURCES\n76: \n77: - [`../scripts/doctor.sh`](../scripts/doctor.sh) — verify-only manual check\n78: - [`../references/mcp-wiring.md`](../references/mcp-wiring.md) — wiring details and auth\n79: - [`../mcp-servers/webflow-mcp/README.md`](../mcp-servers/webflow-mcp/README.md) — server pointer\n\n(End of file - total 79 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: \"Webflow MCP Registered Manual Reference\"\ndescription: \"Reference shape of the registered webflow Code Mode manual in .utcp_config.json — verify, never re-add, never edit.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"webflow manual reference\"\n  - \"webflow utcp manual\"\n  - \"webflow manual shape\"\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.1.0.0\n---\n\n# Webflow MCP Registered Manual Reference - Reference Shape\n\nReference shape of the `webflow` Code Mode manual registered in `.utcp_config.json`.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/utcp-manual-reference.md","text":"---\ntitle: \"Webflow MCP Registered Manual Reference\"\ndescription: \"Reference shape of the registered webflow Code Mode manual in .utcp_config.json — verify, never re-add, never edit.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"webflow manual reference\"\n  - \"webflow utcp manual\"\n  - \"webflow manual shape\"\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.1.0.0\n---\n\n# Webflow MCP Registered Manual Reference - Reference Shape\n\nReference shape of the `webflow` Code Mode manual registered in `.utcp_config.json`.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Purpose\n\nProvide the canonical reference shape of the registered `webflow` manual so operators can verify\nthe live entry without re-adding or editing it. The live config is authoritative; this asset\ndocuments what the entry should look like and why each field is fixed.\n\n### Usage\n\n- Compare the live `webflow` entry in `.utcp_config.json` against the reference shape below.\n- On drift, record it and verify the intended change with the operator — never silently re-add or\n  edit the entry.\n- The env placeholder resolves from the operator's environment; `.env.example` documents the\n  namespaced `webflow_WEBFLOW_TOKEN` name only.\n\n---\n\n## 2. REFERENCE SHAPE\n\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"webflow\",\n  \"call_template_type\": \"mcp\",\n  \"config\": {\n    \"mcpServers\": {\n      \"webflow\": {\n        \"transport\": \"stdio\",\n        \"command\": \"npx\",\n        \"args\": [\"-y\", \"webflow-mcp-server@latest\"],\n        \"env\": { \"WEBFLOW_TOKEN\": \"${WEBFLOW_TOKEN}\" }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. FIELD GUIDELINES\n\n**`transport`**:\n- Fixed to `stdio` — Code Mode consumes stdio; the official server ships as a Node CLI.\n\n**`command` / `args`**:\n- `npx` resolving `webflow-mcp-server@latest` — pin the exact version after the first verified\n  session and record it in `../mcp-servers/webflow-mcp/README.md`.\n\n**`env`**:\n- `WEBFLOW_TOKEN` bound from the operator environment — the value never lives in the repository.\n\n**Server runtime**:\n- Node 22.3.0+ (verified by `../scripts/doctor.sh`).\n\n---\n\n## 4. RELATED RESOURCES\n\n- [`../scripts/doctor.sh`](../scripts/doctor.sh) — verify-only manual check\n- [`../references/mcp-wiring.md`](../references/mcp-wiring.md) — wiring details and auth\n- [`../mcp-servers/webflow-mcp/README.md`](../mcp-servers/webflow-mcp/README.md) — server pointer","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":79,"totalLines":79,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/utcp-manual-reference.md","time":{"start":1785758297223,"end":1785758297233}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0988c57a5556d0f9016a70825804d08191bfe9257161ffb5c1"}},"id":"prt_fc77d2c5c001g8FqjtiL0WP8ob","sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","messageID":"msg_fc77cf028001ZMthqLhmQIiwqU"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785758297264,"sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_6mj9S9GDIaESJLBgOnuY2ljR","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/payload-examples.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/payload-examples.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Webflow MCP Payload Examples\"\n3: description: \"Example payload shapes for Webflow MCP actions (agent instructions, CMS items, variables, sitemap bulk, staging publish) built from the official required-parameter lists.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"webflow payload examples\"\n6:   - \"webflow example payloads\"\n7:   - \"webflow request shapes\"\n8: importance_tier: normal\n9: contextType: implementation\n10: version: 1.1.0.0\n11: ---\n12: \n13: # Webflow MCP Payload Examples - Payload Shapes\n14: \n15: Example payload shapes for Webflow MCP actions, built from the official required-parameter lists.\n16: \n17: ---\n18: \n19: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n20: \n21: ### Purpose\n22: \n23: Show the request shapes an agent sends for representative Webflow MCP actions so operators and\n24: agents can recognize correct payloads before the first authenticated session.\n25: \n26: ### Usage\n27: \n28: - Copy and adapt a shape for the target action.\n29: - These are **shapes, not live-verified payloads** — the exact schema must come from `tool_info`\n30:   on the pinned version at the first authenticated session.\n31: - `siteId`/`pageId` are required on all page-building tools in addition to listed params.\n32: \n33: ---\n34: \n35: ## 2. AGENT INSTRUCTIONS — CREATE A RULE\n36: \n37: ```json\n38: {\n39:   \"site_id\": \"<test-site-id>\",\n40:   \"kind\": \"rule\",\n41:   \"path\": \"guidelines/publish-policy\",\n42:   \"markdown\": \"# Publish policy\\nAlways publish to the staging subdomain (`publishToWebflowSubdomain`); never `customDomains`.\"\n43: }\n44: ```\n45: \n46: ---\n47: \n48: ## 3. CMS — CREATE A DRAFT COLLECTION ITEM\n49: \n50: ```json\n51: {\n52:   \"siteId\": \"<test-site-id>\",\n53:   \"collection_id\": \"<collection-id>\",\n54:   \"request\": { \"fieldData\": { \"name\": \"Draft post\", \"slug\": \"draft-post\", \"body\": \"Draft content\" } }\n55: }\n56: ```\n57: \n58: ---\n59: \n60: ## 4. VARIABLES — CREATE A COLOR VARIABLE\n61: \n62: ```json\n63: {\n64:   \"siteId\": \"<test-site-id>\",\n65:   \"pageId\": \"<page-id>\",\n66:   \"value\": { \"r\": 30, \"g\": 60, \"b\": 90, \"a\": 1 }\n67: }\n68: ```\n69: \n70: ---\n71: \n72: ## 5. SITEMAP — BULK NOINDEX PAGES\n73: \n74: ```json\n75: {\n76:   \"siteId\": \"<test-site-id>\",\n77:   \"pageIds\": [\"<page-id-1>\", \"<page-id-2>\"],\n78:   \"sitemapStatus\": \"noindex\"\n79: }\n80: ```\n81: \n82: ---\n83: \n84: ## 6. PUBLISH — STAGING SUBDOMAIN ONLY\n85: \n86: ```json\n87: {\n88:   \"site_id\": \"<test-site-id>\",\n89:   \"publishToWebflowSubdomain\": true,\n90:   \"pageId\": \"<page-id>\"\n91: }\n92: ```\n93: \n94: Never include `customDomains` in automated or smoke flows.\n95: \n96: ---\n97: \n98: ## 7. RELATED RESOURCES\n99: \n100: - [`../references/action-reference.md`](../references/action-reference.md) — required parameters per action\n101: - [`../SKILL.md`](../SKILL.md) — frozen classes and gates\n\n(End of file - total 101 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: \"Webflow MCP Payload Examples\"\ndescription: \"Example payload shapes for Webflow MCP actions (agent instructions, CMS items, variables, sitemap bulk, staging publish) built from the official required-parameter lists.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"webflow payload examples\"\n  - \"webflow example payloads\"\n  - \"webflow request shapes\"\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.1.0.0\n---\n\n# Webflow MCP Payload Examples - Payload Shapes\n\nExample payload shapes for Webflow MCP actions, built from the official required-parameter lists.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/payload-examples.md","text":"---\ntitle: \"Webflow MCP Payload Examples\"\ndescription: \"Example payload shapes for Webflow MCP actions (agent instructions, CMS items, variables, sitemap bulk, staging publish) built from the official required-parameter lists.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"webflow payload examples\"\n  - \"webflow example payloads\"\n  - \"webflow request shapes\"\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.1.0.0\n---\n\n# Webflow MCP Payload Examples - Payload Shapes\n\nExample payload shapes for Webflow MCP actions, built from the official required-parameter lists.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Purpose\n\nShow the request shapes an agent sends for representative Webflow MCP actions so operators and\nagents can recognize correct payloads before the first authenticated session.\n\n### Usage\n\n- Copy and adapt a shape for the target action.\n- These are **shapes, not live-verified payloads** — the exact schema must come from `tool_info`\n  on the pinned version at the first authenticated session.\n- `siteId`/`pageId` are required on all page-building tools in addition to listed params.\n\n---\n\n## 2. AGENT INSTRUCTIONS — CREATE A RULE\n\n```json\n{\n  \"site_id\": \"<test-site-id>\",\n  \"kind\": \"rule\",\n  \"path\": \"guidelines/publish-policy\",\n  \"markdown\": \"# Publish policy\\nAlways publish to the staging subdomain (`publishToWebflowSubdomain`); never `customDomains`.\"\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. CMS — CREATE A DRAFT COLLECTION ITEM\n\n```json\n{\n  \"siteId\": \"<test-site-id>\",\n  \"collection_id\": \"<collection-id>\",\n  \"request\": { \"fieldData\": { \"name\": \"Draft post\", \"slug\": \"draft-post\", \"body\": \"Draft content\" } }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. VARIABLES — CREATE A COLOR VARIABLE\n\n```json\n{\n  \"siteId\": \"<test-site-id>\",\n  \"pageId\": \"<page-id>\",\n  \"value\": { \"r\": 30, \"g\": 60, \"b\": 90, \"a\": 1 }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. SITEMAP — BULK NOINDEX PAGES\n\n```json\n{\n  \"siteId\": \"<test-site-id>\",\n  \"pageIds\": [\"<page-id-1>\", \"<page-id-2>\"],\n  \"sitemapStatus\": \"noindex\"\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 6. PUBLISH — STAGING SUBDOMAIN ONLY\n\n```json\n{\n  \"site_id\": \"<test-site-id>\",\n  \"publishToWebflowSubdomain\": true,\n  \"pageId\": \"<page-id>\"\n}\n```\n\nNever include `customDomains` in automated or smoke flows.\n\n---\n\n## 7. RELATED RESOURCES\n\n- [`../references/action-reference.md`](../references/action-reference.md) — required parameters per action\n- [`../SKILL.md`](../SKILL.md) — frozen classes and gates","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":101,"totalLines":101,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/payload-examples.md","time":{"start":1785758297248,"end":1785758297262}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0988c57a5556d0f9016a70825804d881918859017563bc5780"}},"id":"prt_fc77d2c9b001vWmq55udZex5PB","sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","messageID":"msg_fc77cf028001ZMthqLhmQIiwqU"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785758297313,"sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_C6C5K2jQzeMdLM9eeTTybr7l","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/SKILL.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/SKILL.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: name: mcp-webflow\n3: description: \"Webflow MCP 2.0 transport: Data/Designer API via Code Mode; frozen safety classes, least-privilege auth, sk-design pairing.\"\n4: compatibility: \"Requires the official webflow-mcp-server (Node 22.3.0+ for local mode), a WEBFLOW_TOKEN (site token for automation; workspace tokens read-only) or the remote OAuth flow (https://mcp.webflow.com/mcp), and Code Mode.\"\n5: allowed-tools: [Read, Bash, Grep, Glob, mcp__code_mode__call_tool_chain]\n6: version: 1.3.0.0\n7: user-invocable: true\n8: ---\n9: \n10: <!-- Keywords: mcp-webflow, webflow, webflow-mcp, webflow mcp 2.0, cms, publish-site, publish-collection-items, designer, bridge-app, webflow-token, sk-design, webflow-transport, code-mode -->\n11: \n12: # Webflow (mcp-webflow)\n13: \n14: Official **Webflow MCP 2.0** transport for the `mcp-tooling` hub: operate Webflow sites, pages, CMS\n15: collections, components, variables, assets, scripts, workflows, webhooks, and Designer state through\n16: the official `webflow-mcp-server` (npm) or the remote Webflow MCP service, reached via Code Mode.\n17: The transport executes; the hub orchestrates; `sk-design` owns taste.\n18: \n19: > **Discovery status (read first).** The `webflow` Code Mode manual **IS REGISTERED** in this repo's\n20: > `.utcp_config.json` (stdio `npx -y webflow-mcp-server@latest`, `WEBFLOW_TOKEN` env). Live tool\n21: > discovery and calls are **BLOCKED pending an operator-provided token and a dedicated non-production\n22: > test site**. The documented inventory is dual-surface: the **remote deployed surface** — **31 tools /\n23: > 220 actions** from the official docs (2026-08-03, `references/action-reference.md`) — and the\n24: > **local OSS server** — 18 modules (`references/tool-surface.md`). The frozen safety contract applies\n25: > to both. Per-session `list_tools()`\n26: > re-confirmation stays MANDATORY before relying on any name: confirm, then call, and fail closed on\n27: > drift. Callable names follow the Code Mode convention (`webflow.webflow.<tool>` registry /\n28: > `webflow.webflow_<tool>` TypeScript) — **UNVERIFIED** until authenticated discovery.\n29: \n30: ---\n31: \n32: ## 1. WHEN TO USE\n33: \n34: ### Activation Triggers\n35: \n36: **Use when** the user wants to:\n37: \n38: - Read Webflow site, page, CMS, component, script, workflow, webhook, or Designer state\n39:   (`list_*`, `get_*`, `query_*`, `search_*` families).\n40: - Mutate Webflow content: CMS collection items (create/update), page settings, static content,\n41:   scripts, webhooks, 301 redirects, robots.txt.\n42: - Publish or deploy: `publish_site`, `publish_collection_items`, `run_workflow` — **always gated**.\n43: - Perform Designer-family edits: elements, styles, variables, components, assets, pages\n44:   (`de*` tools) — **always paired with `sk-design`**.\n45: - Wire, verify, or troubleshoot the registered `webflow` Code Mode manual, its auth, scopes,\n46:   rate limits, or the Designer Bridge App boundary.\n47: \n48: ### Use Cases\n49: \n50: - CMS content operations on a dedicated test site (read, draft-write, staged publish).\n51: - Page metadata and static-content edits with explicit draft vs publish intent.\n52: - Designer canvas changes (elements, styles, variables, components) — with `sk-design`.\n53: - Workflow and script operations under the deploy gate.\n54: - Webhook, redirect, robots.txt, and AI Q&A surface (Enterprise-gated where noted).\n55: \n56: ### When NOT to Use\n57: \n58: - Design judgment itself — load `sk-design` (this transport never decides taste).\n59: - Workspace-level administration outside the documented scope model.\n60: - Anything that must touch a **production site from a smoke/test flow** — that is structurally\n61:   forbidden (staging subdomain only).\n62: - Unverified tool names — never call from memory (discovery first).\n63: \n64: ---\n65: \n66: ## 2. SMART ROUTING\n67: \n68: Routing is registry-driven via the `mcp-tooling` hub (`hub-router.json` → `mode-registry.json`).\n69: `mcp-webflow` is a `transport` mode (`backendKind: code-mode-stdio-mcp`, `mutatesWorkspace: false`)\n70: resolved on Webflow signals; `sk-design` is the mandatory cross-hub judgment partner for\n71: Designer-family operations.\n72: \n73: ### Signal Detection\n74: \n75: | Signal | Route | Action |\n76: |--------|-------|--------|\n77: | \"webflow\", \"webflow mcp\", \"webflow cms/site/page\" | mcp-webflow | load this packet, discover first |\n78: | \"change/design/set ... in webflow\" (element/style/variable/component) | mcp-webflow + `sk-design` | load both; design judgment first |\n79: | \"publish/deploy webflow\" | mcp-webflow (PB/DP gates) | confirmation flow |\n80: | \"figma/refero/mobbin/clickup/chrome ...\" | sibling modes | never route to webflow |\n81: | no tool signal | DEFER (no-mode-scored) | ask for disambiguation |\n82: \n83: ### Smart-Router Pseudocode\n84: \n85: ```text\n86: RESOURCE_BASES = [\"SKILL.md\", \"references\", \"feature-catalog\", \"assets\"]\n87: \n88: def discover_markdown_resources():\n89:     # recursively collect *.md under each base; returns relative paths\n90:     inventory = set()\n91:     for base in RESOURCE_BASES:\n92:         for path in walk(base):                    # recursive traversal\n93:             if path.endswith(\".md\"):\n94:                 inventory.add(relative_path(path))\n95:     return inventory\n96: \n97: def _guard_in_skill(relative_path):\n98:     # only packet-owned resources may carry this mode's routing semantics\n99:     return relative_path not in {\"../\", \"shared/\", \"node_modules/\"}\n100: \n101: def load_if_available(resource):\n102:     # load a resource only when it exists on disk and is guarded; never fabricate\n103:     if exists(resource) and _guard_in_skill(resource):\n104:         return read(resource)\n105:     return None\n106: \n107: def score_intent(intent):\n108:     # weighted signal scoring: webflow aliases, design verbs, sibling tool names\n109:     signals = {\"webflow\": 0.0, \"design\": 0.0, \"sibling_tool\": None}\n110:     for alias in WEBFLOW_ALIASES:                  # webflow, webflow mcp, webflow cms, ...\n111:         if alias in intent: signals[\"webflow\"] += 1.0\n112:     for verb in DESIGN_VERBS:                      # change/design/set + element/style/variable/...\n113:         if verb in intent: signals[\"design\"] += 1.0\n114:     for mode, names in SIBLING_MODES.items():      # figma/refero/mobbin/clickup/chrome\n115:         if any(n in intent for n in names): signals[\"sibling_tool\"] = mode\n116:     return signals\n117: \n118: def route(intent):\n119:     inventory = discover_markdown_resources()      # recursive, guarded\n120:     signals = score_intent(intent)\n121:     if signals[\"sibling_tool\"] and signals[\"webflow\"] == 0:\n122:         return signals[\"sibling_tool\"]\n123:     if signals[\"webflow\"] >= TIEBREAK:\n124:         return \"mcp-webflow\" + (\" + sk-design\" if signals[\"design\"] else \"\")\n125:     return UNKNOWN_FALLBACK                        # defer + disambiguation checklist\n126: \n127: UNKNOWN_FALLBACK_CHECKLIST = [\n128:     \"Restate the request and the tool signals you found.\",\n129:     \"Offer the candidate modes (webflow / sibling modes) explicitly.\",\n130:     \"Ask which mode the user intends; never default to mcp-webflow on ambiguity.\",\n131:     \"If webflow is chosen, run discovery-first before any call.\",\n132: ]\n133: ```\n134: \n135: ### Guarded Intent Router\n136: \n137: | User intent pattern | Route | Notes |\n138: |---------------------|-------|-------|\n139: | \"read/list/get webflow ...\" (pages, cms, sites, scripts, workflows, components, webhooks) | RO | scope check only |\n140: | \"create/update webflow ...\" (draft intent, no publish verb) | DW | confirm target + draft vs live choice for CMS |\n141: | \"delete/remove webflow ...\" | DS | **confirmation** + rollback statement + before/after listing |\n142: | \"publish webflow ...\" | PB | **confirmation**; staging-first; single page when possible |\n143: | \"run a webflow workflow\" | DP | **confirmation**; name the workflow + inputs; blast-radius note |\n144: | \"change the hero heading / style / variable / component in webflow\" | DW + `sk-design` | Designer-family: load `sk-design` before execution |\n145: | \"webflow\" alone | discover-first | enumerate safe read inventory; never auto-execute |\n146: \n147: ---\n148: \n149: ## 3. HOW IT WORKS\n150: \n151: ### 3.1 Operation Classes and Gates (FROZEN)\n152: \n153: Every Webflow operation maps to exactly one class; the gate applies at the agent level before any\n154: `tools/call` reaches the bridge.\n155: \n156: | Class | Meaning | Gate | Rollback |\n157: |-------|---------|------|----------|\n158: | **RO** read-only | `list_*`, `get_*`, `query_*`, `ask_webflow_ai`, guide, activity logs | none (scope check) | n/a |\n159: | **DW** draft-write | CMS draft items, page settings, static content, scripts, redirects, webhooks, Designer canvas edits | none (scope check; target id present) | revert content / discard draft |\n160: | **DS** destructive | `delete_collection_items`, `delete_all_site_scripts`, `delete_all_page_scripts`, `delete_webhook`, `delete_301_redirect`, `delete_robots_txt`, `remove_element`, `remove_attribute`, `remove_style`, `remove_properties`, `delete_variable`, `unregister_component` | **operator confirmation** (idempotency guard; before/after listing) | re-publish prior content; Designer version-history snapshot; API-level site restore UNKNOWN → treated as unsupported |\n161: | **PB** publish | `publish_site`, `publish_collection_items`, `update_page_settings` with publishing-status change | **operator confirmation**; staging-first (`publishToWebflowSubdomain` only, never `customDomains`); optional single `pageId`; 1 publish/min queue | re-publish prior content/snapshot |\n162: | **DP** deploy | `run_workflow` (local OSS surface only — the remote surface has no workflow tool) | **operator confirmation**; named target environment | Webflow-side workflow controls; script removal is DS |\n163: | **UNKNOWN** | any tool/action not in the researched inventory (either surface) | **prohibited until classified** from the live schema — never inferred as DW | n/a — do not execute |\n164: \n165: ### 3.2 Critical Semantics\n166: \n167: - **CMS semantics are surface-specific**: on the remote surface, create/update item actions create\n168:   **drafts**; `publish_collection_items`/`unpublish_collection_items` publish/unpublish live (PB,\n169:   no staging-domain target). On the local OSS surface, items can be created/deleted directly in the\n170:   live site or queued — the client must choose. Never assume draft-safety across surfaces.\n171: - **Nothing auto-publishes**; publishing is always a separate explicit action.\n172: - **One publish per minute** queue; plan-based general limits (60/120 rpm) with `Retry-After` on\n173:   429 — honor it, never blind-replay ambiguous non-idempotent writes.\n174: - **Staging vs production is structural**: `publishToWebflowSubdomain` (`*.webflow.io`) is the only\n175:   publish target allowed from smoke/test flows; a single `pageId` limits blast radius.\n176: - **Unknown tools fail closed**: anything not in the researched inventory is class **UNKNOWN** and\n177:   PROHIBITED until the live schema classifies it — never inferred as DW, and never DS/PB/DP by default.\n178: \n179: ### 3.3 Execution Protocol\n180: \n181: 1. **Discover first (mandatory)**: `list_tools()` in the session; compare names against\n182:    `references/tool-surface.md`; on drift record it and fail closed for mismatched tools.\n183: 2. **Classify** the target tool against the frozen matrix.\n184: 3. **Apply the gate** (confirmation for DS/PB/DP with expected output + rollback statement).\n185: 4. **Execute**; capture evidence; redact token-bearing output.\n186: \n187: ### 3.4b Surface Applicability\n188: \n189: Every tool reference in this packet is labeled by surface: **remote** (31 tools / 220 actions,\n190: `references/action-reference.md`), **local OSS** (18 modules, `references/tool-surface.md`), or\n191: **both**. Actions named only in one surface (e.g., `run_workflow` — local; `insert_whtml` — remote)\n192: must not be called against the other. Discovery compares the live `list_tools` result against the\n193: surface the pinned manual actually resolves.\n194: \n195: ### 3.4 Wiring\n196: \n197: | Concern | Value |\n198: |---------|-------|\n199: | Manual | `webflow` in `.utcp_config.json` (stdio `npx -y webflow-mcp-server@latest`, `WEBFLOW_TOKEN` env) |\n200: | Env name | `webflow_WEBFLOW_TOKEN` in `.env.example` (name only) |\n201: | Local server | `webflow-mcp-server` npm, Node 22.3.0+ |\n202: | Remote endpoint | `https://mcp.webflow.com/mcp` (hosted docs) / `/sse` (README) — reconcile per session |\n203: | Bridge App | Required only for Designer (`de*`) tools; auto-installs on OAuth authorization |\n204: \n205: ### 3.5 Authentication Posture\n206: \n207: - **Remote mode** (primary for humans): OAuth per-site/per-workspace consent; zero local secrets;\n208:   only site owners/admins can authorize; `mcp-remote` is experimental — pin the version.\n209: - **Local mode** (deterministic for automation): `WEBFLOW_TOKEN` site token with least-privilege\n210:   scopes (read-only baseline: `cms:read`, `pages:read`, `sites:read`, `assets:read`,\n211:   `components:read`, `forms:read`, `authorized_user:read`); escalate to `sites:write` only for the\n212:   staging publish test. Workspace tokens: read-only only (no `site` scope). `custom_code` scopes\n213:   are Data-Client-app-only.\n214: - Token values live only in the operator environment; the repo carries names and placeholders.\n215: \n216: ### 3.6 Version-Surface Reconciliation\n217: \n218: The public `webflow/mcp-server` README documents `/sse` + no resources, while current hosted docs\n219: describe the remote Streamable HTTP surface at `https://mcp.webflow.com/mcp` (registry\n220: `com.webflow/mcp` 2.0.0) with read-only resources and Agent Instructions. Treat the deployed\n221: remote surface and the OSS snapshot as different surfaces until a version-specific reconciliation\n222: lands; the local stdio server is the deterministic baseline for automation.\n223: \n224: ---\n225: \n226: ## 4. RULES\n227: \n228: ### ✅ ALWAYS\n229: - Discover first; fail closed on drift.\n230: - Classify before executing; apply the frozen gate.\n231: - Confirm destructive/publish/deploy immediately before the call with expected output and\n232:   rollback statement.\n233: - Publish to `publishToWebflowSubdomain` only from smoke/test flows; single `pageId` when possible.\n234: - Honor `Retry-After`; respect the 1-publish/min queue.\n235: - Route Designer-family operations through `sk-design`.\n236: - Keep token values out of the repository, logs, and transcripts (redact tool output).\n237: \n238: ### ⚠️ ESCALATE\n239: \n240: - Escalate to the operator (and, for design work, `sk-design`) when: an operation's class is\n241:   ambiguous from the live surface, a bulk write's blast radius cannot be enumerated, discovery\n242:   drift affects the target tool, a publish target is unclear (production vs staging), or a\n243:   confirmation was given for a different operation than the one about to execute.\n244: - Escalation means: stop, state the facts, and ask — never guess the class or the gate.\n245: \n246: ### ⛔ NEVER\n247: - Never call an unverified tool name from memory.\n248: - Never publish to production `customDomains` from any automated or test flow.\n249: - Never use workspace-token writes.\n250: - Never blind-replay a failed non-idempotent write.\n251: - Never treat CMS mutations as implicitly draft-safe.\n252: - Never perform API-level site backup/restore — it does not exist in the Data API v2 surface.\n253: \n254: ---\n255: \n256: ## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n257: \n258: - **SC-001**: Every Webflow operation is classified and gated before execution; no un-gated\n259:   destructive/publish/deploy call; UNKNOWN actions are never executed.\n260: - **SC-002**: Discovery runs per session and drift is recorded; no tool is called from memory.\n261: - **SC-003**: Designer-family operations always pair with `sk-design`.\n262: - **SC-004**: Smoke/test flows never touch production (`customDomains`); staging subdomain only.\n263: - **SC-005**: No token value or account identifier enters the repository, logs, or transcripts.\n264: \n265: ---\n266: \n267: ## 6. INTEGRATION POINTS\n268: \n269: | Surface | Role | Status |\n270: |---------|------|--------|\n271: | `mcp-tooling` hub | registry (`mode-registry.json`), router (`hub-router.json`), smart-routing, leaf-manifest, advisor metadata | registered (2026-08-02) |\n272: | `sk-design` | cross-hub judgment partner for Designer-family operations | mandatory pairing |\n273: | `.utcp_config.json` | `webflow` stdio manual | registered; token env from operator |\n274: | `.env.example` | `webflow_WEBFLOW_TOKEN` name only | added |\n275: | `mcp-servers/webflow-mcp/` | server pointer + pinned-version fixture slot | present; pin after first verified session |\n276: \n277: ---\n278: \n279: ## 7. QUICK REFERENCE\n280: \n281: | Class | Gate | Example tools |\n282: |-------|------|---------------|\n283: | RO | none (scope check) | `list_sites`, `list_pages`, `list_collection_items`, `ask_webflow_ai` |\n284: | DW | none (scope check) | `update_page_settings`, `create_collection_items`, `add_inline_site_script` |\n285: | DS | confirmation + rollback | `delete_collection_items`, `delete_all_site_scripts`, `remove_element` |\n286: | PB | confirmation + staging-first | `publish_site`, `publish_collection_items` |\n287: | DP | confirmation | `run_workflow` |\n288: \n289: Docs: `INSTALL-GUIDE.md` · `references/mcp-wiring.md` · `references/tool-surface.md` ·\n290: `references/troubleshooting.md` · `feature-catalog/` · `manual-testing-playbook/` ·\n291: `scripts/doctor.sh` · `assets/utcp-manual-reference.md`\n292: \n293: ---\n294: \n295: ## 8. REFERENCES AND RELATED RESOURCES\n296: \n297: - `INSTALL-GUIDE.md` — operator setup: token, scopes, verification, version pinning.\n298: - `references/mcp-wiring.md` — Code Mode wiring, auth, scope model, rate limits, Bridge App\n299:   boundary, version-surface table.\n300: - `references/action-reference.md` — complete remote-surface action reference (31 tools, 220 actions, required parameters).\n301: - `references/tool-surface.md` — local OSS 18-module tool inventory with risk classes.\n302: - `references/troubleshooting.md` — failure modes and never-list.\n303: - `feature-catalog/` — capability cards (cms, publish-deploy, designer, site-pages-scripts).\n304: - `manual-testing-playbook/` — 16 scenarios across discovery, read, draft, safety gates,\n305:   pairing, and negative classes.\n306: - `scripts/` — `doctor.sh` (verify-only) and `install.sh`.\n307: - `assets/utcp-manual-reference.md` — registered-manual reference shape.\n308: - `mcp-servers/webflow-mcp/README.md` — server pointer and pinned-version fixture slot.\n309: - `changelog/` — release notes (v1.0.0.0 scaffold, v1.1.0.0 depth upgrade, v1.2.0.0 template\n310:   alignment).\n311: - Research base: `../../specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/001-deep-research/research/research.md`.\n\n(End of file - total 311 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\nname: mcp-webflow\ndescription: \"Webflow MCP 2.0 transport: Data/Designer API via Code Mode; frozen safety classes, least-privilege auth, sk-design pairing.\"\ncompatibility: \"Requires the official webflow-mcp-server (Node 22.3.0+ for local mode), a WEBFLOW_TOKEN (site token for automation; workspace tokens read-only) or the remote OAuth flow (https://mcp.webflow.com/mcp), and Code Mode.\"\nallowed-tools: [Read, Bash, Grep, Glob, mcp__code_mode__call_tool_chain]\nversion: 1.3.0.0\nuser-invocable: true\n---\n\n<!-- Keywords: mcp-webflow, webflow, webflow-mcp, webflow mcp 2.0, cms, publish-site, publish-collection-items, designer, bridge-app, webflow-token, sk-design, webflow-transport, code-mode -->\n\n# Webflow (mcp-webflow)\n\nOfficial **Webflow MCP 2.0** transport for the `mcp-tooling` hub: operate Webflow sites, pages, CMS\ncollections, components, variables, assets, scripts, workflows, webhooks, and Designer state through\nthe official `webflow-mcp-server` (npm) or the remote Webflow MCP service, reached via Code Mode.\nThe transport executes; the hub orchestrates; `sk-design` owns taste.\n\n> **Discovery status (read first).** The `webflow` Code Mode manual **IS REGISTERED** in this repo's\n> `.utcp_config.json` (stdio `npx -y webflow-mcp-server@latest`, `WEBFLOW_TOKEN` env). Live tool","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/SKILL.md","text":"---\nname: mcp-webflow\ndescription: \"Webflow MCP 2.0 transport: Data/Designer API via Code Mode; frozen safety classes, least-privilege auth, sk-design pairing.\"\ncompatibility: \"Requires the official webflow-mcp-server (Node 22.3.0+ for local mode), a WEBFLOW_TOKEN (site token for automation; workspace tokens read-only) or the remote OAuth flow (https://mcp.webflow.com/mcp), and Code Mode.\"\nallowed-tools: [Read, Bash, Grep, Glob, mcp__code_mode__call_tool_chain]\nversion: 1.3.0.0\nuser-invocable: true\n---\n\n<!-- Keywords: mcp-webflow, webflow, webflow-mcp, webflow mcp 2.0, cms, publish-site, publish-collection-items, designer, bridge-app, webflow-token, sk-design, webflow-transport, code-mode -->\n\n# Webflow (mcp-webflow)\n\nOfficial **Webflow MCP 2.0** transport for the `mcp-tooling` hub: operate Webflow sites, pages, CMS\ncollections, components, variables, assets, scripts, workflows, webhooks, and Designer state through\nthe official `webflow-mcp-server` (npm) or the remote Webflow MCP service, reached via Code Mode.\nThe transport executes; the hub orchestrates; `sk-design` owns taste.\n\n> **Discovery status (read first).** The `webflow` Code Mode manual **IS REGISTERED** in this repo's\n> `.utcp_config.json` (stdio `npx -y webflow-mcp-server@latest`, `WEBFLOW_TOKEN` env). Live tool\n> discovery and calls are **BLOCKED pending an operator-provided token and a dedicated non-production\n> test site**. The documented inventory is dual-surface: the **remote deployed surface** — **31 tools /\n> 220 actions** from the official docs (2026-08-03, `references/action-reference.md`) — and the\n> **local OSS server** — 18 modules (`references/tool-surface.md`). The frozen safety contract applies\n> to both. Per-session `list_tools()`\n> re-confirmation stays MANDATORY before relying on any name: confirm, then call, and fail closed on\n> drift. Callable names follow the Code Mode convention (`webflow.webflow.<tool>` registry /\n> `webflow.webflow_<tool>` TypeScript) — **UNVERIFIED** until authenticated discovery.\n\n---\n\n## 1. WHEN TO USE\n\n### Activation Triggers\n\n**Use when** the user wants to:\n\n- Read Webflow site, page, CMS, component, script, workflow, webhook, or Designer state\n  (`list_*`, `get_*`, `query_*`, `search_*` families).\n- Mutate Webflow content: CMS collection items (create/update), page settings, static content,\n  scripts, webhooks, 301 redirects, robots.txt.\n- Publish or deploy: `publish_site`, `publish_collection_items`, `run_workflow` — **always gated**.\n- Perform Designer-family edits: elements, styles, variables, components, assets, pages\n  (`de*` tools) — **always paired with `sk-design`**.\n- Wire, verify, or troubleshoot the registered `webflow` Code Mode manual, its auth, scopes,\n  rate limits, or the Designer Bridge App boundary.\n\n### Use Cases\n\n- CMS content operations on a dedicated test site (read, draft-write, staged publish).\n- Page metadata and static-content edits with explicit draft vs publish intent.\n- Designer canvas changes (elements, styles, variables, components) — with `sk-design`.\n- Workflow and script operations under the deploy gate.\n- Webhook, redirect, robots.txt, and AI Q&A surface (Enterprise-gated where noted).\n\n### When NOT to Use\n\n- Design judgment itself — load `sk-design` (this transport never decides taste).\n- Workspace-level administration outside the documented scope model.\n- Anything that must touch a **production site from a smoke/test flow** — that is structurally\n  forbidden (staging subdomain only).\n- Unverified tool names — never call from memory (discovery first).\n\n---\n\n## 2. SMART ROUTING\n\nRouting is registry-driven via the `mcp-tooling` hub (`hub-router.json` → `mode-registry.json`).\n`mcp-webflow` is a `transport` mode (`backendKind: code-mode-stdio-mcp`, `mutatesWorkspace: false`)\nresolved on Webflow signals; `sk-design` is the mandatory cross-hub judgment partner for\nDesigner-family operations.\n\n### Signal Detection\n\n| Signal | Route | Action |\n|--------|-------|--------|\n| \"webflow\", \"webflow mcp\", \"webflow cms/site/page\" | mcp-webflow | load this packet, discover first |\n| \"change/design/set ... in webflow\" (element/style/variable/component) | mcp-webflow + `sk-design` | load both; design judgment first |\n| \"publish/deploy webflow\" | mcp-webflow (PB/DP gates) | confirmation flow |\n| \"figma/refero/mobbin/clickup/chrome ...\" | sibling modes | never route to webflow |\n| no tool signal | DEFER (no-mode-scored) | ask for disambiguation |\n\n### Smart-Router Pseudocode\n\n```text\nRESOURCE_BASES = [\"SKILL.md\", \"references\", \"feature-catalog\", \"assets\"]\n\ndef discover_markdown_resources():\n    # recursively collect *.md under each base; returns relative paths\n    inventory = set()\n    for base in RESOURCE_BASES:\n        for path in walk(base):                    # recursive traversal\n            if path.endswith(\".md\"):\n                inventory.add(relative_path(path))\n    return inventory\n\ndef _guard_in_skill(relative_path):\n    # only packet-owned resources may carry this mode's routing semantics\n    return relative_path not in {\"../\", \"shared/\", \"node_modules/\"}\n\ndef load_if_available(resource):\n    # load a resource only when it exists on disk and is guarded; never fabricate\n    if exists(resource) and _guard_in_skill(resource):\n        return read(resource)\n    return None\n\ndef score_intent(intent):\n    # weighted signal scoring: webflow aliases, design verbs, sibling tool names\n    signals = {\"webflow\": 0.0, \"design\": 0.0, \"sibling_tool\": None}\n    for alias in WEBFLOW_ALIASES:                  # webflow, webflow mcp, webflow cms, ...\n        if alias in intent: signals[\"webflow\"] += 1.0\n    for verb in DESIGN_VERBS:                      # change/design/set + element/style/variable/...\n        if verb in intent: signals[\"design\"] += 1.0\n    for mode, names in SIBLING_MODES.items():      # figma/refero/mobbin/clickup/chrome\n        if any(n in intent for n in names): signals[\"sibling_tool\"] = mode\n    return signals\n\ndef route(intent):\n    inventory = discover_markdown_resources()      # recursive, guarded\n    signals = score_intent(intent)\n    if signals[\"sibling_tool\"] and signals[\"webflow\"] == 0:\n        return signals[\"sibling_tool\"]\n    if signals[\"webflow\"] >= TIEBREAK:\n        return \"mcp-webflow\" + (\" + sk-design\" if signals[\"design\"] else \"\")\n    return UNKNOWN_FALLBACK                        # defer + disambiguation checklist\n\nUNKNOWN_FALLBACK_CHECKLIST = [\n    \"Restate the request and the tool signals you found.\",\n    \"Offer the candidate modes (webflow / sibling modes) explicitly.\",\n    \"Ask which mode the user intends; never default to mcp-webflow on ambiguity.\",\n    \"If webflow is chosen, run discovery-first before any call.\",\n]\n```\n\n### Guarded Intent Router\n\n| User intent pattern | Route | Notes |\n|---------------------|-------|-------|\n| \"read/list/get webflow ...\" (pages, cms, sites, scripts, workflows, components, webhooks) | RO | scope check only |\n| \"create/update webflow ...\" (draft intent, no publish verb) | DW | confirm target + draft vs live choice for CMS |\n| \"delete/remove webflow ...\" | DS | **confirmation** + rollback statement + before/after listing |\n| \"publish webflow ...\" | PB | **confirmation**; staging-first; single page when possible |\n| \"run a webflow workflow\" | DP | **confirmation**; name the workflow + inputs; blast-radius note |\n| \"change the hero heading / style / variable / component in webflow\" | DW + `sk-design` | Designer-family: load `sk-design` before execution |\n| \"webflow\" alone | discover-first | enumerate safe read inventory; never auto-execute |\n\n---\n\n## 3. HOW IT WORKS\n\n### 3.1 Operation Classes and Gates (FROZEN)\n\nEvery Webflow operation maps to exactly one class; the gate applies at the agent level before any\n`tools/call` reaches the bridge.\n\n| Class | Meaning | Gate | Rollback |\n|-------|---------|------|----------|\n| **RO** read-only | `list_*`, `get_*`, `query_*`, `ask_webflow_ai`, guide, activity logs | none (scope check) | n/a |\n| **DW** draft-write | CMS draft items, page settings, static content, scripts, redirects, webhooks, Designer canvas edits | none (scope check; target id present) | revert content / discard draft |\n| **DS** destructive | `delete_collection_items`, `delete_all_site_scripts`, `delete_all_page_scripts`, `delete_webhook`, `delete_301_redirect`, `delete_robots_txt`, `remove_element`, `remove_attribute`, `remove_style`, `remove_properties`, `delete_variable`, `unregister_component` | **operator confirmation** (idempotency guard; before/after listing) | re-publish prior content; Designer version-history snapshot; API-level site restore UNKNOWN → treated as unsupported |\n| **PB** publish | `publish_site`, `publish_collection_items`, `update_page_settings` with publishing-status change | **operator confirmation**; staging-first (`publishToWebflowSubdomain` only, never `customDomains`); optional single `pageId`; 1 publish/min queue | re-publish prior content/snapshot |\n| **DP** deploy | `run_workflow` (local OSS surface only — the remote surface has no workflow tool) | **operator confirmation**; named target environment | Webflow-side workflow controls; script removal is DS |\n| **UNKNOWN** | any tool/action not in the researched inventory (either surface) | **prohibited until classified** from the live schema — never inferred as DW | n/a — do not execute |\n\n### 3.2 Critical Semantics\n\n- **CMS semantics are surface-specific**: on the remote surface, create/update item actions create\n  **drafts**; `publish_collection_items`/`unpublish_collection_items` publish/unpublish live (PB,\n  no staging-domain target). On the local OSS surface, items can be created/deleted directly in the\n  live site or queued — the client must choose. Never assume draft-safety across surfaces.\n- **Nothing auto-publishes**; publishing is always a separate explicit action.\n- **One publish per minute** queue; plan-based general limits (60/120 rpm) with `Retry-After` on\n  429 — honor it, never blind-replay ambiguous non-idempotent writes.\n- **Staging vs production is structural**: `publishToWebflowSubdomain` (`*.webflow.io`) is the only\n  publish target allowed from smoke/test flows; a single `pageId` limits blast radius.\n- **Unknown tools fail closed**: anything not in the researched inventory is class **UNKNOWN** and\n  PROHIBITED until the live schema classifies it — never inferred as DW, and never DS/PB/DP by default.\n\n### 3.3 Execution Protocol\n\n1. **Discover first (mandatory)**: `list_tools()` in the session; compare names against\n   `references/tool-surface.md`; on drift record it and fail closed for mismatched tools.\n2. **Classify** the target tool against the frozen matrix.\n3. **Apply the gate** (confirmation for DS/PB/DP with expected output + rollback statement).\n4. **Execute**; capture evidence; redact token-bearing output.\n\n### 3.4b Surface Applicability\n\nEvery tool reference in this packet is labeled by surface: **remote** (31 tools / 220 actions,\n`references/action-reference.md`), **local OSS** (18 modules, `references/tool-surface.md`), or\n**both**. Actions named only in one surface (e.g., `run_workflow` — local; `insert_whtml` — remote)\nmust not be called against the other. Discovery compares the live `list_tools` result against the\nsurface the pinned manual actually resolves.\n\n### 3.4 Wiring\n\n| Concern | Value |\n|---------|-------|\n| Manual | `webflow` in `.utcp_config.json` (stdio `npx -y webflow-mcp-server@latest`, `WEBFLOW_TOKEN` env) |\n| Env name | `webflow_WEBFLOW_TOKEN` in `.env.example` (name only) |\n| Local server | `webflow-mcp-server` npm, Node 22.3.0+ |\n| Remote endpoint | `https://mcp.webflow.com/mcp` (hosted docs) / `/sse` (README) — reconcile per session |\n| Bridge App | Required only for Designer (`de*`) tools; auto-installs on OAuth authorization |\n\n### 3.5 Authentication Posture\n\n- **Remote mode** (primary for humans): OAuth per-site/per-workspace consent; zero local secrets;\n  only site owners/admins can authorize; `mcp-remote` is experimental — pin the version.\n- **Local mode** (deterministic for automation): `WEBFLOW_TOKEN` site token with least-privilege\n  scopes (read-only baseline: `cms:read`, `pages:read`, `sites:read`, `assets:read`,\n  `components:read`, `forms:read`, `authorized_user:read`); escalate to `sites:write` only for the\n  staging publish test. Workspace tokens: read-only only (no `site` scope). `custom_code` scopes\n  are Data-Client-app-only.\n- Token values live only in the operator environment; the repo carries names and placeholders.\n\n### 3.6 Version-Surface Reconciliation\n\nThe public `webflow/mcp-server` README documents `/sse` + no resources, while current hosted docs\ndescribe the remote Streamable HTTP surface at `https://mcp.webflow.com/mcp` (registry\n`com.webflow/mcp` 2.0.0) with read-only resources and Agent Instructions. Treat the deployed\nremote surface and the OSS snapshot as different surfaces until a version-specific reconciliation\nlands; the local stdio server is the deterministic baseline for automation.\n\n---\n\n## 4. RULES\n\n### ✅ ALWAYS\n- Discover first; fail closed on drift.\n- Classify before executing; apply the frozen gate.\n- Confirm destructive/publish/deploy immediately before the call with expected output and\n  rollback statement.\n- Publish to `publishToWebflowSubdomain` only from smoke/test flows; single `pageId` when possible.\n- Honor `Retry-After`; respect the 1-publish/min queue.\n- Route Designer-family operations through `sk-design`.\n- Keep token values out of the repository, logs, and transcripts (redact tool output).\n\n### ⚠️ ESCALATE\n\n- Escalate to the operator (and, for design work, `sk-design`) when: an operation's class is\n  ambiguous from the live surface, a bulk write's blast radius cannot be enumerated, discovery\n  drift affects the target tool, a publish target is unclear (production vs staging), or a\n  confirmation was given for a different operation than the one about to execute.\n- Escalation means: stop, state the facts, and ask — never guess the class or the gate.\n\n### ⛔ NEVER\n- Never call an unverified tool name from memory.\n- Never publish to production `customDomains` from any automated or test flow.\n- Never use workspace-token writes.\n- Never blind-replay a failed non-idempotent write.\n- Never treat CMS mutations as implicitly draft-safe.\n- Never perform API-level site backup/restore — it does not exist in the Data API v2 surface.\n\n---\n\n## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n\n- **SC-001**: Every Webflow operation is classified and gated before execution; no un-gated\n  destructive/publish/deploy call; UNKNOWN actions are never executed.\n- **SC-002**: Discovery runs per session and drift is recorded; no tool is called from memory.\n- **SC-003**: Designer-family operations always pair with `sk-design`.\n- **SC-004**: Smoke/test flows never touch production (`customDomains`); staging subdomain only.\n- **SC-005**: No token value or account identifier enters the repository, logs, or transcripts.\n\n---\n\n## 6. INTEGRATION POINTS\n\n| Surface | Role | Status |\n|---------|------|--------|\n| `mcp-tooling` hub | registry (`mode-registry.json`), router (`hub-router.json`), smart-routing, leaf-manifest, advisor metadata | registered (2026-08-02) |\n| `sk-design` | cross-hub judgment partner for Designer-family operations | mandatory pairing |\n| `.utcp_config.json` | `webflow` stdio manual | registered; token env from operator |\n| `.env.example` | `webflow_WEBFLOW_TOKEN` name only | added |\n| `mcp-servers/webflow-mcp/` | server pointer + pinned-version fixture slot | present; pin after first verified session |\n\n---\n\n## 7. QUICK REFERENCE\n\n| Class | Gate | Example tools |\n|-------|------|---------------|\n| RO | none (scope check) | `list_sites`, `list_pages`, `list_collection_items`, `ask_webflow_ai` |\n| DW | none (scope check) | `update_page_settings`, `create_collection_items`, `add_inline_site_script` |\n| DS | confirmation + rollback | `delete_collection_items`, `delete_all_site_scripts`, `remove_element` |\n| PB | confirmation + staging-first | `publish_site`, `publish_collection_items` |\n| DP | confirmation | `run_workflow` |\n\nDocs: `INSTALL-GUIDE.md` · `references/mcp-wiring.md` · `references/tool-surface.md` ·\n`references/troubleshooting.md` · `feature-catalog/` · `manual-testing-playbook/` ·\n`scripts/doctor.sh` · `assets/utcp-manual-reference.md`\n\n---\n\n## 8. REFERENCES AND RELATED RESOURCES\n\n- `INSTALL-GUIDE.md` — operator setup: token, scopes, verification, version pinning.\n- `references/mcp-wiring.md` — Code Mode wiring, auth, scope model, rate limits, Bridge App\n  boundary, version-surface table.\n- `references/action-reference.md` — complete remote-surface action reference (31 tools, 220 actions, required parameters).\n- `references/tool-surface.md` — local OSS 18-module tool inventory with risk classes.\n- `references/troubleshooting.md` — failure modes and never-list.\n- `feature-catalog/` — capability cards (cms, publish-deploy, designer, site-pages-scripts).\n- `manual-testing-playbook/` — 16 scenarios across discovery, read, draft, safety gates,\n  pairing, and negative classes.\n- `scripts/` — `doctor.sh` (verify-only) and `install.sh`.\n- `assets/utcp-manual-reference.md` — registered-manual reference shape.\n- `mcp-servers/webflow-mcp/README.md` — server pointer and pinned-version fixture slot.\n- `changelog/` — release notes (v1.0.0.0 scaffold, v1.1.0.0 depth upgrade, v1.2.0.0 template\n  alignment).\n- Research base: `../../specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/001-deep-research/research/research.md`.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":311,"totalLines":311,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/SKILL.md","time":{"start":1785758297292,"end":1785758297307}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0988c57a5556d0f9016a70825804e08191afbab8ddcffd5e77"}},"id":"prt_fc77d2ca8001aI2tK40UDs3LO8","sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","messageID":"msg_fc77cf028001ZMthqLhmQIiwqU"}}
