{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1785758728149,"sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","part":{"id":"prt_fc783bfcf001rgrklFLBSRefKJ","messageID":"msg_fc783adff001lQyiyUUoVRMK1z","sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","snapshot":"fe03b20dde9c4dbba7dc0e6f79ecce2c3c838fcc","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785758747140,"sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"webfetch","callID":"call_NfrbtwOHESO6KySR84snKW0p","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"url":"https://developers.webflow.com/data/v2.0.0/reference/rate-limits.md","format":"markdown","timeout":120},"output":"> For clean Markdown of any page, append .md to the page URL.\n> For a complete documentation index, see https://developers.webflow.com/llms.txt.\n> For AI client integration (Claude Code, Cursor, etc.), connect to the MCP server at https://developers.webflow.com/_mcp/server.\n\n# Rate Limits\n\nTo ensure consistent performance and fair access to all users, Webflow enforces rate limits on its Data API. These limits vary based on your [site subscription plan](https://www.webflow.com/pricing) and are essential for maintaining the stability of the services.\n\nYour Webflow site plan determines your rate limit:\n\n| Plan                         | Request Per Minute |\n| :--------------------------- | :----------------- |\n| Starter and Basic            | 60                 |\n| CMS, eCommerce, and Business | 120                |\n| Enterprise                   | Custom             |\n\nIf you exceed your rate limit, Webflow’s API will return an HTTP `429` Too Many Requests error. Along with this response, the `Retry-After` header will tell you how long to wait before attempting new requests—typically, this reset time is 60 seconds.\n\nIf your App or integration requires a higher limit, consider [exploring the enterprise options](https://webflow.com/pricing) to request increased access.\n\n<br />\n\n### Endpoint-specific limits\n\nWhile the general rate limits apply to most API requests, some endpoints have additional constraints. For example, [Site Publish](/data/reference/webhooks/events/site-publish) operations are limited to **one successful publish per minute.** Any endpoint-specific rate limits will be identified within the endpoint's documentation.\n\n<br />\n\n## Caching and rate limits\n\nFor cached requests to the [content delivery API](/data/docs/working-with-the-cms/content-delivery), there are effectively no rate limits. However, uncached requests to the origin server count against your plan's rate limits. To learn more about serving live CMS content from a CDN, see the [multi-channel content delivery documentation](/data/docs/working-with-the-cms/content-delivery).\n\n## How rate limits apply to Webflow APIs\n\nRate limits are applied on a per API key basis. This means that each API key is subject to its own rate limit, independent of any other keys you may be using. Whether you’re running multiple applications or integrating various services, each API key’s usage is tracked.\n\n<br />\n\n## Tracking your API usage\n\nTo help you monitor and manage your API usage, Webflow provides three key HTTP response headers with every API request:\n\n| HTTP Response Header  | Description                                                               |\n| :-------------------- | :------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| X-RateLimit-Remaining | Contains the number of available requests remaining in the current minute |\n| X-RateLimit-Limit     | Contains your current overall rate limit per minute                       |\n| Retry-After           | Contains the time to wait before attempting new requests                  |\n\n<br />\n\n### Example Request\n\nTo illustrate how these headers work, here's an example using cURL to make a request to the Webflow Data API:\n\n```curl cURL Request\ncurl --request GET \\\n    --url https://api.webflow.com/v2/token/authorized_by \\\n    --header 'accept: application/json' \\\n    --header 'authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_TOKEN'\n```\n\n<br />\n\n### Example response headers\n\n```\nHTTP/1.1 200 OK\nDate: Sat, 14 May 2022 09:00:00 GMT\nStatus: 200 OK\nX-RateLimit-Limit: 60\nX-RateLimit-Remaining: 59\nRetry-After: 60\n```\n\n<br />\n\n## Exceeding rate limits\n\nIf your application exceeds the rate limit and encounters a `429 Too Many Requests` error, it’s important to handle retries. [The Webflow SDK](https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/sdks) includes built-in exponential backoff, automatically adjusting the wait time between retries to minimize further errors. If you’re not using the SDK, it's recommended to implement your own retry logic that respects the `Retry-After` header to keep your application running.\n\n<br />\n\n### Example error\n\n```json\n{\n    \"message\": \"Too Many Requests\",\n    \"code\": \"too_many_requests\",\n    \"externalReference\": null,\n    \"details\": []\n}\n```\n\nIf you are seeing these errors, you should ensure your application is built to limit the rate of requests it's performing. It could, for example, be triggered by polling aggressively when waiting for resources to be created or making a large number of highly concurrent API calls.\n\n<br />\n\n### Optimizing API usage with webhooks\n\nFrequent polling of the API can lead to rate limit issues, especially if your application is waiting for specific changes or updates. To mitigate this, Webflow offers [Webhooks](https://developers.webflow.com/data/docs/working-with-webhooks), which allow your application to receive real-time updates without the need for continuous API calls. [Implementing webhooks](https://developers.webflow.com/data/docs/working-with-webhooks) is a highly effective way to stay within your rate limits while still maintaining responsive applications.","metadata":{"truncated":false},"title":"https://developers.webflow.com/data/v2.0.0/reference/rate-limits.md (text/markdown; charset=utf-8)","time":{"start":1785758746985,"end":1785758747139}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0426dad13d96f365016a70841ad62081918d22ccf33c22f498"}},"id":"prt_fc78409610019C0Bm60xyAkcA7","sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","messageID":"msg_fc783adff001lQyiyUUoVRMK1z"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785758747162,"sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"webfetch","callID":"call_aA5lKx3MSAOjByR6ZtIvDEPr","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"url":"https://developers.webflow.com/mcp/llms.txt","format":"text","timeout":120},"output":"> For clean Markdown of any page, append .md to the page URL.\n> For a complete documentation index, see https://developers.webflow.com/mcp/llms.txt.\n> For AI client integration (Claude Code, Cursor, etc.), connect to the MCP server at https://developers.webflow.com/mcp/_mcp/server.\n\n# MCP Server\n\n## Docs\n\n- [Webflow MCP server](https://developers.webflow.com/mcp/reference/overview.md): Webflow's MCP server and AI tools for building with Webflow APIs\n- [Getting started](https://developers.webflow.com/mcp/reference/getting-started.md): Install and configure Webflow's MCP server and AI tools\n- [Claude Desktop](https://developers.webflow.com/mcp/installing/claude-desktop.md): Install and configure Webflow's MCP server and AI tools with the Claude Desktop Connector\n- [Claude Code](https://developers.webflow.com/mcp/installing/claude-code.md): Install and configure Webflow's MCP server with Claude Code\n- [Cursor](https://developers.webflow.com/mcp/installing/cursor.md): Install and configure Webflow's MCP server and AI tools with the Cursor plugin\n- [Postman](https://developers.webflow.com/mcp/installing/postman.md): Connect to Webflow's MCP server from Postman\n- [Windsurf](https://developers.webflow.com/mcp/installing/windsurf.md): Install and configure Webflow's MCP server in Windsurf\n- [Beta server](https://developers.webflow.com/mcp/installing/beta.md): Connect to the Webflow Beta MCP server\n- [Documentation server](https://developers.webflow.com/mcp/installing/documentation-server.md): Connect directly to Webflow's documentation MCP server\n- [How it works](https://developers.webflow.com/mcp/reference/how-it-works.md): Learn how Webflow's MCP server works\n- [Skills](https://developers.webflow.com/mcp/reference/skills.md): Production-ready agent skills for popular agents that work with the Webflow MCP server\n- [Skill Migration](https://developers.webflow.com/mcp/skills/skill-migration.md): Update skills and automations that reference older Webflow MCP tool and action names to the names the current version expects.\n- [FAQs and troubleshooting](https://developers.webflow.com/mcp/faqs.md): Frequently asked questions and troubleshooting for Webflow's MCP server\n- [Data](https://developers.webflow.com/mcp/tools/data-tools.md): Reference for Webflow MCP data tools: work with sites, pages, elements, CMS, and more.\n- [Designer Session](https://developers.webflow.com/mcp/tools/designer-tools.md): Reference for Webflow MCP designer tools: interact with a live Designer session, select elements, navigate between pages, and capture visual snapshots.\n- [Utility tools](https://developers.webflow.com/mcp/tools/utility-tools.md): Reference for Webflow MCP utility tools: AI assistance, workflow guidance, tool discovery, and asset preview.\n- [Prompt Library](https://developers.webflow.com/mcp/examples/prompts.md): A curated collection of prompts for building, styling, and optimizing Webflow sites with the MCP server.\n- [Image Optimizer](https://developers.webflow.com/mcp/prompts/image-optimizer.md): Audit a Webflow site's images and compress oversized ones in place to WebP or AVIF using Webflow's native asset compression.\n- [Keyword Optimizer](https://developers.webflow.com/mcp/prompts/keyword-optimizer.md): Review static pages and CMS items, then update copy, meta titles, and descriptions to align with keyword optimization goals.\n- [SEO Metadata Auditor](https://developers.webflow.com/mcp/prompts/SEO-metadata-auditor.md): Check all pages for missing or weak SEO metadata, get suggestions on improvments, and make all changes with user approval.\n- [Variables Refactor](https://developers.webflow.com/mcp/prompts/variables-refactor.md): Find all hardcoded colors, spacing, and font values, then convert them to a design system using variables.\n- [Link Auditor And Fixer](https://developers.webflow.com/mcp/prompts/link-auditor-and-fixer.md): Find and fix broken or insecure links across an entire site, including CMS content, to improve SEO and user experience.\n- [Breakpoint Styles Updater](https://developers.webflow.com/mcp/prompts/breakpoint-styles-updater.md): Systematically update CSS styles across all Webflow breakpoints to ensure responsive design consistency.\n- [Breakpoint Style Migrator](https://developers.webflow.com/mcp/prompts/breakpoint-style-migrator.md): Rescue design work done on the wrong breakpoint by copying or moving styles from one breakpoint to another.\n- [Slider Builder](https://developers.webflow.com/mcp/prompts/slider-builder.md): Build a fully functional interactive image slider using Swiper.js library with autoplay, navigation, and responsive design.\n","metadata":{"truncated":false},"title":"https://developers.webflow.com/mcp/llms.txt (text/markdown; charset=utf-8)","time":{"start":1785758746975,"end":1785758747161}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0426dad13d96f365016a70841ad6088191af655f5c8dd12f3d"}},"id":"prt_fc784092e001ycNlFiHuvhlKUc","sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","messageID":"msg_fc783adff001lQyiyUUoVRMK1z"}}
