bflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/sol-high-fast/deep-research-dashboard.md\nM .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/sol-high-fast/orchestration-status.log","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/sol-high-fast/deep-research-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/sol-high-fast/deep-research-strategy.md\n+++ /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/sol-high-fast/deep-research-strategy.md\n@@ -8,9 +8,9 @@\n ## 2. Key Questions\n \n - [ ] Q1: Does the local packet accurately and sufficiently describe its own tool inventory, safety boundaries, payloads, and local-versus-remote reconciliation?\n - [x] Q2: Does it cover the official Designer canvas, Bridge App, element-tree, component, style, variable-mode, and breakpoint semantics deeply enough for reliable execution? Answer: architecture yes, execution semantics no; see iteration 2.\n-- [ ] Q3: Does it cover CMS drafts, sites/pages, publish/branches, scripts, forms, localization, assets/compression, webhooks, and enterprise behavior deeply enough?\n+- [x] Q3: Does it cover CMS drafts, sites/pages, publish/branches, scripts, forms, localization, assets/compression, webhooks, and enterprise behavior deeply enough? Answer: breadth yes, lifecycle constraints no; see iteration 3.\n - [ ] Q4: Does it cover AI tools, agent instructions, WHTML, utility tools, rate limits, and remote-only/local-OSS differences without overclaiming support?\n - [ ] Q5: Do the nine feature cards plus root and all 17 manual scenarios trace to the important official behavior, edge cases, and failure modes?\n <!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n \n@@ -29,23 +29,26 @@\n <!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n ## 5. Answered Questions\n \n - Q2: The Bridge boundary is correct, but mode errors, replacement semantics, component/variant constraints, effect classification, and breakpoint/pseudo behavior are materially under-documented. (iteration 2)\n+- Q3: Remote CMS draft behavior is correct, but asset, script, locale, form, branch, endpoint-limit, and rate-budget semantics are incomplete. (iteration 3)\n <!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n \n <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n <!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n ## 6. What Worked\n \n - Cross-reading the action table, semantic reference, and examples exposed contradictions hidden by any single artifact. (iteration 1)\n - Grouped official Designer/Data pages exposed behavior omitted from the local required-parameter inventory. (iteration 2)\n+- Comparing action descriptions rather than names exposed irreversible, replace-all, async, and cardinality behavior. (iteration 3)\n <!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n ## 7. What Failed\n \n - Local packet evidence cannot validate deployed remote semantics without official documentation or live discovery. (iteration 1)\n - Guessed per-tool official URLs are not canonical; grouped tool-family pages must be used. (iteration 2)\n+- Guessed individual REST branch/publish URLs were stale; grouped MCP docs supplied the needed boundary evidence. (iteration 3)\n <!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n ## 8. Exhausted Approaches\n@@ -57,8 +60,9 @@\n ## 9. Ruled-Out Directions\n \n - Treating the entire packet as uniformly too concise: the 498-line action inventory is broad; the gap is uneven executable depth. (iteration 1, evidence: `references/action-reference.md:12-24`)\n - Assuming every Designer operation requires the Bridge App: official architecture limits the requirement to live canvas/session state and snapshots. (iteration 2, evidence: official how-it-works)\n+- Assuming remote CMS create/update is live: official remote actions create/update drafts and publish separately. (iteration 3, evidence: official Data tools)\n <!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n ## 10. Divergence Frontier\n@@ -71,15 +75,15 @@\n <!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n ## 11. Carried-Forward Open Questions\n \n - Which Canvas actions mutate persistent site state versus only remote Designer session state?\n-- How do content, publish, branch, script, form, localization, asset, webhook, and enterprise edge cases compare with local guidance?\n+- How do Agent Instructions/resources, utility discovery, WHTML, official limitations, and tool-name migration affect the packet?\n <!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n ## 12. Next Focus\n \n-Validate official CMS draft/publish, page/branch, script, form, localization, site, asset/compression, webhook, and enterprise semantics.\n+Validate AI tools, Agent Instructions/resources, WHTML, utility discovery, official limitations, and local-OSS versus remote migration/reconciliation.\n <!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n \n ## 13. Known Context\n\nIndex: /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/sol-high-fast/findings-registry.json\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/sol-high-fast/findings-registry.json\n+++ /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/sol-high-fast/findings-registry.json\n@@ -1,13 +1,13 @@\n {\n   \"openQuestions\": [\n     {\"id\":\"Q1\",\"text\":\"Does the local packet accurately and sufficiently describe its own tool inventory, safety boundaries, payloads, and local-versus-remote reconciliation?\"},\n-    {\"id\":\"Q3\",\"text\":\"Does it cover content, publishing, branches, scripts, forms, localization, assets, webhooks, and enterprise behavior deeply enough?\"},\n     {\"id\":\"Q4\",\"text\":\"Does it cover AI tools, agent instructions, WHTML, utility tools, rate limits, and local-versus-remote differences without overclaiming?\"},\n     {\"id\":\"Q5\",\"text\":\"Do feature cards and manual scenarios trace to important official behavior and edge cases?\"}\n   ],\n   \"resolvedQuestions\": [\n     {\"id\":\"Q2\",\"text\":\"Does it cover official Designer and Bridge App semantics deeply enough for reliable execution?\",\"answer\":\"Bridge architecture is correct, but execution semantics are materially incomplete.\",\"iteration\":2}\n+    ,{\"id\":\"Q3\",\"text\":\"Does it cover content, publishing, branches, scripts, forms, localization, assets, webhooks, and enterprise behavior deeply enough?\",\"answer\":\"Coverage breadth is high, but lifecycle constraints and endpoint limits are materially incomplete.\",\"iteration\":3}\n   ],\n   \"keyFindings\": [\n     {\"id\":\"f-iter001-001\",\"severity\":\"P1\",\"title\":\"Payload examples omit or mismatch required keys\",\"iteration\":1,\"source\":\"iterations/iteration-001.md\"},\n     {\"id\":\"f-iter001-002\",\"severity\":\"P1\",\"title\":\"Action index lacks invocation semantics\",\"iteration\":1,\"source\":\"iterations/iteration-001.md\"},\n@@ -19,24 +19,32 @@\n     {\"id\":\"f-iter002-002\",\"severity\":\"P1\",\"title\":\"set_style replacement semantics omitted\",\"iteration\":2,\"source\":\"iterations/iteration-002.md\"},\n     {\"id\":\"f-iter002-003\",\"severity\":\"P1\",\"title\":\"Component prop and binding semantics too concise\",\"iteration\":2,\