{"type":"text","timestamp":1785758981427,"sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","part":{"id":"prt_fc7879a1f001qBBi7l02W88Uf0","messageID":"msg_fc78730df001i47y5hNqtwC4J2","sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","type":"text","text":"Official migration guidance reveals a more serious reconciliation issue: the local “remote 2.0.0” inventory already uses tool splits introduced only in 2.0.1, while the local OSS baseline still uses v1.3-era names and the configured npm manual runs `@latest`. Agent Instructions also introduce a safety-critical trust boundary because Webflow provides site-authored instructions automatically and the packet does not state that they can never override operator gates.","time":{"start":1785758980639,"end":1785758981424},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_0dfd4b715b0d015d016a7085046dd08191b91179cb8039a64a","phase":"commentary"}}}}
