{"type":"text","timestamp":1785759198744,"sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","part":{"id":"prt_fc78ad554001otuwZj2GBlcWoj","messageID":"msg_fc78a9c56001i0XGfC3W2yIECS","sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","type":"text","text":"The iteration-4 evidence artifacts passed, but the reducer refresh patch failed atomically because one strategy question differed from the expected wording. No file received a partial reducer update; I am re-reading the current generated surfaces and applying a context-correct refresh before iteration 5.","time":{"start":1785759192404,"end":1785759198743},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_0a716be80e04d936016a7085d85988819193695e2e3b2c23c0","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785759198904,"sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_dJDDS6u0M5PyjfWOT2lwTm4I","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/sol-high-fast/deep-research-strategy.md","offset":1,"limit":180},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/sol-high-fast/deep-research-strategy.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Deep Research Strategy: mcp-webflow Quality Gaps\n2: \n3: ## 1. Research Topic\n4: \n5: Audit `.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow` for overly concise or missing Webflow MCP 2.0 logic across references, assets, feature-catalog cards, and the 17-scenario manual-testing playbook.\n6: \n7: <!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n8: ## 2. Key Questions\n9: \n10: - [ ] Q1: Does the local packet accurately and sufficiently describe its own tool inventory, safety boundaries, payloads, and local-versus-remote reconciliation?\n11: - [x] Q2: Does it cover the official Designer canvas, Bridge App, element-tree, component, style, variable-mode, and breakpoint semantics deeply enough for reliable execution? Answer: architecture yes, execution semantics no; see iteration 2.\n12: - [x] Q3: Does it cover CMS drafts, sites/pages, publish/branches, scripts, forms, localization, assets/compression, webhooks, and enterprise behavior deeply enough? Answer: breadth yes, lifecycle constraints no; see iteration 3.\n13: - [ ] Q4: Does it cover AI tools, agent instructions, WHTML, utility tools, rate limits, and remote-only/local-OSS differences without overclaiming support?\n14: - [ ] Q5: Do the nine feature cards plus root and all 17 manual scenarios trace to the important official behavior, edge cases, and failure modes?\n15: <!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n16: \n17: ## 3. Non-Goals\n18: \n19: - Do not implement fixes or modify the audited skill packet.\n20: - Do not authenticate to or mutate a live Webflow workspace.\n21: - Do not infer remote tools solely from the local OSS repository when official remote documentation differs.\n22: \n23: ## 4. Stop Conditions\n24: \n25: - Complete exactly five iterations because `stopPolicy=max-iterations`.\n26: - Every reported gap must cite a local file/line or official URL.\n27: - Final synthesis must classify concrete gaps as P0, P1, or P2 and recommend bounded corrections.\n28: \n29: <!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n30: ## 5. Answered Questions\n31: \n32: - Q2: The Bridge boundary is correct, but mode errors, replacement semantics, component/variant constraints, effect classification, and breakpoint/pseudo behavior are materially under-documented. (iteration 2)\n33: - Q3: Remote CMS draft behavior is correct, but asset, script, locale, form, branch, endpoint-limit, and rate-budget semantics are incomplete. (iteration 3)\n34: <!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n35: \n36: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n37: <!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n38: ## 6. What Worked\n39: \n40: - Cross-reading the action table, semantic reference, and examples exposed contradictions hidden by any single artifact. (iteration 1)\n41: - Grouped official Designer/Data pages exposed behavior omitted from the local required-parameter inventory. (iteration 2)\n42: - Comparing action descriptions rather than names exposed irreversible, replace-all, async, and cardinality behavior. (iteration 3)\n43: <!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n44: \n45: <!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n46: ## 7. What Failed\n47: \n48: - Local packet evidence cannot validate deployed remote semantics without official documentation or live discovery. (iteration 1)\n49: - Guessed per-tool official URLs are not canonical; grouped tool-family pages must be used. (iteration 2)\n50: - Guessed individual REST branch/publish URLs were stale; grouped MCP docs supplied the needed boundary evidence. (iteration 3)\n51: <!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n52: \n53: <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n54: ## 8. Exhausted Approaches\n55: \n56: None.\n57: <!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n58: \n59: <!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n60: ## 9. Ruled-Out Directions\n61: \n62: - Treating the entire packet as uniformly too concise: the 498-line action inventory is broad; the gap is uneven executable depth. (iteration 1, evidence: `references/action-reference.md:12-24`)\n63: - Assuming every Designer operation requires the Bridge App: official architecture limits the requirement to live canvas/session state and snapshots. (iteration 2, evidence: official how-it-works)\n64: - Assuming remote CMS create/update is live: official remote actions create/update drafts and publish separately. (iteration 3, evidence: official Data tools)\n65: <!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n66: \n67: <!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n68: ## 10. Divergence Frontier\n69: \n70: - Completed pivots: 0\n71: - Saturated directions: none\n72: - Remaining frontier: all five key questions\n73: <!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n74: \n75: <!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n76: ## 11. Carried-Forward Open Questions\n77: \n78: - Which Canvas actions mutate persistent site state versus only remote Designer session state?\n79: - How do Agent Instructions/resources, utility discovery, WHTML, official limitations, and tool-name migration affect the packet?\n80: <!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n81: \n82: <!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n83: ## 12. Next Focus\n84: \n85: Validate AI tools, Agent Instructions/resources, WHTML, utility discovery, official limitations, and local-OSS versus remote migration/reconciliation.\n86: <!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n87: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n88: \n89: ## 13. Known Context\n90: \n91: - Source pointers: `.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/`, `assets/`, `feature-catalog/`, and `manual-testing-playbook/`.\n92: - The packet contains five named references, two root assets plus five worked examples, nine feature cards plus a root catalog, and 17 scenario snippets plus a root playbook.\n93: - `resource-map.md` is not present in the target spec; skipping the existing-map coverage gate.\n94: - Spec write-back and continuity save are outside this detached lineage's authorized write root and will be recorded as skipped.\n95: \n96: ## 14. Research Boundaries\n97: \n98: - Max iterations: 5\n99: - Convergence threshold: 0.05 (telemetry only before iteration 5)\n100: - Stop policy: max-iterations\n101: - Allowed write root: `.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/sol-high-fast`\n102: - Audited files are read-only.\n\n(End of file - total 102 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Deep Research Strategy: mcp-webflow Quality Gaps\n\n## 1. Research Topic\n\nAudit `.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow` for overly concise or missing Webflow MCP 2.0 logic across references, assets, feature-catalog cards, and the 17-scenario manual-testing playbook.\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n## 2. Key Questions\n\n- [ ] Q1: Does the local packet accurately and sufficiently describe its own tool inventory, safety boundaries, payloads, and local-versus-remote reconciliation?\n- [x] Q2: Does it cover the official Designer canvas, Bridge App, element-tree, component, style, variable-mode, and breakpoint semantics deeply enough for reliable execution? Answer: architecture yes, execution semantics no; see iteration 2.\n- [x] Q3: Does it cover CMS drafts, sites/pages, publish/branches, scripts, forms, localization, assets/compression, webhooks, and enterprise behavior deeply enough? Answer: breadth yes, lifecycle constraints no; see iteration 3.\n- [ ] Q4: Does it cover AI tools, agent instructions, WHTML, utility tools, rate limits, and remote-only/local-OSS differences without overclaiming support?\n- [ ] Q5: Do the nine feature cards plus root and all 17 manual scenarios trace to the important official behavior, edge cases, and failure modes?\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n\n## 3. Non-Goals\n\n- Do not implement fixes or modify the audited skill packet.\n- Do not authenticate to or mutate a live Webflow workspace.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/sol-high-fast/deep-research-strategy.md","text":"# Deep Research Strategy: mcp-webflow Quality Gaps\n\n## 1. Research Topic\n\nAudit `.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow` for overly concise or missing Webflow MCP 2.0 logic across references, assets, feature-catalog cards, and the 17-scenario manual-testing playbook.\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n## 2. Key Questions\n\n- [ ] Q1: Does the local packet accurately and sufficiently describe its own tool inventory, safety boundaries, payloads, and local-versus-remote reconciliation?\n- [x] Q2: Does it cover the official Designer canvas, Bridge App, element-tree, component, style, variable-mode, and breakpoint semantics deeply enough for reliable execution? Answer: architecture yes, execution semantics no; see iteration 2.\n- [x] Q3: Does it cover CMS drafts, sites/pages, publish/branches, scripts, forms, localization, assets/compression, webhooks, and enterprise behavior deeply enough? Answer: breadth yes, lifecycle constraints no; see iteration 3.\n- [ ] Q4: Does it cover AI tools, agent instructions, WHTML, utility tools, rate limits, and remote-only/local-OSS differences without overclaiming support?\n- [ ] Q5: Do the nine feature cards plus root and all 17 manual scenarios trace to the important official behavior, edge cases, and failure modes?\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n\n## 3. Non-Goals\n\n- Do not implement fixes or modify the audited skill packet.\n- Do not authenticate to or mutate a live Webflow workspace.\n- Do not infer remote tools solely from the local OSS repository when official remote documentation differs.\n\n## 4. Stop Conditions\n\n- Complete exactly five iterations because `stopPolicy=max-iterations`.\n- Every reported gap must cite a local file/line or official URL.\n- Final synthesis must classify concrete gaps as P0, P1, or P2 and recommend bounded corrections.\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n## 5. Answered Questions\n\n- Q2: The Bridge boundary is correct, but mode errors, replacement semantics, component/variant constraints, effect classification, and breakpoint/pseudo behavior are materially under-documented. (iteration 2)\n- Q3: Remote CMS draft behavior is correct, but asset, script, locale, form, branch, endpoint-limit, and rate-budget semantics are incomplete. (iteration 3)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n## 6. What Worked\n\n- Cross-reading the action table, semantic reference, and examples exposed contradictions hidden by any single artifact. (iteration 1)\n- Grouped official Designer/Data pages exposed behavior omitted from the local required-parameter inventory. (iteration 2)\n- Comparing action descriptions rather than names exposed irreversible, replace-all, async, and cardinality behavior. (iteration 3)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n## 7. What Failed\n\n- Local packet evidence cannot validate deployed remote semantics without official documentation or live discovery. (iteration 1)\n- Guessed per-tool official URLs are not canonical; grouped tool-family pages must be used. (iteration 2)\n- Guessed individual REST branch/publish URLs were stale; grouped MCP docs supplied the needed boundary evidence. (iteration 3)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n## 8. Exhausted Approaches\n\nNone.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n## 9. Ruled-Out Directions\n\n- Treating the entire packet as uniformly too concise: the 498-line action inventory is broad; the gap is uneven executable depth. (iteration 1, evidence: `references/action-reference.md:12-24`)\n- Assuming every Designer operation requires the Bridge App: official architecture limits the requirement to live canvas/session state and snapshots. (iteration 2, evidence: official how-it-works)\n- Assuming remote CMS create/update is live: official remote actions create/update drafts and publish separately. (iteration 3, evidence: official Data tools)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n## 10. Divergence Frontier\n\n- Completed pivots: 0\n- Saturated directions: none\n- Remaining frontier: all five key questions\n<!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n## 11. Carried-Forward Open Questions\n\n- Which Canvas actions mutate persistent site state versus only remote Designer session state?\n- How do Agent Instructions/resources, utility discovery, WHTML, official limitations, and tool-name migration affect the packet?\n<!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 12. Next Focus\n\nValidate AI tools, Agent Instructions/resources, WHTML, utility discovery, official limitations, and local-OSS versus remote migration/reconciliation.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n## 13. Known Context\n\n- Source pointers: `.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/`, `assets/`, `feature-catalog/`, and `manual-testing-playbook/`.\n- The packet contains five named references, two root assets plus five worked examples, nine feature cards plus a root catalog, and 17 scenario snippets plus a root playbook.\n- `resource-map.md` is not present in the target spec; skipping the existing-map coverage gate.\n- Spec write-back and continuity save are outside this detached lineage's authorized write root and will be recorded as skipped.\n\n## 14. Research Boundaries\n\n- Max iterations: 5\n- Convergence threshold: 0.05 (telemetry only before iteration 5)\n- Stop policy: max-iterations\n- Allowed write root: `.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/sol-high-fast`\n- Audited files are read-only.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":102,"totalLines":102,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/sol-high-fast/deep-research-strategy.md","time":{"start":1785759198892,"end":1785759198903}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0a716be80e04d936016a7085deac2c8191bd61b87af1887c6c"}},"id":"prt_fc78aee4a0019vDyG3ZuUnGfC7","sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","messageID":"msg_fc78a9c56001i0XGfC3W2yIECS"}}
