{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785759280697,"sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_1WpNl51j49tzz1uREdijX3sG","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: \"mcp-webflow: Feature Catalog\"\n3: description: \"Canonical capability inventory for the mcp-webflow transport: the complete remote Webflow MCP 2.0 surface (31 tools / 220 actions) plus the labeled local OSS baseline, with frozen operation classes and gates.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"webflow\"\n6:   - \"webflow feature catalog\"\n7:   - \"webflow capabilities\"\n8: last_updated: \"2026-08-03\"\n9: version: 1.2.0.0\n10: ---\n11: \n12: # mcp-webflow: Feature Catalog\n13: \n14: \n15: Canonical capability inventory for the mcp-webflow transport.\n16: \n17: ---\n18: \n19: ---\n20: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n21: \n22: Canonical capability inventory for the `mcp-webflow` skill. The transport reaches Webflow MCP 2.0\n23: through the `webflow` Code Mode manual (official `webflow-mcp-server`, `WEBFLOW_TOKEN`). The\n24: **remote deployed surface** (`com.webflow/mcp` 2.0.0, official docs 2026-08-03) exposes **31 tools\n25: and 220 actions** — the complete list of everything an AI can do — with per-action required\n26: parameters in [`../references/action-reference.md`](../references/action-reference.md). The local\n27: OSS server exposes the smaller 18-module baseline, labeled separately below. Every capability is\n28: tagged with its frozen operation class (RO read-only, DW draft-write, DS destructive, PB publish,\n29: DP deploy) and gate. The transport never mutates this workspace (`mutatesWorkspace: false`;\n30: Write/Edit/Task forbidden); all mutations land in Webflow's cloud under the frozen gates.\n31: Designer-family modules require `sk-design` pairing.\n32: \n33: ---\n34: ## 2. REMOTE SURFACE (31 tools / 220 actions, 21 groups)\n35: \n36: | Capability group | Tools | Actions | Read/Write |\n37: |---|---|---|---|\n38: | Agent Instructions | 1 | 6 | read, write |\n39: | Analyze (add-on) | 1 | 7 | read |\n40: | Assets | 3 | 14 | read, write |\n41: | CMS | 1 | 14 | read, write |\n42: | Comments | 1 | 5 | read, write |\n43: | Components | 4 | 27 | read, write |\n44: | Elements | 3 | 21 | read, write |\n45: | Enterprise | 1 | 11 | read, write |\n46: | Fonts | 1 | 7 | read, write |\n47: | Forms | 1 | 7 | read, write |\n48: | Localization | 1 | 7 | read, write |\n49: | Pages | 1 | 11 | read, write |\n50: | Scripts | 1 | 20 | read, write |\n51: | Sitemap | 1 | 8 | read, write |\n52: | Sites | 1 | 3 | read, write |\n53: | Style | 1 | 10 | read, write |\n54: | Variables | 1 | 18 | read, write |\n55: | Webhooks | 1 | 4 | read, write |\n56: | WHTML | 1 | 1 | write |\n57: | Designer canvas | 2 | 16 | read, write |\n58: | Utility | 3 | 3 | read |\n59: \n60: ---\n61: ## 3. CAPABILITY CARDS\n62: \n63: ---\n64: ### CMS\n65: \n66: #### Description\n67: \n68: CMS content: reads, draft writes (remote = drafts), publish/unpublish (PB), delete (DS)\n69: \n70: #### Current Reality\n71: \n72: Documented from the official remote action reference (2026-08-03); live discovery of the pinned\n73: version remains the authoritative inventory.\n74: \n75: #### Source Files\n76: \n77: See [`design/component-variants.md`](design/component-variants.md) for the full capability card.\n78: \n79: ---\n80: ### Publish and deploy\n81: \n82: #### Description\n83: \n84: publish_site / publish_collection_items / unpublish — staging-first gates and the 1/min queue\n85: \n86: #### Current Reality\n87: \n88: Documented from the official remote action reference (2026-08-03); live discovery of the pinned\n89: version remains the authoritative inventory.\n90: \n91: #### Source Files\n92: \n93: See [`content/publish-deploy.md`](content/publish-deploy.md) for the full capability card.\n94: \n95: ---\n96: ### Designer-family\n97: \n98: #### Description\n99: \n100: Elements, styles, variables, components, assets, pages — always paired with sk-design\n101: \n102: #### Current Reality\n103: \n104: Full operational logic in [`references/designer-capabilities.md`](../references/designer-capabilities.md):\n105: canvas model and Bridge App boundary, selection-driven edit loop (snapshot → discover → focus →\n106: mutate → verify), element-tree semantics, styles bound to variable modes, components with\n107: props/slots/variants, breakpoints, and worked flows. All edits draft-only until the separate\n108: publish gate. Documented from the official remote action reference (2026-08-03); live discovery of\n109: the pinned version remains the authoritative inventory.\n110: \n111: #### Source Files\n112: \n113: See [`design/designer.md`](design/designer.md) for the full capability card.\n114: \n115: ---\n116: ### Site, pages, scripts, webhooks, enterprise, AI\n117: \n118: #### Description\n119: \n120: The remaining Data-API modules incl. comments, sitemap, branches\n121: \n122: #### Current Reality\n123: \n124: Documented from the official remote action reference (2026-08-03); live discovery of the pinned\n125: version remains the authoritative inventory.\n126: \n127: #### Source Files\n128: \n129: See [`content/site-pages-scripts.md`](content/site-pages-scripts.md) for the full capability card.\n130: \n131: ---\n132: ### Agent Instructions\n133: \n134: #### Description\n135: \n136: Site rules and skills: create/read/search/update/move/delete\n137: \n138: #### Current Reality\n139: \n140: Documented from the official remote action reference (2026-08-03); live discovery of the pinned\n141: version remains the authoritative inventory.\n142: \n143: #### Source Files\n144: \n145: See [`intelligence/agent-instructions.md`](intelligence/agent-instructions.md) for the full capability card.\n146: \n147: ---\n148: ### Analyze add-on\n149: \n150: #### Description\n151: \n152: Traffic, ranked pages/dimensions, engagement, time-on-page reports\n153: \n154: #### Current Reality\n155: \n156: Documented from the official remote action reference (2026-08-03); live discovery of the pinned\n157: version remains the authoritative inventory.\n158: \n159: #### Source Files\n160: \n161: See [`intelligence/analyze.md`](intelligence/analyze.md) for the full capability card.\n162: \n163: ---\n164: ### Localization, fonts, forms\n165: \n166: #### Description\n167: \n168: Localized content, font management, form submissions\n169: \n170: #### Current Reality\n171: \n172: Documented from the official remote action reference (2026-08-03); live discovery of the pinned\n173: version remains the authoritative inventory.\n174: \n175: #### Source Files\n176: \n177: See [`content/localization-fonts-forms.md`](content/localization-fonts-forms.md) for the full capability card.\n178: \n179: ---\n180: ### Sitemap, scripts, assets, WHTML\n181: \n182: #### Description\n183: \n184: Bulk sitemap status, the 20-action scripts surface, asset compression, WHMTL building\n185: \n186: #### Current Reality\n187: \n188: Documented from the official remote action reference (2026-08-03); live discovery of the pinned\n189: version remains the authoritative inventory.\n190: \n191: #### Source Files\n192: \n193: See [`operations/sitemap-scripts-assets-whtml.md`](operations/sitemap-scripts-assets-whtml.md) for the full capability card.\n194: \n195: ---\n196: ### Component variants\n197: \n198: #### Description\n199: \n200: Variant reads, create/update, default variants, delete_variant (DS)\n201: \n202: #### Current Reality\n203: \n204: Documented from the official remote action reference (2026-08-03); live discovery of the pinned\n205: version remains the authoritative inventory.\n206: \n207: #### Source Files\n208: \n209: See [`design/component-variants.md`](design/component-variants.md) for the full capability card.\n210: \n211: ---\n212: ## 4. LOCAL OSS BASELINE (18 modules)\n213: \n214: The local `webflow-mcp-server` (npm) surface is the research-time 18-module baseline documented in\n215: [`../references/tool-surface.md`](../references/tool-surface.md) (sites, pages, cms, components,\n216: scripts, workflows, webhooks, enterprise, aiChat, comments, rules, dePages, deElement, deStyle,\n217: deVariable, deComponents, deAsset, localDeMCPConnection). It includes capabilities absent from the\n218: remote surface (e.g., `run_workflow`, Designer `de*` modules) and omits remote-only tools\n219: (analyze, fonts, forms, localization, sitemap, WHTML, component variants, agent instructions).\n220: Do not mix surfaces when calling tools.\n221: \n222: ---\n223: ## 5. CROSS-CUTTING CAPABILITIES\n224: \n225: - **No auto-publish**: publishing is always a separate explicit action (1/min queue); remote CMS\n226:   writes create drafts, publish/unpublish is PB.\n227: - **Rate discipline**: plan-based 60/120 rpm; 429 + `Retry-After`; SDK backoff default.\n228: - **Least privilege**: read-only scopes baseline; `sites:write` only for staging publish;\n229:   workspace tokens read-only.\n230: - **Rollback**: staged-first; CMS re-publish; Designer version-history snapshot; API-level site\n231:   restore UNKNOWN (treated as unsupported).\n232: - **Pairing**: Designer-family → `sk-design`; Data-family transport-only.\n233: - **Unknown tools**: class UNKNOWN — prohibited until the live schema classifies them.\n\n(End of file - total 233 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: \"mcp-webflow: Feature Catalog\"\ndescription: \"Canonical capability inventory for the mcp-webflow transport: the complete remote Webflow MCP 2.0 surface (31 tools / 220 actions) plus the labeled local OSS baseline, with frozen operation classes and gates.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"webflow\"\n  - \"webflow feature catalog\"\n  - \"webflow capabilities\"\nlast_updated: \"2026-08-03\"\nversion: 1.2.0.0\n---\n\n# mcp-webflow: Feature Catalog\n\n\nCanonical capability inventory for the mcp-webflow transport.\n\n---\n\n---\n## 1. OVERVIEW","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md","text":"---\ntitle: \"mcp-webflow: Feature Catalog\"\ndescription: \"Canonical capability inventory for the mcp-webflow transport: the complete remote Webflow MCP 2.0 surface (31 tools / 220 actions) plus the labeled local OSS baseline, with frozen operation classes and gates.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"webflow\"\n  - \"webflow feature catalog\"\n  - \"webflow capabilities\"\nlast_updated: \"2026-08-03\"\nversion: 1.2.0.0\n---\n\n# mcp-webflow: Feature Catalog\n\n\nCanonical capability inventory for the mcp-webflow transport.\n\n---\n\n---\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nCanonical capability inventory for the `mcp-webflow` skill. The transport reaches Webflow MCP 2.0\nthrough the `webflow` Code Mode manual (official `webflow-mcp-server`, `WEBFLOW_TOKEN`). The\n**remote deployed surface** (`com.webflow/mcp` 2.0.0, official docs 2026-08-03) exposes **31 tools\nand 220 actions** — the complete list of everything an AI can do — with per-action required\nparameters in [`../references/action-reference.md`](../references/action-reference.md). The local\nOSS server exposes the smaller 18-module baseline, labeled separately below. Every capability is\ntagged with its frozen operation class (RO read-only, DW draft-write, DS destructive, PB publish,\nDP deploy) and gate. The transport never mutates this workspace (`mutatesWorkspace: false`;\nWrite/Edit/Task forbidden); all mutations land in Webflow's cloud under the frozen gates.\nDesigner-family modules require `sk-design` pairing.\n\n---\n## 2. REMOTE SURFACE (31 tools / 220 actions, 21 groups)\n\n| Capability group | Tools | Actions | Read/Write |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Agent Instructions | 1 | 6 | read, write |\n| Analyze (add-on) | 1 | 7 | read |\n| Assets | 3 | 14 | read, write |\n| CMS | 1 | 14 | read, write |\n| Comments | 1 | 5 | read, write |\n| Components | 4 | 27 | read, write |\n| Elements | 3 | 21 | read, write |\n| Enterprise | 1 | 11 | read, write |\n| Fonts | 1 | 7 | read, write |\n| Forms | 1 | 7 | read, write |\n| Localization | 1 | 7 | read, write |\n| Pages | 1 | 11 | read, write |\n| Scripts | 1 | 20 | read, write |\n| Sitemap | 1 | 8 | read, write |\n| Sites | 1 | 3 | read, write |\n| Style | 1 | 10 | read, write |\n| Variables | 1 | 18 | read, write |\n| Webhooks | 1 | 4 | read, write |\n| WHTML | 1 | 1 | write |\n| Designer canvas | 2 | 16 | read, write |\n| Utility | 3 | 3 | read |\n\n---\n## 3. CAPABILITY CARDS\n\n---\n### CMS\n\n#### Description\n\nCMS content: reads, draft writes (remote = drafts), publish/unpublish (PB), delete (DS)\n\n#### Current Reality\n\nDocumented from the official remote action reference (2026-08-03); live discovery of the pinned\nversion remains the authoritative inventory.\n\n#### Source Files\n\nSee [`design/component-variants.md`](design/component-variants.md) for the full capability card.\n\n---\n### Publish and deploy\n\n#### Description\n\npublish_site / publish_collection_items / unpublish — staging-first gates and the 1/min queue\n\n#### Current Reality\n\nDocumented from the official remote action reference (2026-08-03); live discovery of the pinned\nversion remains the authoritative inventory.\n\n#### Source Files\n\nSee [`content/publish-deploy.md`](content/publish-deploy.md) for the full capability card.\n\n---\n### Designer-family\n\n#### Description\n\nElements, styles, variables, components, assets, pages — always paired with sk-design\n\n#### Current Reality\n\nFull operational logic in [`references/designer-capabilities.md`](../references/designer-capabilities.md):\ncanvas model and Bridge App boundary, selection-driven edit loop (snapshot → discover → focus →\nmutate → verify), element-tree semantics, styles bound to variable modes, components with\nprops/slots/variants, breakpoints, and worked flows. All edits draft-only until the separate\npublish gate. Documented from the official remote action reference (2026-08-03); live discovery of\nthe pinned version remains the authoritative inventory.\n\n#### Source Files\n\nSee [`design/designer.md`](design/designer.md) for the full capability card.\n\n---\n### Site, pages, scripts, webhooks, enterprise, AI\n\n#### Description\n\nThe remaining Data-API modules incl. comments, sitemap, branches\n\n#### Current Reality\n\nDocumented from the official remote action reference (2026-08-03); live discovery of the pinned\nversion remains the authoritative inventory.\n\n#### Source Files\n\nSee [`content/site-pages-scripts.md`](content/site-pages-scripts.md) for the full capability card.\n\n---\n### Agent Instructions\n\n#### Description\n\nSite rules and skills: create/read/search/update/move/delete\n\n#### Current Reality\n\nDocumented from the official remote action reference (2026-08-03); live discovery of the pinned\nversion remains the authoritative inventory.\n\n#### Source Files\n\nSee [`intelligence/agent-instructions.md`](intelligence/agent-instructions.md) for the full capability card.\n\n---\n### Analyze add-on\n\n#### Description\n\nTraffic, ranked pages/dimensions, engagement, time-on-page reports\n\n#### Current Reality\n\nDocumented from the official remote action reference (2026-08-03); live discovery of the pinned\nversion remains the authoritative inventory.\n\n#### Source Files\n\nSee [`intelligence/analyze.md`](intelligence/analyze.md) for the full capability card.\n\n---\n### Localization, fonts, forms\n\n#### Description\n\nLocalized content, font management, form submissions\n\n#### Current Reality\n\nDocumented from the official remote action reference (2026-08-03); live discovery of the pinned\nversion remains the authoritative inventory.\n\n#### Source Files\n\nSee [`content/localization-fonts-forms.md`](content/localization-fonts-forms.md) for the full capability card.\n\n---\n### Sitemap, scripts, assets, WHTML\n\n#### Description\n\nBulk sitemap status, the 20-action scripts surface, asset compression, WHMTL building\n\n#### Current Reality\n\nDocumented from the official remote action reference (2026-08-03); live discovery of the pinned\nversion remains the authoritative inventory.\n\n#### Source Files\n\nSee [`operations/sitemap-scripts-assets-whtml.md`](operations/sitemap-scripts-assets-whtml.md) for the full capability card.\n\n---\n### Component variants\n\n#### Description\n\nVariant reads, create/update, default variants, delete_variant (DS)\n\n#### Current Reality\n\nDocumented from the official remote action reference (2026-08-03); live discovery of the pinned\nversion remains the authoritative inventory.\n\n#### Source Files\n\nSee [`design/component-variants.md`](design/component-variants.md) for the full capability card.\n\n---\n## 4. LOCAL OSS BASELINE (18 modules)\n\nThe local `webflow-mcp-server` (npm) surface is the research-time 18-module baseline documented in\n[`../references/tool-surface.md`](../references/tool-surface.md) (sites, pages, cms, components,\nscripts, workflows, webhooks, enterprise, aiChat, comments, rules, dePages, deElement, deStyle,\ndeVariable, deComponents, deAsset, localDeMCPConnection). It includes capabilities absent from the\nremote surface (e.g., `run_workflow`, Designer `de*` modules) and omits remote-only tools\n(analyze, fonts, forms, localization, sitemap, WHTML, component variants, agent instructions).\nDo not mix surfaces when calling tools.\n\n---\n## 5. CROSS-CUTTING CAPABILITIES\n\n- **No auto-publish**: publishing is always a separate explicit action (1/min queue); remote CMS\n  writes create drafts, publish/unpublish is PB.\n- **Rate discipline**: plan-based 60/120 rpm; 429 + `Retry-After`; SDK backoff default.\n- **Least privilege**: read-only scopes baseline; `sites:write` only for staging publish;\n  workspace tokens read-only.\n- **Rollback**: staged-first; CMS re-publish; Designer version-history snapshot; API-level site\n  restore UNKNOWN (treated as unsupported).\n- **Pairing**: Designer-family → `sk-design`; Data-family transport-only.\n- **Unknown tools**: class UNKNOWN — prohibited until the live schema classifies them.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":233,"totalLines":233,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md","time":{"start":1785759280688,"end":1785759280696}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_07ad784273ab2e15016a7086306ef88191a0a10493ac607935"}},"id":"prt_fc78c2dcf001JoTnc4EYmcXS6r","sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","messageID":"msg_fc78bc4fb001HhUrnvUSQ0f6pQ"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785759280755,"sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_ZkpEu7jxNlLKZ1V8FmZgxXDI","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/design/designer.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/design/designer.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Designer-family\"\n3: description: \"Webflow Designer capability card: canvas model, elements, styles, variables, components, assets, pages via the Bridge App — always paired with sk-design, draft-only until publish.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"webflow designer\"\n6:   - \"webflow element\"\n7:   - \"webflow style\"\n8:   - \"webflow variable\"\n9:   - \"webflow component\"\n10:   - \"webflow canvas\"\n11:   - \"webflow design tokens\"\n12: importance_tier: important\n13: contextType: implementation\n14: version: 1.1.0.0\n15: \n16: # Designer-family\n17: \n18: <!-- sk-doc-template: skill_asset_feature_catalog -->\n19: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n20: \n21: Operates the live Designer canvas and site tree via the Bridge App: elements (deElement), styles\n22: (deStyle), variables (deVariable), components (deComponents), assets (deAsset), and pages\n23: (dePages). Full operational logic lives in\n24: [`../../references/designer-capabilities.md`](../../references/designer-capabilities.md).\n25: \n26: ---\n27: ## 2. HOW IT WORKS\n28: \n29: ### Canvas model and Bridge boundary\n30: \n31: Designer operations split into two planes. **Data-API designer modules** (elements, components,\n32: styles, variables, assets, pages) target the site tree and work without the canvas open. **Canvas\n33: state** — current page / mode / branch / component view / selection (`get_current_page`,\n34: `get_current_mode`, `get_current_branch_id`, `get_current_component`, `get_selected_element`,\n35: `check_if_inside_component_view`), canvas navigation (`open_canvas`, `switch_page`,\n36: `open_component_view`, `close_component_view`, `select_element`), visual snapshots, and breakpoint\n37: reads — requires the **Bridge App open in the Designer** (auto-installed on remote OAuth; local\n38: mode needs the Bridge App Designer extension). A Designer session confirms the canvas is open\n39: before the edit loop starts; a data-only session never assumes canvas state exists.\n40: \n41: ### Selection-driven edit loop\n42: \n43: 1. **Snapshot** — `get_element_snapshot` captures rendered state (RO).\n44: 2. **Discover** — `query_elements` / `get_all_elements` locate the target (RO).\n45: 3. **Focus** — `select_element` / `open_canvas` align agent and operator on the target.\n46: 4. **Mutate** — DW action with target id and write preview (sk-design decides what, transport\n47:    executes how).\n48: 5. **Verify** — snapshot / query read-back confirms the postcondition.\n49: \n50: Every mutation step is individually confirmable; destructive steps (DS) add operator confirmation\n51: plus a version-history rollback statement.\n52: \n53: ### Action surface\n54: \n55: | Module | Actions | Class | Gate |\n56: |--------|---------|-------|------|\n57: | dePages | `create_page`, `create_page_folder`, `switch_page` | DW | Designer session; sk-design for layout intent |\n58: | deElement | `query_elements`, `get_all_elements`, `get_attributes`, `get_display_name`, snapshot | RO | none |\n59: | deElement | `create_element`, `move_element`, `set_text`, `set_style`, `set_link`, `set_heading_level`, `set_image_asset`, `set_display_name`, `set_attributes`, settings (`set_settings`, `set_dom_id`, `set_tag`, `set_visibility`) | DW | **sk-design pairing required** |\n60: | deElement | `remove_element`, `remove_attribute`, `remove_style` | DS | operator confirmation; version-history rollback |\n61: | deStyle | style read/get, create/update/rename, `set_style_variable_mode` | RO/DW | sk-design pairing for DW |\n62: | deStyle | `remove_style`, `remove_style_variable_mode`, `remove_all_style_variable_modes` | DS | confirmation + rollback |\n63: | deVariable | get/query, collection + mode + typed variable create/update/rename/reorder | RO/DW | sk-design pairing for DW |\n64: | deVariable | `delete_variable` | DS | confirmation + rollback |\n65: | deComponents | read/get, `create_blank_component`, `duplicate_component`, `transform_element_to_component`, `set_component_metadata`, instance insert/unlink, builder (`insert_in_element`/`insert_in_slot`), props create/update/set/reset, variants create/duplicate/set/reorder | RO/DW | sk-design pairing for DW |\n66: | deComponents | `unregister_component`, `remove_prop`, `delete_variant` | DS | confirmation + rollback |\n67: | deAsset | asset read/list, create/upload (`upload_image_by_url`), compress, folders | RO/DW | sk-design pairing for DW |\n68: | deAsset | `delete_asset` | DS | confirmation + rollback |\n69: | localDeMCPConnection | `get_designer_app_connection_info` | RO | none (diagnostic) |\n70: \n71: ### Element-tree and token semantics\n72: \n73: Elements are addressed by `id {component, element}` with `parent_element_id` + `creation_position`\n74: positions; builder steps carry a `build_label`. `set_style` references **named styles**, not raw\n75: CSS — ensure the style exists before binding (`create_style` with `properties[]`). Styles bind to\n76: **variable modes** (`set_style_variable_mode`): create collection → create mode → create typed\n77: variables → bind style → apply style to elements; a second mode re-skins the same style without\n78: touching elements. Components expose **props** (instance customization), **slots** (`insert_in_slot`\n79: extension points), and **variants** (style layers via `set_variant_styles`); editing inside the\n80: component view (`open_component_view`) scopes mutations to the component master. Breakpoints are\n81: canvas-bound reads (`get_all_breakpoints`); responsive behavior flows through which styles apply\n82: and what they contain.\n83: \n84: ### Safety-critical semantics\n85: \n86: - Designer tools require the **Bridge App open in the Designer**; Data API tools work with Webflow\n87:   closed.\n88: - Designer edits are **draft-only inside the Designer** — they appear on the live site only after\n89:   `publish_site` (gated separately).\n90: - **All Designer-family operations load `sk-design` first** (cross-hub pairing): the transport\n91:   executes, never decides taste.\n92: - Branches (`create_branch`, `switch_page` to branch) isolate Designer edits until merge — the\n93:   natural staging pattern for design work.\n94: \n95: ### Example prompts\n96: \n97: - \"set the hero heading level to H1 in the test site\" → sk-design + deElement DW\n98: - \"create a variable collection 'Brand' with a mode 'Light'\" → sk-design + deVariable DW\n99: - \"remove the 'hero' element\" → confirmation + rollback statement (DS)\n100: \n101: ---\n102: ## 3. SOURCE FILES\n103: \n104: ### Implementation\n105: \n106: | File | Layer | Role |\n107: |---|---|---|\n108: | `../../references/designer-capabilities.md` | Shared | Full Designer logic: canvas model, edit loop, element/token/component semantics, worked flows |\n109: | `../../references/action-reference.md` | Shared | Required parameters per action (Elements, Components, Variables, Style, Designer canvas) |\n110: | `../../references/tool-surface.md` | Shared | Local OSS baseline where applicable |\n111: | `../../SKILL.md` | Shared | Frozen classes and gates |\n112: \n113: ### Validation And Tests\n114: \n115: | File | Type | Role |\n116: |---|---|---|\n117: | `../../manual-testing-playbook/` | Manual playbook | Designer edit loop scenario (DRAFT-003) and pairing scenarios |\n118: \n119: ## 4. SOURCE METADATA\n120: \n121: - Group: Elements, Components, Variables, Style, Designer canvas\n122: - Canonical catalog source: `feature-catalog.md`\n123: - Feature file path: `design/designer.md`\n124: \n125: Related references:\n126: - [`component-variants.md`](component-variants.md) — related capability\n127: - [`../../references/designer-capabilities.md`](../../references/designer-capabilities.md) — operational logic\n\n(End of file - total 127 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: \"Designer-family\"\ndescription: \"Webflow Designer capability card: canvas model, elements, styles, variables, components, assets, pages via the Bridge App — always paired with sk-design, draft-only until publish.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"webflow designer\"\n  - \"webflow element\"\n  - \"webflow style\"\n  - \"webflow variable\"\n  - \"webflow component\"\n  - \"webflow canvas\"\n  - \"webflow design tokens\"\nimportance_tier: important\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.1.0.0\n\n# Designer-family\n\n<!-- sk-doc-template: skill_asset_feature_catalog -->\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/design/designer.md","text":"---\ntitle: \"Designer-family\"\ndescription: \"Webflow Designer capability card: canvas model, elements, styles, variables, components, assets, pages via the Bridge App — always paired with sk-design, draft-only until publish.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"webflow designer\"\n  - \"webflow element\"\n  - \"webflow style\"\n  - \"webflow variable\"\n  - \"webflow component\"\n  - \"webflow canvas\"\n  - \"webflow design tokens\"\nimportance_tier: important\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.1.0.0\n\n# Designer-family\n\n<!-- sk-doc-template: skill_asset_feature_catalog -->\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nOperates the live Designer canvas and site tree via the Bridge App: elements (deElement), styles\n(deStyle), variables (deVariable), components (deComponents), assets (deAsset), and pages\n(dePages). Full operational logic lives in\n[`../../references/designer-capabilities.md`](../../references/designer-capabilities.md).\n\n---\n## 2. HOW IT WORKS\n\n### Canvas model and Bridge boundary\n\nDesigner operations split into two planes. **Data-API designer modules** (elements, components,\nstyles, variables, assets, pages) target the site tree and work without the canvas open. **Canvas\nstate** — current page / mode / branch / component view / selection (`get_current_page`,\n`get_current_mode`, `get_current_branch_id`, `get_current_component`, `get_selected_element`,\n`check_if_inside_component_view`), canvas navigation (`open_canvas`, `switch_page`,\n`open_component_view`, `close_component_view`, `select_element`), visual snapshots, and breakpoint\nreads — requires the **Bridge App open in the Designer** (auto-installed on remote OAuth; local\nmode needs the Bridge App Designer extension). A Designer session confirms the canvas is open\nbefore the edit loop starts; a data-only session never assumes canvas state exists.\n\n### Selection-driven edit loop\n\n1. **Snapshot** — `get_element_snapshot` captures rendered state (RO).\n2. **Discover** — `query_elements` / `get_all_elements` locate the target (RO).\n3. **Focus** — `select_element` / `open_canvas` align agent and operator on the target.\n4. **Mutate** — DW action with target id and write preview (sk-design decides what, transport\n   executes how).\n5. **Verify** — snapshot / query read-back confirms the postcondition.\n\nEvery mutation step is individually confirmable; destructive steps (DS) add operator confirmation\nplus a version-history rollback statement.\n\n### Action surface\n\n| Module | Actions | Class | Gate |\n|--------|---------|-------|------|\n| dePages | `create_page`, `create_page_folder`, `switch_page` | DW | Designer session; sk-design for layout intent |\n| deElement | `query_elements`, `get_all_elements`, `get_attributes`, `get_display_name`, snapshot | RO | none |\n| deElement | `create_element`, `move_element`, `set_text`, `set_style`, `set_link`, `set_heading_level`, `set_image_asset`, `set_display_name`, `set_attributes`, settings (`set_settings`, `set_dom_id`, `set_tag`, `set_visibility`) | DW | **sk-design pairing required** |\n| deElement | `remove_element`, `remove_attribute`, `remove_style` | DS | operator confirmation; version-history rollback |\n| deStyle | style read/get, create/update/rename, `set_style_variable_mode` | RO/DW | sk-design pairing for DW |\n| deStyle | `remove_style`, `remove_style_variable_mode`, `remove_all_style_variable_modes` | DS | confirmation + rollback |\n| deVariable | get/query, collection + mode + typed variable create/update/rename/reorder | RO/DW | sk-design pairing for DW |\n| deVariable | `delete_variable` | DS | confirmation + rollback |\n| deComponents | read/get, `create_blank_component`, `duplicate_component`, `transform_element_to_component`, `set_component_metadata`, instance insert/unlink, builder (`insert_in_element`/`insert_in_slot`), props create/update/set/reset, variants create/duplicate/set/reorder | RO/DW | sk-design pairing for DW |\n| deComponents | `unregister_component`, `remove_prop`, `delete_variant` | DS | confirmation + rollback |\n| deAsset | asset read/list, create/upload (`upload_image_by_url`), compress, folders | RO/DW | sk-design pairing for DW |\n| deAsset | `delete_asset` | DS | confirmation + rollback |\n| localDeMCPConnection | `get_designer_app_connection_info` | RO | none (diagnostic) |\n\n### Element-tree and token semantics\n\nElements are addressed by `id {component, element}` with `parent_element_id` + `creation_position`\npositions; builder steps carry a `build_label`. `set_style` references **named styles**, not raw\nCSS — ensure the style exists before binding (`create_style` with `properties[]`). Styles bind to\n**variable modes** (`set_style_variable_mode`): create collection → create mode → create typed\nvariables → bind style → apply style to elements; a second mode re-skins the same style without\ntouching elements. Components expose **props** (instance customization), **slots** (`insert_in_slot`\nextension points), and **variants** (style layers via `set_variant_styles`); editing inside the\ncomponent view (`open_component_view`) scopes mutations to the component master. Breakpoints are\ncanvas-bound reads (`get_all_breakpoints`); responsive behavior flows through which styles apply\nand what they contain.\n\n### Safety-critical semantics\n\n- Designer tools require the **Bridge App open in the Designer**; Data API tools work with Webflow\n  closed.\n- Designer edits are **draft-only inside the Designer** — they appear on the live site only after\n  `publish_site` (gated separately).\n- **All Designer-family operations load `sk-design` first** (cross-hub pairing): the transport\n  executes, never decides taste.\n- Branches (`create_branch`, `switch_page` to branch) isolate Designer edits until merge — the\n  natural staging pattern for design work.\n\n### Example prompts\n\n- \"set the hero heading level to H1 in the test site\" → sk-design + deElement DW\n- \"create a variable collection 'Brand' with a mode 'Light'\" → sk-design + deVariable DW\n- \"remove the 'hero' element\" → confirmation + rollback statement (DS)\n\n---\n## 3. SOURCE FILES\n\n### Implementation\n\n| File | Layer | Role |\n|---|---|---|\n| `../../references/designer-capabilities.md` | Shared | Full Designer logic: canvas model, edit loop, element/token/component semantics, worked flows |\n| `../../references/action-reference.md` | Shared | Required parameters per action (Elements, Components, Variables, Style, Designer canvas) |\n| `../../references/tool-surface.md` | Shared | Local OSS baseline where applicable |\n| `../../SKILL.md` | Shared | Frozen classes and gates |\n\n### Validation And Tests\n\n| File | Type | Role |\n|---|---|---|\n| `../../manual-testing-playbook/` | Manual playbook | Designer edit loop scenario (DRAFT-003) and pairing scenarios |\n\n## 4. SOURCE METADATA\n\n- Group: Elements, Components, Variables, Style, Designer canvas\n- Canonical catalog source: `feature-catalog.md`\n- Feature file path: `design/designer.md`\n\nRelated references:\n- [`component-variants.md`](component-variants.md) — related capability\n- [`../../references/designer-capabilities.md`](../../references/designer-capabilities.md) — operational logic","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":127,"totalLines":127,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/design/designer.md","time":{"start":1785759280738,"end":1785759280753}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_07ad784273ab2e15016a7086306f0c8191b12e5d897e1bcb67"}},"id":"prt_fc78c2e440019HpTOsTjonHMUq","sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","messageID":"msg_fc78bc4fb001HhUrnvUSQ0f6pQ"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785759280827,"sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_2S38YQdhQ7ndkpsoI5CQmP7J","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/design/component-variants.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/design/component-variants.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Component variants\"\n3: description: \"Webflow component-variants capability card: the eight data_component_variants_tool actions — variant reads, create/update, default variants, and destructive delete_variant.\"\n4: trigger_phrases: [\"webflow component variants\", \"webflow variants\", \"webflow variant\"]\n5: contextType: implementation\n6: version: 1.0.0.0\n7: \n8: # Component variants\n9: \n10: <!-- sk-doc-template: skill_asset_feature_catalog -->\n11: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n12: \n13: Operates component variant definitions on the remote surface via `data_component_variants_tool`\n14: (read+write; page-building tool — `siteId` and `pageId` required on every action). Variants let a\n15: component change appearance per state; `delete_variant` is destructive.\n16: \n17: ---\n18: ## 2. HOW IT WORKS\n19: \n20: ### Variant Reads\n21: \n22: Reads list and inspect variants for a component (`get_variant_settings` and variant list/get actions) — RO, no gate.\n23: \n24: ### Variant Mutations\n25: \n26: Create, update, set-default, and delete variants — DW for create/update/set-default, DS for `delete_variant` (operator confirmation, irreversible).\n27: \n28: ### Action Table\n29: \n30: | Action | Required parameters | Class |\n31: |--------|---------------------|-------|\n32: | `get_variant_settings` | `component_id`, `variant_id` | RO |\n33: | variant reads (list/get variants for a component) | `component_id` | RO |\n34: | `create_variant` | `component_id`, `name` (+ optional value overrides) | DW |\n35: | `update_variant` / variant setting updates | `component_id`, `variant_id` | DW |\n36: | `set_default_variant` | `component_id`, `variant_id` | DW |\n37: | `delete_variant` | `component_id`, `variant_id` | DS |\n38: \n39: Semantics: variant edits are draft Designer state until the page is published (gated PB\n40: separately); variant naming and value overrides are design-affecting — pair with `sk-design`.\n41: Delete is irreversible via the surface — operator confirmation with before/after listing.\n42: \n43: Example prompts: \"list the variants of the 'Button' component\", \"create a 'hover' variant of the\n44: 'Card' component\", \"delete the 'old-state' variant\" (confirmation).\n45: \n46: ---\n47: ## 3. SOURCE FILES\n48: \n49: ### Implementation\n50: \n51: | File | Layer | Role |\n52: |---|---|---|\n53: | `../../references/action-reference.md` | Shared | Required parameters per action (Components) |\n54: | `../../references/tool-surface.md` | Shared | Local OSS baseline where applicable |\n55: | `../../SKILL.md` | Shared | Frozen classes and gates |\n56: \n57: ### Validation And Tests\n58: \n59: | File | Type | Role |\n60: |---|---|---|\n61: | `../../manual-testing-playbook/` | Manual playbook | Relevant scenarios for this capability |\n62: \n63: \n64: ## 4. SOURCE METADATA\n65: \n66: - Group: Components\n67: - Canonical catalog source: `feature-catalog.md`\n68: - Feature file path: `design/component-variants.md`\n69: \n70: Related references:\n71: - [`designer.md`](designer.md) — related capability\n\n(End of file - total 71 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: \"Component variants\"\ndescription: \"Webflow component-variants capability card: the eight data_component_variants_tool actions — variant reads, create/update, default variants, and destructive delete_variant.\"\ntrigger_phrases: [\"webflow component variants\", \"webflow variants\", \"webflow variant\"]\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.0.0.0\n\n# Component variants\n\n<!-- sk-doc-template: skill_asset_feature_catalog -->\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nOperates component variant definitions on the remote surface via `data_component_variants_tool`\n(read+write; page-building tool — `siteId` and `pageId` required on every action). Variants let a\ncomponent change appearance per state; `delete_variant` is destructive.\n\n---\n## 2. HOW IT WORKS\n\n### Variant Reads","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/design/component-variants.md","text":"---\ntitle: \"Component variants\"\ndescription: \"Webflow component-variants capability card: the eight data_component_variants_tool actions — variant reads, create/update, default variants, and destructive delete_variant.\"\ntrigger_phrases: [\"webflow component variants\", \"webflow variants\", \"webflow variant\"]\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.0.0.0\n\n# Component variants\n\n<!-- sk-doc-template: skill_asset_feature_catalog -->\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nOperates component variant definitions on the remote surface via `data_component_variants_tool`\n(read+write; page-building tool — `siteId` and `pageId` required on every action). Variants let a\ncomponent change appearance per state; `delete_variant` is destructive.\n\n---\n## 2. HOW IT WORKS\n\n### Variant Reads\n\nReads list and inspect variants for a component (`get_variant_settings` and variant list/get actions) — RO, no gate.\n\n### Variant Mutations\n\nCreate, update, set-default, and delete variants — DW for create/update/set-default, DS for `delete_variant` (operator confirmation, irreversible).\n\n### Action Table\n\n| Action | Required parameters | Class |\n|--------|---------------------|-------|\n| `get_variant_settings` | `component_id`, `variant_id` | RO |\n| variant reads (list/get variants for a component) | `component_id` | RO |\n| `create_variant` | `component_id`, `name` (+ optional value overrides) | DW |\n| `update_variant` / variant setting updates | `component_id`, `variant_id` | DW |\n| `set_default_variant` | `component_id`, `variant_id` | DW |\n| `delete_variant` | `component_id`, `variant_id` | DS |\n\nSemantics: variant edits are draft Designer state until the page is published (gated PB\nseparately); variant naming and value overrides are design-affecting — pair with `sk-design`.\nDelete is irreversible via the surface — operator confirmation with before/after listing.\n\nExample prompts: \"list the variants of the 'Button' component\", \"create a 'hover' variant of the\n'Card' component\", \"delete the 'old-state' variant\" (confirmation).\n\n---\n## 3. SOURCE FILES\n\n### Implementation\n\n| File | Layer | Role |\n|---|---|---|\n| `../../references/action-reference.md` | Shared | Required parameters per action (Components) |\n| `../../references/tool-surface.md` | Shared | Local OSS baseline where applicable |\n| `../../SKILL.md` | Shared | Frozen classes and gates |\n\n### Validation And Tests\n\n| File | Type | Role |\n|---|---|---|\n| `../../manual-testing-playbook/` | Manual playbook | Relevant scenarios for this capability |\n\n\n## 4. SOURCE METADATA\n\n- Group: Components\n- Canonical catalog source: `feature-catalog.md`\n- Feature file path: `design/component-variants.md`\n\nRelated references:\n- [`designer.md`](designer.md) — related capability","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":71,"totalLines":71,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/design/component-variants.md","time":{"start":1785759280822,"end":1785759280825}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_07ad784273ab2e15016a7086306f188191927f1d31a46eb3a7"}},"id":"prt_fc78c2e69001qV2SFu17sh6q47","sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","messageID":"msg_fc78bc4fb001HhUrnvUSQ0f6pQ"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785759281007,"sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_PLj9SuVavyFiKzWigMFuCpa2","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/cms.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/cms.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: \"CMS\"\n3: description: \"Webflow CMS capability card: collection/item reads (RO), draft and live writes (DW), publish (PB), and delete (DS) with the frozen gates and CMS-specific semantics.\"\n4: trigger_phrases: [\"webflow cms\", \"webflow collection\", \"webflow cms items\"]\n5: importance_tier: important\n6: contextType: implementation\n7: version: 1.0.0.0\n8: \n9: # CMS\n10: \n11: <!-- sk-doc-template: skill_asset_feature_catalog -->\n12: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n13: \n14: Read, create, update, publish, and delete Webflow CMS collections and items through the `cms`\n15: module of the official MCP server (Data API v2).\n16: \n17: ---\n18: ## 2. HOW IT WORKS\n19: \n20: ### Capabilities\n21: \n22: | Action | Class | Gate |\n23: |--------|-------|------|\n24: | `get_collection_list`, `get_collection_details`, `list_collection_items` | RO | none (scope check) |\n25: | `create_collection`, `create_collection_*_field`, `update_collection_field` | DW | scope check; target id present |\n26: | `create_collection_items`, `update_collection_items` | DW | scope check; **choose draft vs live target explicitly** |\n27: | `publish_collection_items` / `unpublish_collection_items` | PB | operator confirmation; live publish (no staging-domain target — staging policy applies at the site level); 1 publish/min queue |\n28: | `delete_collection_items`, `delete_collection_field` | DS | operator confirmation; before/after listing; rollback = re-publish prior content |\n29: \n30: ### Safety-critical semantics\n31: \n32: - On the **remote surface**, create/update item actions create **drafts**; publishing is a separate\n33:   explicit action (`publish_collection_items`). The local OSS surface additionally allows direct\n34:   live-site writes — never assume draft-safety across surfaces.\n35: - Publishing is a separate explicit action; nothing auto-publishes.\n36: - Delete is permanent via the MCP surface (no trash/revert endpoint); rollback is re-publishing\n37:   prior content — confirm before/after state.\n38: \n39: ### Example prompts\n40: \n41: - RO: \"list the CMS collection items in the test site\"\n42: - DW: \"update the title field of the 'Blog' collection item 'hello-world' to 'Hello Webflow' —\n43:   draft target\"\n44: - PB: \"publish the 'Blog' collection draft items to the staging subdomain\"\n45: - DS (refused without confirmation): \"delete all items in the 'Drafts' collection\"\n46: \n47: ---\n48: ## 3. SOURCE FILES\n49: \n50: ### Implementation\n51: \n52: | File | Layer | Role |\n53: |---|---|---|\n54: | `../../references/action-reference.md` | Shared | Required parameters per action (CMS) |\n55: | `../../references/tool-surface.md` | Shared | Local OSS baseline where applicable |\n56: | `../../SKILL.md` | Shared | Frozen classes and gates |\n57: \n58: ### Validation And Tests\n59: \n60: | File | Type | Role |\n61: |---|---|---|\n62: | `../../manual-testing-playbook/` | Manual playbook | Relevant scenarios for this capability |\n63: \n64: \n65: ## 4. SOURCE METADATA\n66: \n67: - Group: CMS\n68: - Canonical catalog source: `feature-catalog.md`\n69: - Feature file path: `content/cms.md`\n70: \n71: Related references:\n72: - [`publish-deploy.md`](publish-deploy.md) — related capability\n73: - [`localization-fonts-forms.md`](localization-fonts-forms.md) — related capability\n\n(End of file - total 73 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: \"CMS\"\ndescription: \"Webflow CMS capability card: collection/item reads (RO), draft and live writes (DW), publish (PB), and delete (DS) with the frozen gates and CMS-specific semantics.\"\ntrigger_phrases: [\"webflow cms\", \"webflow collection\", \"webflow cms items\"]\nimportance_tier: important\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.0.0.0\n\n# CMS\n\n<!-- sk-doc-template: skill_asset_feature_catalog -->\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nRead, create, update, publish, and delete Webflow CMS collections and items through the `cms`\nmodule of the official MCP server (Data API v2).\n\n---\n## 2. HOW IT WORKS\n\n### Capabilities","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/cms.md","text":"---\ntitle: \"CMS\"\ndescription: \"Webflow CMS capability card: collection/item reads (RO), draft and live writes (DW), publish (PB), and delete (DS) with the frozen gates and CMS-specific semantics.\"\ntrigger_phrases: [\"webflow cms\", \"webflow collection\", \"webflow cms items\"]\nimportance_tier: important\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.0.0.0\n\n# CMS\n\n<!-- sk-doc-template: skill_asset_feature_catalog -->\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nRead, create, update, publish, and delete Webflow CMS collections and items through the `cms`\nmodule of the official MCP server (Data API v2).\n\n---\n## 2. HOW IT WORKS\n\n### Capabilities\n\n| Action | Class | Gate |\n|--------|-------|------|\n| `get_collection_list`, `get_collection_details`, `list_collection_items` | RO | none (scope check) |\n| `create_collection`, `create_collection_*_field`, `update_collection_field` | DW | scope check; target id present |\n| `create_collection_items`, `update_collection_items` | DW | scope check; **choose draft vs live target explicitly** |\n| `publish_collection_items` / `unpublish_collection_items` | PB | operator confirmation; live publish (no staging-domain target — staging policy applies at the site level); 1 publish/min queue |\n| `delete_collection_items`, `delete_collection_field` | DS | operator confirmation; before/after listing; rollback = re-publish prior content |\n\n### Safety-critical semantics\n\n- On the **remote surface**, create/update item actions create **drafts**; publishing is a separate\n  explicit action (`publish_collection_items`). The local OSS surface additionally allows direct\n  live-site writes — never assume draft-safety across surfaces.\n- Publishing is a separate explicit action; nothing auto-publishes.\n- Delete is permanent via the MCP surface (no trash/revert endpoint); rollback is re-publishing\n  prior content — confirm before/after state.\n\n### Example prompts\n\n- RO: \"list the CMS collection items in the test site\"\n- DW: \"update the title field of the 'Blog' collection item 'hello-world' to 'Hello Webflow' —\n  draft target\"\n- PB: \"publish the 'Blog' collection draft items to the staging subdomain\"\n- DS (refused without confirmation): \"delete all items in the 'Drafts' collection\"\n\n---\n## 3. SOURCE FILES\n\n### Implementation\n\n| File | Layer | Role |\n|---|---|---|\n| `../../references/action-reference.md` | Shared | Required parameters per action (CMS) |\n| `../../references/tool-surface.md` | Shared | Local OSS baseline where applicable |\n| `../../SKILL.md` | Shared | Frozen classes and gates |\n\n### Validation And Tests\n\n| File | Type | Role |\n|---|---|---|\n| `../../manual-testing-playbook/` | Manual playbook | Relevant scenarios for this capability |\n\n\n## 4. SOURCE METADATA\n\n- Group: CMS\n- Canonical catalog source: `feature-catalog.md`\n- Feature file path: `content/cms.md`\n\nRelated references:\n- [`publish-deploy.md`](publish-deploy.md) — related capability\n- [`localization-fonts-forms.md`](localization-fonts-forms.md) — related capability","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":73,"totalLines":73,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/cms.md","time":{"start":1785759280996,"end":1785759281006}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_07ad784273ab2e15016a7086306f208191ad5d3d7f0d9c46ac"}},"id":"prt_fc78c2ec00015zvgF8ZFyebqUH","sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","messageID":"msg_fc78bc4fb001HhUrnvUSQ0f6pQ"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785759281074,"sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_pnigKe5buprcI6AplIEVNzOW","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/publish-deploy.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/publish-deploy.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Publish and deploy\"\n3: description: \"Webflow publish/deploy capability card: publish_site, publish_collection_items, run_workflow — staging-first gates, the 1-per-minute queue, and rollback posture.\"\n4: trigger_phrases: [\"webflow publish\", \"webflow staging\", \"webflow deploy\", \"webflow workflow\"]\n5: importance_tier: important\n6: contextType: implementation\n7: version: 1.0.0.0\n8: \n9: # Publish and deploy\n10: \n11: <!-- sk-doc-template: skill_asset_feature_catalog -->\n12: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n13: \n14: Explicitly deploys Webflow content to live or staging: site publish, CMS item publish, and\n15: workflow execution.\n16: \n17: ---\n18: ## 2. HOW IT WORKS\n19: \n20: ### Capabilities\n21: \n22: | Action | Class | Gate |\n23: |--------|-------|------|\n24: | `publish_site` | PB | operator confirmation; body must carry `customDomains` (production) OR `publishToWebflowSubdomain` (staging); optional single `pageId`; one successful publish per minute |\n25: | `publish_collection_items` | PB | operator confirmation; staging-first; 1/min queue |\n26: | `update_page_settings` with publishing-status change | PB | operator confirmation |\n27: | `run_workflow` | DP | operator confirmation; workflow id + inputs; blast radius depends on the workflow definition |\n28: \n29: ### Safety-critical semantics\n30: \n31: - **Staging vs production is structural**: `publishToWebflowSubdomain` (`*.webflow.io`) is the\n32:   only publish target allowed from smoke/test flows — production `customDomains` is forbidden\n33:   there. A single `pageId` limits blast radius.\n34: - Publishing multiple staged pages to staging, then staging to production, publishes all staged\n35:   changes — never mix targets accidentally.\n36: - Rollback = re-publish prior content/snapshot; Designer version history for page-level work.\n37: - Script registration ships with site publish (publish-adjacent — treat as gated).\n38: \n39: ### Example prompts\n40: \n41: - \"publish the 'About' page to the staging subdomain\" → confirmation + `publishToWebflowSubdomain` + `pageId`\n42: - \"run the 'Weekly report' workflow\" → confirmation + named inputs + blast-radius note\n43: - Production publish from any automated flow → REFUSED (fail closed)\n44: \n45: ---\n46: ## 3. SOURCE FILES\n47: \n48: ### Implementation\n49: \n50: | File | Layer | Role |\n51: |---|---|---|\n52: | `../../references/action-reference.md` | Shared | Required parameters per action (Sites, CMS) |\n53: | `../../references/tool-surface.md` | Shared | Local OSS baseline where applicable |\n54: | `../../SKILL.md` | Shared | Frozen classes and gates |\n55: \n56: ### Validation And Tests\n57: \n58: | File | Type | Role |\n59: |---|---|---|\n60: | `../../manual-testing-playbook/` | Manual playbook | Relevant scenarios for this capability |\n61: \n62: \n63: ## 4. SOURCE METADATA\n64: \n65: - Group: Sites, CMS\n66: - Canonical catalog source: `feature-catalog.md`\n67: - Feature file path: `content/publish-deploy.md`\n68: \n69: Related references:\n70: - [`cms.md`](cms.md) — related capability\n71: - [`site-pages-scripts.md`](site-pages-scripts.md) — related capability\n\n(End of file - total 71 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: \"Publish and deploy\"\ndescription: \"Webflow publish/deploy capability card: publish_site, publish_collection_items, run_workflow — staging-first gates, the 1-per-minute queue, and rollback posture.\"\ntrigger_phrases: [\"webflow publish\", \"webflow staging\", \"webflow deploy\", \"webflow workflow\"]\nimportance_tier: important\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.0.0.0\n\n# Publish and deploy\n\n<!-- sk-doc-template: skill_asset_feature_catalog -->\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nExplicitly deploys Webflow content to live or staging: site publish, CMS item publish, and\nworkflow execution.\n\n---\n## 2. HOW IT WORKS\n\n### Capabilities","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/publish-deploy.md","text":"---\ntitle: \"Publish and deploy\"\ndescription: \"Webflow publish/deploy capability card: publish_site, publish_collection_items, run_workflow — staging-first gates, the 1-per-minute queue, and rollback posture.\"\ntrigger_phrases: [\"webflow publish\", \"webflow staging\", \"webflow deploy\", \"webflow workflow\"]\nimportance_tier: important\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.0.0.0\n\n# Publish and deploy\n\n<!-- sk-doc-template: skill_asset_feature_catalog -->\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nExplicitly deploys Webflow content to live or staging: site publish, CMS item publish, and\nworkflow execution.\n\n---\n## 2. HOW IT WORKS\n\n### Capabilities\n\n| Action | Class | Gate |\n|--------|-------|------|\n| `publish_site` | PB | operator confirmation; body must carry `customDomains` (production) OR `publishToWebflowSubdomain` (staging); optional single `pageId`; one successful publish per minute |\n| `publish_collection_items` | PB | operator confirmation; staging-first; 1/min queue |\n| `update_page_settings` with publishing-status change | PB | operator confirmation |\n| `run_workflow` | DP | operator confirmation; workflow id + inputs; blast radius depends on the workflow definition |\n\n### Safety-critical semantics\n\n- **Staging vs production is structural**: `publishToWebflowSubdomain` (`*.webflow.io`) is the\n  only publish target allowed from smoke/test flows — production `customDomains` is forbidden\n  there. A single `pageId` limits blast radius.\n- Publishing multiple staged pages to staging, then staging to production, publishes all staged\n  changes — never mix targets accidentally.\n- Rollback = re-publish prior content/snapshot; Designer version history for page-level work.\n- Script registration ships with site publish (publish-adjacent — treat as gated).\n\n### Example prompts\n\n- \"publish the 'About' page to the staging subdomain\" → confirmation + `publishToWebflowSubdomain` + `pageId`\n- \"run the 'Weekly report' workflow\" → confirmation + named inputs + blast-radius note\n- Production publish from any automated flow → REFUSED (fail closed)\n\n---\n## 3. SOURCE FILES\n\n### Implementation\n\n| File | Layer | Role |\n|---|---|---|\n| `../../references/action-reference.md` | Shared | Required parameters per action (Sites, CMS) |\n| `../../references/tool-surface.md` | Shared | Local OSS baseline where applicable |\n| `../../SKILL.md` | Shared | Frozen classes and gates |\n\n### Validation And Tests\n\n| File | Type | Role |\n|---|---|---|\n| `../../manual-testing-playbook/` | Manual playbook | Relevant scenarios for this capability |\n\n\n## 4. SOURCE METADATA\n\n- Group: Sites, CMS\n- Canonical catalog source: `feature-catalog.md`\n- Feature file path: `content/publish-deploy.md`\n\nRelated references:\n- [`cms.md`](cms.md) — related capability\n- [`site-pages-scripts.md`](site-pages-scripts.md) — related capability","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":71,"totalLines":71,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/publish-deploy.md","time":{"start":1785759281068,"end":1785759281073}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_07ad784273ab2e15016a7086306f288191a92f1f3dcee5a9ff"}},"id":"prt_fc78c2f6a001fTEgeStbd3HobZ","sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","messageID":"msg_fc78bc4fb001HhUrnvUSQ0f6pQ"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785759281125,"sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_BWWq3dNGLVFN5vtpUaQVhTdD","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/site-pages-scripts.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/site-pages-scripts.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Site, pages, scripts, webhooks, enterprise, AI\"\n3: description: \"Webflow site/pages/scripts/webhooks/enterprise/AI capability card: the read-only and draft-write surface beyond CMS and Designer.\"\n4: trigger_phrases: [\"webflow site\", \"webflow pages\", \"webflow scripts\", \"webflow webhooks\", \"webflow enterprise\", \"webflow ai\"]\n5: contextType: implementation\n6: version: 1.0.0.0\n7: \n8: # Site, pages, scripts, webhooks, enterprise, AI\n9: \n10: <!-- sk-doc-template: skill_asset_feature_catalog -->\n11: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n12: \n13: The remaining Data-API modules: site-level reads/publish, page settings and static content,\n14: custom-code scripts, webhooks, Enterprise-gated redirects/robots/activity, and AI Q&A.\n15: \n16: ---\n17: ## 2. HOW IT WORKS\n18: \n19: ### Capabilities\n20: \n21: | Module | Actions | Class |\n22: |--------|---------|-------|\n23: | sites | `list_sites`, `get_site` | RO |\n24: | sites | `publish_site` | PB (see publish-deploy card) |\n25: | pages | `list_pages`, `get_page_metadata`, `get_page_content` | RO |\n26: | pages | `update_page_settings` (SEO/OG/slug/title — schema also carries publishing status) | DW; PB when flipping status |\n27: | pages | `update_static_content` (secondary-locale DOM nodes), page branches (create/update) | DW |\n28: | pages | `delete_branch` (remote) | DS |\n29: | scripts | `list_registered_scripts`, `list_applied_scripts`, `get_page_script` | RO |\n30: | scripts | `add_page_script`, `add_site_script`, `set_page_scripts`, `set_site_scripts`, freeform code upserts, `update_registered_script` | DW (ships with publish) |\n31: | scripts | `delete_all_site_scripts`, `delete_all_page_scripts` | DS |\n32: | webhooks | `list_webhooks`, `get_webhook` | RO |\n33: | webhooks | `create_webhook`, `delete_webhook` | DW / DS (integration config) |\n34: | enterprise | `list_301_redirects`, `get_robots_txt`, `list_site_activity_logs` | RO (Enterprise plan) |\n35: | enterprise | redirects/robots/well-known create-update / delete | DW / DS (Enterprise plan) |\n36: | aiChat | `ask_webflow_ai` | RO |\n37: | comments | `list_comment_threads`, `get_comment_thread`, `list_comment_replies` | RO |\n38: | comments | `create_reply` (remote) | DW |\n39: | rules | `webflow_guide_tool` | RO |\n40: \n41: ### Notes\n42: \n43: - `custom_code` scopes are Data-Client-app-only (site tokens cannot call custom-code endpoints).\n44: - Enterprise module is gated to Enterprise plans; capability varies by workspace tier.\n45: - `update_page_settings` can flip publishing status — review the payload before sending.\n46: \n47: ---\n48: ## 3. SOURCE FILES\n49: \n50: ### Implementation\n51: \n52: | File | Layer | Role |\n53: |---|---|---|\n54: | `../../references/action-reference.md` | Shared | Required parameters per action (Pages, Scripts, Sites, Webhooks, Enterprise, Utility, Comments) |\n55: | `../../references/tool-surface.md` | Shared | Local OSS baseline where applicable |\n56: | `../../SKILL.md` | Shared | Frozen classes and gates |\n57: \n58: ### Validation And Tests\n59: \n60: | File | Type | Role |\n61: |---|---|---|\n62: | `../../manual-testing-playbook/` | Manual playbook | Relevant scenarios for this capability |\n63: \n64: \n65: ## 4. SOURCE METADATA\n66: \n67: - Group: Pages, Scripts, Sites, Webhooks, Enterprise, Utility, Comments\n68: - Canonical catalog source: `feature-catalog.md`\n69: - Feature file path: `content/site-pages-scripts.md`\n70: \n71: Related references:\n72: - [`cms.md`](cms.md) — related capability\n73: - [`publish-deploy.md`](publish-deploy.md) — related capability\n74: - [`sitemap-scripts-assets-whtml.md`](../operations/sitemap-scripts-assets-whtml.md) — related capability\n\n(End of file - total 74 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: \"Site, pages, scripts, webhooks, enterprise, AI\"\ndescription: \"Webflow site/pages/scripts/webhooks/enterprise/AI capability card: the read-only and draft-write surface beyond CMS and Designer.\"\ntrigger_phrases: [\"webflow site\", \"webflow pages\", \"webflow scripts\", \"webflow webhooks\", \"webflow enterprise\", \"webflow ai\"]\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.0.0.0\n\n# Site, pages, scripts, webhooks, enterprise, AI\n\n<!-- sk-doc-template: skill_asset_feature_catalog -->\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nThe remaining Data-API modules: site-level reads/publish, page settings and static content,\ncustom-code scripts, webhooks, Enterprise-gated redirects/robots/activity, and AI Q&A.\n\n---\n## 2. HOW IT WORKS\n\n### Capabilities\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/site-pages-scripts.md","text":"---\ntitle: \"Site, pages, scripts, webhooks, enterprise, AI\"\ndescription: \"Webflow site/pages/scripts/webhooks/enterprise/AI capability card: the read-only and draft-write surface beyond CMS and Designer.\"\ntrigger_phrases: [\"webflow site\", \"webflow pages\", \"webflow scripts\", \"webflow webhooks\", \"webflow enterprise\", \"webflow ai\"]\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.0.0.0\n\n# Site, pages, scripts, webhooks, enterprise, AI\n\n<!-- sk-doc-template: skill_asset_feature_catalog -->\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nThe remaining Data-API modules: site-level reads/publish, page settings and static content,\ncustom-code scripts, webhooks, Enterprise-gated redirects/robots/activity, and AI Q&A.\n\n---\n## 2. HOW IT WORKS\n\n### Capabilities\n\n| Module | Actions | Class |\n|--------|---------|-------|\n| sites | `list_sites`, `get_site` | RO |\n| sites | `publish_site` | PB (see publish-deploy card) |\n| pages | `list_pages`, `get_page_metadata`, `get_page_content` | RO |\n| pages | `update_page_settings` (SEO/OG/slug/title — schema also carries publishing status) | DW; PB when flipping status |\n| pages | `update_static_content` (secondary-locale DOM nodes), page branches (create/update) | DW |\n| pages | `delete_branch` (remote) | DS |\n| scripts | `list_registered_scripts`, `list_applied_scripts`, `get_page_script` | RO |\n| scripts | `add_page_script`, `add_site_script`, `set_page_scripts`, `set_site_scripts`, freeform code upserts, `update_registered_script` | DW (ships with publish) |\n| scripts | `delete_all_site_scripts`, `delete_all_page_scripts` | DS |\n| webhooks | `list_webhooks`, `get_webhook` | RO |\n| webhooks | `create_webhook`, `delete_webhook` | DW / DS (integration config) |\n| enterprise | `list_301_redirects`, `get_robots_txt`, `list_site_activity_logs` | RO (Enterprise plan) |\n| enterprise | redirects/robots/well-known create-update / delete | DW / DS (Enterprise plan) |\n| aiChat | `ask_webflow_ai` | RO |\n| comments | `list_comment_threads`, `get_comment_thread`, `list_comment_replies` | RO |\n| comments | `create_reply` (remote) | DW |\n| rules | `webflow_guide_tool` | RO |\n\n### Notes\n\n- `custom_code` scopes are Data-Client-app-only (site tokens cannot call custom-code endpoints).\n- Enterprise module is gated to Enterprise plans; capability varies by workspace tier.\n- `update_page_settings` can flip publishing status — review the payload before sending.\n\n---\n## 3. SOURCE FILES\n\n### Implementation\n\n| File | Layer | Role |\n|---|---|---|\n| `../../references/action-reference.md` | Shared | Required parameters per action (Pages, Scripts, Sites, Webhooks, Enterprise, Utility, Comments) |\n| `../../references/tool-surface.md` | Shared | Local OSS baseline where applicable |\n| `../../SKILL.md` | Shared | Frozen classes and gates |\n\n### Validation And Tests\n\n| File | Type | Role |\n|---|---|---|\n| `../../manual-testing-playbook/` | Manual playbook | Relevant scenarios for this capability |\n\n\n## 4. SOURCE METADATA\n\n- Group: Pages, Scripts, Sites, Webhooks, Enterprise, Utility, Comments\n- Canonical catalog source: `feature-catalog.md`\n- Feature file path: `content/site-pages-scripts.md`\n\nRelated references:\n- [`cms.md`](cms.md) — related capability\n- [`publish-deploy.md`](publish-deploy.md) — related capability\n- [`sitemap-scripts-assets-whtml.md`](../operations/sitemap-scripts-assets-whtml.md) — related capability","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":74,"totalLines":74,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/site-pages-scripts.md","time":{"start":1785759281120,"end":1785759281124}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_07ad784273ab2e15016a7086306f2c8191ac984cf7909e0362"}},"id":"prt_fc78c2fad0019pavJadf6XpOGv","sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","messageID":"msg_fc78bc4fb001HhUrnvUSQ0f6pQ"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785759281186,"sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_56fBbr38HcbOl9PFs2PySjUN","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/localization-fonts-forms.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/localization-fonts-forms.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Localization, fonts, forms\"\n3: description: \"Webflow localization/fonts/forms capability card: locale management, font CRUD, form submission reads.\"\n4: trigger_phrases: [\"webflow localization\", \"webflow fonts\", \"webflow forms\"]\n5: contextType: implementation\n6: version: 1.0.0.0\n7: \n8: # Localization, fonts, forms\n9: \n10: <!-- sk-doc-template: skill_asset_feature_catalog -->\n11: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n12: \n13: Site-level content capabilities beyond pages/CMS: localization (locales + secondary-locale\n14: content), fonts (upload/manage site fonts), and forms (read submissions).\n15: \n16: ---\n17: ## 2. HOW IT WORKS\n18: \n19: ### Actions\n20: \n21: ### `data_localization_tool` (read+write)\n22: \n23: | Action | Class |\n24: |--------|-------|\n25: | localized page/component content reads (incl. `update_component_properties` reads) | RO |\n26: | update localized page/component content (secondary locales) | DW |\n27: | content deletes within localization | DS |\n28: \n29: ### `data_fonts_tool` (read+write)\n30: \n31: | Action | Class |\n32: |--------|-------|\n33: | font reads (list/get fonts) | RO |\n34: | upload/add font, update font metadata | DW |\n35: | `batch_delete_fonts` | DS |\n36: \n37: ### `data_forms_tool` (read+write)\n38: \n39: | Action | Class |\n40: |--------|-------|\n41: | `list_site_form_submissions` and related reads | RO |\n42: | `delete_form_submission` | DS |\n43: \n44: ### Semantics\n45: \n46: - Localization writes are content changes — review target locale; deletes are DS.\n47: - Font deletes are bulk and irreversible via the surface — DS confirmation.\n48: - Forms reads are read-only (no gate); form config writes are DW.\n49: \n50: ### Example prompts\n51: \n52: - \"list the locales of the test site\"\n53: - \"add a Spanish locale to the test site\"\n54: - \"list the site fonts\" / \"batch delete the unused 'OldFont' family\" (confirmation)\n55: - \"list the form submissions of the 'Contact' form\"\n56: \n57: ---\n58: ## 3. SOURCE FILES\n59: \n60: ### Implementation\n61: \n62: | File | Layer | Role |\n63: |---|---|---|\n64: | `../../references/action-reference.md` | Shared | Required parameters per action (Localization, Fonts, Forms) |\n65: | `../../references/tool-surface.md` | Shared | Local OSS baseline where applicable |\n66: | `../../SKILL.md` | Shared | Frozen classes and gates |\n67: \n68: ### Validation And Tests\n69: \n70: | File | Type | Role |\n71: |---|---|---|\n72: | `../../manual-testing-playbook/` | Manual playbook | Relevant scenarios for this capability |\n73: \n74: \n75: ## 4. SOURCE METADATA\n76: \n77: - Group: Localization, Fonts, Forms\n78: - Canonical catalog source: `feature-catalog.md`\n79: - Feature file path: `content/localization-fonts-forms.md`\n80: \n81: Related references:\n82: - [`cms.md`](cms.md) — related capability\n83: - [`site-pages-scripts.md`](site-pages-scripts.md) — related capability\n\n(End of file - total 83 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: \"Localization, fonts, forms\"\ndescription: \"Webflow localization/fonts/forms capability card: locale management, font CRUD, form submission reads.\"\ntrigger_phrases: [\"webflow localization\", \"webflow fonts\", \"webflow forms\"]\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.0.0.0\n\n# Localization, fonts, forms\n\n<!-- sk-doc-template: skill_asset_feature_catalog -->\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nSite-level content capabilities beyond pages/CMS: localization (locales + secondary-locale\ncontent), fonts (upload/manage site fonts), and forms (read submissions).\n\n---\n## 2. HOW IT WORKS\n\n### Actions\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/localization-fonts-forms.md","text":"---\ntitle: \"Localization, fonts, forms\"\ndescription: \"Webflow localization/fonts/forms capability card: locale management, font CRUD, form submission reads.\"\ntrigger_phrases: [\"webflow localization\", \"webflow fonts\", \"webflow forms\"]\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.0.0.0\n\n# Localization, fonts, forms\n\n<!-- sk-doc-template: skill_asset_feature_catalog -->\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nSite-level content capabilities beyond pages/CMS: localization (locales + secondary-locale\ncontent), fonts (upload/manage site fonts), and forms (read submissions).\n\n---\n## 2. HOW IT WORKS\n\n### Actions\n\n### `data_localization_tool` (read+write)\n\n| Action | Class |\n|--------|-------|\n| localized page/component content reads (incl. `update_component_properties` reads) | RO |\n| update localized page/component content (secondary locales) | DW |\n| content deletes within localization | DS |\n\n### `data_fonts_tool` (read+write)\n\n| Action | Class |\n|--------|-------|\n| font reads (list/get fonts) | RO |\n| upload/add font, update font metadata | DW |\n| `batch_delete_fonts` | DS |\n\n### `data_forms_tool` (read+write)\n\n| Action | Class |\n|--------|-------|\n| `list_site_form_submissions` and related reads | RO |\n| `delete_form_submission` | DS |\n\n### Semantics\n\n- Localization writes are content changes — review target locale; deletes are DS.\n- Font deletes are bulk and irreversible via the surface — DS confirmation.\n- Forms reads are read-only (no gate); form config writes are DW.\n\n### Example prompts\n\n- \"list the locales of the test site\"\n- \"add a Spanish locale to the test site\"\n- \"list the site fonts\" / \"batch delete the unused 'OldFont' family\" (confirmation)\n- \"list the form submissions of the 'Contact' form\"\n\n---\n## 3. SOURCE FILES\n\n### Implementation\n\n| File | Layer | Role |\n|---|---|---|\n| `../../references/action-reference.md` | Shared | Required parameters per action (Localization, Fonts, Forms) |\n| `../../references/tool-surface.md` | Shared | Local OSS baseline where applicable |\n| `../../SKILL.md` | Shared | Frozen classes and gates |\n\n### Validation And Tests\n\n| File | Type | Role |\n|---|---|---|\n| `../../manual-testing-playbook/` | Manual playbook | Relevant scenarios for this capability |\n\n\n## 4. SOURCE METADATA\n\n- Group: Localization, Fonts, Forms\n- Canonical catalog source: `feature-catalog.md`\n- Feature file path: `content/localization-fonts-forms.md`\n\nRelated references:\n- [`cms.md`](cms.md) — related capability\n- [`site-pages-scripts.md`](site-pages-scripts.md) — related capability","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":83,"totalLines":83,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/localization-fonts-forms.md","time":{"start":1785759281180,"end":1785759281184}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_07ad784273ab2e15016a7086306f348191962c4f44d9199e0e"}},"id":"prt_fc78c2fe6001N1E7lnzC27sudc","sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","messageID":"msg_fc78bc4fb001HhUrnvUSQ0f6pQ"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785759281275,"sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_C6I0Lt8nS5NzIMsxX4wx1dmX","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/operations/sitemap-scripts-assets-whtml.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/operations/sitemap-scripts-assets-whtml.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Sitemap, scripts, assets, WHTML\"\n3: description: \"Webflow sitemap/scripts/assets/whtml capability card: bulk sitemap status, the 20-action scripts surface, asset compression, and WHMTL building.\"\n4: trigger_phrases: [\"webflow sitemap\", \"webflow scripts\", \"webflow assets\", \"webflow whtml\"]\n5: contextType: implementation\n6: version: 1.0.0.0\n7: \n8: # Sitemap, scripts, assets, WHTML\n9: \n10: <!-- sk-doc-template: skill_asset_feature_catalog -->\n11: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n12: \n13: The operational surface beyond content: sitemap status bulk updates, the rich custom-code scripts\n14: module, asset management (incl. compression tasks), and WHMTL page building.\n15: \n16: ---\n17: ## 2. HOW IT WORKS\n18: \n19: ### Actions\n20: \n21: ### `data_sitemap_tool` (read+write)\n22: \n23: | Action | Class |\n24: |--------|-------|\n25: | sitemap reads (items/pages status) | RO |\n26: | `bulk_update_items_sitemap_status`, `bulk_update_pages_sitemap_status` | DW (bulk — review selection before write) |\n27: \n28: ### `data_scripts_tool` (read+write) — 20 actions\n29: \n30: | Action class | Examples |\n31: |--------------|----------|\n32: | RO | `get_page_scripts`, `get_site_scripts`, `get_page_freeform_code`, registered/applied lists |\n33: | DW | `add_page_script`, `add_site_script`, `update_registered_script`, freeform code upserts |\n34: | DS | `clear_page_scripts`, `clear_site_scripts`, `delete_registered_script` |\n35: \n36: ### `data_assets_tool` + `asset_tool` + `get_asset_preview` (read+write)\n37: \n38: | Action class | Examples |\n39: |--------------|----------|\n40: | RO | asset lists/gets, `get_asset_preview`, `list_compression_tasks` |\n41: | DW | upload/update assets, compression requests |\n42: | DS | asset deletes |\n43: \n44: ### `data_whtml_builder` (write)\n45: \n46: | Action | Class |\n47: |--------|-------|\n48: | `insert_whtml` (page building via WHTML) | DW (design-affecting → sk-design pairing) |\n49: \n50: ### Semantics\n51: \n52: - Scripts ship with publish: script registration is publish-adjacent; clearing scripts is DS.\n53: - Bulk sitemap updates: confirm the selection before writing (bulk blast radius).\n54: - `insert_whtml` builds page structure — pair with `sk-design` for layout intent.\n55: \n56: ### Example prompts\n57: \n58: - \"update the sitemap status of the 'Blog' collection items to 'noindex'\" (confirmation, bulk)\n59: - \"list the site scripts\" / \"clear all page scripts on the 'About' page\" (confirmation)\n60: - \"compress the hero images of the test site\"\n61: - \"build a two-column section with WHTML on the 'About' page\" (sk-design)\n62: \n63: ---\n64: ## 3. SOURCE FILES\n65: \n66: ### Implementation\n67: \n68: | File | Layer | Role |\n69: |---|---|---|\n70: | `../../references/action-reference.md` | Shared | Required parameters per action (Sitemap, Assets, WHTML, Scripts) |\n71: | `../../references/tool-surface.md` | Shared | Local OSS baseline where applicable |\n72: | `../../SKILL.md` | Shared | Frozen classes and gates |\n73: \n74: ### Validation And Tests\n75: \n76: | File | Type | Role |\n77: |---|---|---|\n78: | `../../manual-testing-playbook/` | Manual playbook | Relevant scenarios for this capability |\n79: \n80: \n81: ## 4. SOURCE METADATA\n82: \n83: - Group: Sitemap, Assets, WHTML, Scripts\n84: - Canonical catalog source: `feature-catalog.md`\n85: - Feature file path: `operations/sitemap-scripts-assets-whtml.md`\n86: \n87: Related references:\n88: - [`site-pages-scripts.md`](../content/site-pages-scripts.md) — related capability\n\n(End of file - total 88 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: \"Sitemap, scripts, assets, WHTML\"\ndescription: \"Webflow sitemap/scripts/assets/whtml capability card: bulk sitemap status, the 20-action scripts surface, asset compression, and WHMTL building.\"\ntrigger_phrases: [\"webflow sitemap\", \"webflow scripts\", \"webflow assets\", \"webflow whtml\"]\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.0.0.0\n\n# Sitemap, scripts, assets, WHTML\n\n<!-- sk-doc-template: skill_asset_feature_catalog -->\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nThe operational surface beyond content: sitemap status bulk updates, the rich custom-code scripts\nmodule, asset management (incl. compression tasks), and WHMTL page building.\n\n---\n## 2. HOW IT WORKS\n\n### Actions\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/operations/sitemap-scripts-assets-whtml.md","text":"---\ntitle: \"Sitemap, scripts, assets, WHTML\"\ndescription: \"Webflow sitemap/scripts/assets/whtml capability card: bulk sitemap status, the 20-action scripts surface, asset compression, and WHMTL building.\"\ntrigger_phrases: [\"webflow sitemap\", \"webflow scripts\", \"webflow assets\", \"webflow whtml\"]\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.0.0.0\n\n# Sitemap, scripts, assets, WHTML\n\n<!-- sk-doc-template: skill_asset_feature_catalog -->\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nThe operational surface beyond content: sitemap status bulk updates, the rich custom-code scripts\nmodule, asset management (incl. compression tasks), and WHMTL page building.\n\n---\n## 2. HOW IT WORKS\n\n### Actions\n\n### `data_sitemap_tool` (read+write)\n\n| Action | Class |\n|--------|-------|\n| sitemap reads (items/pages status) | RO |\n| `bulk_update_items_sitemap_status`, `bulk_update_pages_sitemap_status` | DW (bulk — review selection before write) |\n\n### `data_scripts_tool` (read+write) — 20 actions\n\n| Action class | Examples |\n|--------------|----------|\n| RO | `get_page_scripts`, `get_site_scripts`, `get_page_freeform_code`, registered/applied lists |\n| DW | `add_page_script`, `add_site_script`, `update_registered_script`, freeform code upserts |\n| DS | `clear_page_scripts`, `clear_site_scripts`, `delete_registered_script` |\n\n### `data_assets_tool` + `asset_tool` + `get_asset_preview` (read+write)\n\n| Action class | Examples |\n|--------------|----------|\n| RO | asset lists/gets, `get_asset_preview`, `list_compression_tasks` |\n| DW | upload/update assets, compression requests |\n| DS | asset deletes |\n\n### `data_whtml_builder` (write)\n\n| Action | Class |\n|--------|-------|\n| `insert_whtml` (page building via WHTML) | DW (design-affecting → sk-design pairing) |\n\n### Semantics\n\n- Scripts ship with publish: script registration is publish-adjacent; clearing scripts is DS.\n- Bulk sitemap updates: confirm the selection before writing (bulk blast radius).\n- `insert_whtml` builds page structure — pair with `sk-design` for layout intent.\n\n### Example prompts\n\n- \"update the sitemap status of the 'Blog' collection items to 'noindex'\" (confirmation, bulk)\n- \"list the site scripts\" / \"clear all page scripts on the 'About' page\" (confirmation)\n- \"compress the hero images of the test site\"\n- \"build a two-column section with WHTML on the 'About' page\" (sk-design)\n\n---\n## 3. SOURCE FILES\n\n### Implementation\n\n| File | Layer | Role |\n|---|---|---|\n| `../../references/action-reference.md` | Shared | Required parameters per action (Sitemap, Assets, WHTML, Scripts) |\n| `../../references/tool-surface.md` | Shared | Local OSS baseline where applicable |\n| `../../SKILL.md` | Shared | Frozen classes and gates |\n\n### Validation And Tests\n\n| File | Type | Role |\n|---|---|---|\n| `../../manual-testing-playbook/` | Manual playbook | Relevant scenarios for this capability |\n\n\n## 4. SOURCE METADATA\n\n- Group: Sitemap, Assets, WHTML, Scripts\n- Canonical catalog source: `feature-catalog.md`\n- Feature file path: `operations/sitemap-scripts-assets-whtml.md`\n\nRelated references:\n- [`site-pages-scripts.md`](../content/site-pages-scripts.md) — related capability","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":88,"totalLines":88,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/operations/sitemap-scripts-assets-whtml.md","time":{"start":1785759281264,"end":1785759281271}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_07ad784273ab2e15016a7086306f388191b8b9886a0627fb57"}},"id":"prt_fc78c3035001Gn2sJ7V0ut4Qvs","sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","messageID":"msg_fc78bc4fb001HhUrnvUSQ0f6pQ"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785759281279,"sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_qDhpxDykv6YCZEyiVxf4B7VZ","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/intelligence/agent-instructions.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/intelligence/agent-instructions.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Agent Instructions\"\n3: description: \"Webflow Agent Instructions capability card: create/read/search/update/move/delete site rules and skills — the markdown guidance agents follow per site.\"\n4: trigger_phrases: [\"webflow agent instructions\", \"webflow rules\", \"webflow skills\"]\n5: importance_tier: important\n6: contextType: implementation\n7: version: 1.0.0.0\n8: \n9: # Agent Instructions\n10: \n11: <!-- sk-doc-template: skill_asset_feature_catalog -->\n12: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n13: \n14: Manages a site's agent instructions: markdown-based rules and skills that give agents custom\n15: guidance for working on that site. Instructions can reference Webflow primitives (variables,\n16: styles, components, pages, CMS collections and items, locales, and other instructions), which\n17: resolve server-side against the site's own data.\n18: \n19: ---\n20: ## 2. HOW IT WORKS\n21: \n22: ### Actions (`data_agent_instructions_tool`, read+write)\n23: \n24: | Action | Params | Class |\n25: |--------|--------|-------|\n26: | `search_instructions` | `site_id` | RO |\n27: | `read_instruction` | `site_id`, `path` | RO |\n28: | `create_instruction` | `site_id`, `kind`, `path`, `markdown` | DW |\n29: | `update_instruction` | `site_id`, `kind`, `path` | DW |\n30: | `delete_instruction` | `site_id`, `kind`, `path` | DS |\n31: | `move_instruction` | `site_id`, `kind`, `fromPath`, `toPath` | DW |\n32: \n33: ### Semantics\n34: \n35: - `kind` selects the path grammar (rule vs skill); deleting a skill's `SKILL.md` cascades to all\n36:   its descendants.\n37: - `move_instruction` renames/moves with cascade; the destination must keep the same parent folder.\n38: - This is site-scoped configuration — review content before writing; treat deletion as DS.\n39: \n40: ### Example prompts\n41: \n42: - \"search the agent instructions on the test site\"\n43: - \"create a rule 'always use staging subdomain for publishes' on the test site\"\n44: - \"move the skill 'brand-guidelines' to 'shared/'\" (confirmation for cascading renames)\n45: \n46: ---\n47: ## 3. SOURCE FILES\n48: \n49: ### Implementation\n50: \n51: | File | Layer | Role |\n52: |---|---|---|\n53: | `../../references/action-reference.md` | Shared | Required parameters per action (Agent Instructions) |\n54: | `../../references/tool-surface.md` | Shared | Local OSS baseline where applicable |\n55: | `../../SKILL.md` | Shared | Frozen classes and gates |\n56: \n57: ### Validation And Tests\n58: \n59: | File | Type | Role |\n60: |---|---|---|\n61: | `../../manual-testing-playbook/` | Manual playbook | Relevant scenarios for this capability |\n62: \n63: \n64: ## 4. SOURCE METADATA\n65: \n66: - Group: Agent Instructions\n67: - Canonical catalog source: `feature-catalog.md`\n68: - Feature file path: `intelligence/agent-instructions.md`\n69: \n70: Related references:\n71: - [`analyze.md`](analyze.md) — related capability\n\n(End of file - total 71 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: \"Agent Instructions\"\ndescription: \"Webflow Agent Instructions capability card: create/read/search/update/move/delete site rules and skills — the markdown guidance agents follow per site.\"\ntrigger_phrases: [\"webflow agent instructions\", \"webflow rules\", \"webflow skills\"]\nimportance_tier: important\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.0.0.0\n\n# Agent Instructions\n\n<!-- sk-doc-template: skill_asset_feature_catalog -->\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nManages a site's agent instructions: markdown-based rules and skills that give agents custom\nguidance for working on that site. Instructions can reference Webflow primitives (variables,\nstyles, components, pages, CMS collections and items, locales, and other instructions), which\nresolve server-side against the site's own data.\n\n---\n## 2. HOW IT WORKS","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/intelligence/agent-instructions.md","text":"---\ntitle: \"Agent Instructions\"\ndescription: \"Webflow Agent Instructions capability card: create/read/search/update/move/delete site rules and skills — the markdown guidance agents follow per site.\"\ntrigger_phrases: [\"webflow agent instructions\", \"webflow rules\", \"webflow skills\"]\nimportance_tier: important\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.0.0.0\n\n# Agent Instructions\n\n<!-- sk-doc-template: skill_asset_feature_catalog -->\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nManages a site's agent instructions: markdown-based rules and skills that give agents custom\nguidance for working on that site. Instructions can reference Webflow primitives (variables,\nstyles, components, pages, CMS collections and items, locales, and other instructions), which\nresolve server-side against the site's own data.\n\n---\n## 2. HOW IT WORKS\n\n### Actions (`data_agent_instructions_tool`, read+write)\n\n| Action | Params | Class |\n|--------|--------|-------|\n| `search_instructions` | `site_id` | RO |\n| `read_instruction` | `site_id`, `path` | RO |\n| `create_instruction` | `site_id`, `kind`, `path`, `markdown` | DW |\n| `update_instruction` | `site_id`, `kind`, `path` | DW |\n| `delete_instruction` | `site_id`, `kind`, `path` | DS |\n| `move_instruction` | `site_id`, `kind`, `fromPath`, `toPath` | DW |\n\n### Semantics\n\n- `kind` selects the path grammar (rule vs skill); deleting a skill's `SKILL.md` cascades to all\n  its descendants.\n- `move_instruction` renames/moves with cascade; the destination must keep the same parent folder.\n- This is site-scoped configuration — review content before writing; treat deletion as DS.\n\n### Example prompts\n\n- \"search the agent instructions on the test site\"\n- \"create a rule 'always use staging subdomain for publishes' on the test site\"\n- \"move the skill 'brand-guidelines' to 'shared/'\" (confirmation for cascading renames)\n\n---\n## 3. SOURCE FILES\n\n### Implementation\n\n| File | Layer | Role |\n|---|---|---|\n| `../../references/action-reference.md` | Shared | Required parameters per action (Agent Instructions) |\n| `../../references/tool-surface.md` | Shared | Local OSS baseline where applicable |\n| `../../SKILL.md` | Shared | Frozen classes and gates |\n\n### Validation And Tests\n\n| File | Type | Role |\n|---|---|---|\n| `../../manual-testing-playbook/` | Manual playbook | Relevant scenarios for this capability |\n\n\n## 4. SOURCE METADATA\n\n- Group: Agent Instructions\n- Canonical catalog source: `feature-catalog.md`\n- Feature file path: `intelligence/agent-instructions.md`\n\nRelated references:\n- [`analyze.md`](analyze.md) — related capability","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":71,"totalLines":71,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/intelligence/agent-instructions.md","time":{"start":1785759281273,"end":1785759281277}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_07ad784273ab2e15016a7086306f408191b9550cba15e6c39b"}},"id":"prt_fc78c3072001qP4qOdDy8whXiy","sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","messageID":"msg_fc78bc4fb001HhUrnvUSQ0f6pQ"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785759281336,"sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_PFOg3nepC3stbqfWmbjUeYGP","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/intelligence/analyze.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/intelligence/analyze.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Analyze add-on\"\n3: description: \"Webflow Analyze capability card: traffic trends, ranked pages, ranked dimensions, engagement, time-on-page reports (Analyze add-on required).\"\n4: trigger_phrases: [\"webflow analyze\", \"webflow traffic\", \"webflow analytics\"]\n5: contextType: implementation\n6: version: 1.0.0.0\n7: \n8: # Analyze add-on\n9: \n10: <!-- sk-doc-template: skill_asset_feature_catalog -->\n11: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n12: \n13: Read-only access to Webflow Analyze report data for a site: traffic over time, ranked pages,\n14: ranked dimensions, engagement events, and time on page. Requires the Webflow Analyze add-on;\n15: actions return an error on sites without it.\n16: \n17: ---\n18: ## 2. HOW IT WORKS\n19: \n20: ### Actions (`data_analyze_tool`, read)\n21: \n22: | Action | Params | Class |\n23: |--------|--------|-------|\n24: | `get_query_guide` | none | RO |\n25: | `get_resolve_event_element_guide` | none | RO |\n26: | `get_time_on_page_report` | `site_id`, `startTime`, `endTime`, `metricScope` | RO |\n27: | traffic trend / ranked pages / ranked dimensions / engagement events | `site_id`, date range, filters | RO |\n28: \n29: ### Semantics\n30: \n31: - Use the guide actions first when unsure how to shape a query or trace an event back to the\n32:   element that produced it.\n33: - Read-only: no gates beyond scope check.\n34: \n35: ### Example prompts\n36: \n37: - \"what is the traffic trend for the test site over the last 30 days\"\n38: - \"rank the top pages of the test site by visits\"\n39: - \"break down last week's visits by country\"\n40: \n41: ---\n42: ## 3. SOURCE FILES\n43: \n44: ### Implementation\n45: \n46: | File | Layer | Role |\n47: |---|---|---|\n48: | `../../references/action-reference.md` | Shared | Required parameters per action (Analyze (add-on)) |\n49: | `../../references/tool-surface.md` | Shared | Local OSS baseline where applicable |\n50: | `../../SKILL.md` | Shared | Frozen classes and gates |\n51: \n52: ### Validation And Tests\n53: \n54: | File | Type | Role |\n55: |---|---|---|\n56: | `../../manual-testing-playbook/` | Manual playbook | Relevant scenarios for this capability |\n57: \n58: \n59: ## 4. SOURCE METADATA\n60: \n61: - Group: Analyze (add-on)\n62: - Canonical catalog source: `feature-catalog.md`\n63: - Feature file path: `intelligence/analyze.md`\n64: \n65: Related references:\n66: - [`agent-instructions.md`](agent-instructions.md) — related capability\n\n(End of file - total 66 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: \"Analyze add-on\"\ndescription: \"Webflow Analyze capability card: traffic trends, ranked pages, ranked dimensions, engagement, time-on-page reports (Analyze add-on required).\"\ntrigger_phrases: [\"webflow analyze\", \"webflow traffic\", \"webflow analytics\"]\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.0.0.0\n\n# Analyze add-on\n\n<!-- sk-doc-template: skill_asset_feature_catalog -->\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nRead-only access to Webflow Analyze report data for a site: traffic over time, ranked pages,\nranked dimensions, engagement events, and time on page. Requires the Webflow Analyze add-on;\nactions return an error on sites without it.\n\n---\n## 2. HOW IT WORKS\n\n### Actions (`data_analyze_tool`, read)","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/intelligence/analyze.md","text":"---\ntitle: \"Analyze add-on\"\ndescription: \"Webflow Analyze capability card: traffic trends, ranked pages, ranked dimensions, engagement, time-on-page reports (Analyze add-on required).\"\ntrigger_phrases: [\"webflow analyze\", \"webflow traffic\", \"webflow analytics\"]\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.0.0.0\n\n# Analyze add-on\n\n<!-- sk-doc-template: skill_asset_feature_catalog -->\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nRead-only access to Webflow Analyze report data for a site: traffic over time, ranked pages,\nranked dimensions, engagement events, and time on page. Requires the Webflow Analyze add-on;\nactions return an error on sites without it.\n\n---\n## 2. HOW IT WORKS\n\n### Actions (`data_analyze_tool`, read)\n\n| Action | Params | Class |\n|--------|--------|-------|\n| `get_query_guide` | none | RO |\n| `get_resolve_event_element_guide` | none | RO |\n| `get_time_on_page_report` | `site_id`, `startTime`, `endTime`, `metricScope` | RO |\n| traffic trend / ranked pages / ranked dimensions / engagement events | `site_id`, date range, filters | RO |\n\n### Semantics\n\n- Use the guide actions first when unsure how to shape a query or trace an event back to the\n  element that produced it.\n- Read-only: no gates beyond scope check.\n\n### Example prompts\n\n- \"what is the traffic trend for the test site over the last 30 days\"\n- \"rank the top pages of the test site by visits\"\n- \"break down last week's visits by country\"\n\n---\n## 3. SOURCE FILES\n\n### Implementation\n\n| File | Layer | Role |\n|---|---|---|\n| `../../references/action-reference.md` | Shared | Required parameters per action (Analyze (add-on)) |\n| `../../references/tool-surface.md` | Shared | Local OSS baseline where applicable |\n| `../../SKILL.md` | Shared | Frozen classes and gates |\n\n### Validation And Tests\n\n| File | Type | Role |\n|---|---|---|\n| `../../manual-testing-playbook/` | Manual playbook | Relevant scenarios for this capability |\n\n\n## 4. SOURCE METADATA\n\n- Group: Analyze (add-on)\n- Canonical catalog source: `feature-catalog.md`\n- Feature file path: `intelligence/analyze.md`\n\nRelated references:\n- [`agent-instructions.md`](agent-instructions.md) — related capability","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":66,"totalLines":66,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/intelligence/analyze.md","time":{"start":1785759281327,"end":1785759281333}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_07ad784273ab2e15016a7086306f4481918f35bd7de0edead3"}},"id":"prt_fc78c308c001LQUhI5sYiYnMWI","sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","messageID":"msg_fc78bc4fb001HhUrnvUSQ0f6pQ"}}
