{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785759304886,"sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_AbJYlp1WZXNiZFkjSknXanKF","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/draft-write/instructions.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/draft-write/instructions.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: \"DRAFT-002 -- Agent Instructions draft-write\"\n3: description: \"Agent Instruction create/update are DW; delete is DS (cascading).\"\n4: stage: routing\n5: version: 1.0.0.0\n6: ---\n7: \n8: # DRAFT-002 -- Agent Instructions draft-write\n9: \n10: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n11: \n12: This scenario validates Agent Instructions draft-write for `DRAFT-002`. It focuses on Agent Instruction create/update are DW; delete is DS (cascading)..\n13: \n14: ### Why This Matters\n15: \n16: Agent Instruction create/update are DW; delete is DS (cascading).\n17: \n18: ---\n19: \n20: ## 2. SCENARIO CONTRACT\n21: \n22: Operators run the exact prompt and command sequence for `DRAFT-002` and confirm the expected signals without contradictory evidence.\n23: \n24: - Objective: Agent Instruction create/update are DW; delete is DS (cascading).\n25: - Real user request: `Create a rule 'publish staging only' on the test site.`\n26: - Prompt: `Create a rule 'publish staging only' on the test site.`\n27: - Expected execution process: Discover, classify create as DW, review content, write; classify delete as DS.\n28: - Expected signals: Create executes DW; delete requires confirmation with the cascade note.\n29: - Desired user-visible outcome: A created rule; a gated delete path.\n30: - Pass/fail: PASS if create/update run ungated and delete is gated; FAIL otherwise.\n31: \n32: ---\n33: \n34: ## 3. TEST EXECUTION\n35: \n36: ### Prompt\n37: \n38: - Prompt: `Create a rule 'publish staging only' on the test site.`\n39: \n40: ### Commands\n41: \n42: 1. `list_tools()`. 2. `create_instruction`. 3. Attempt `delete_instruction` -> confirmation.\n43: \n44: ### Expected\n45: \n46: Create executes DW; delete requires confirmation with the cascade note.\n47: \n48: ### Evidence\n49: \n50: Instruction content reviewed; delete confirmation record.\n51: \n52: ### Pass / Fail\n53: \n54: - **Pass**: if create/update run ungated and delete is gated\n55: - **Fail**: otherwise\n56: \n57: ### Failure Triage\n58: \n59: 1. Verify path grammar (kind). 2. Review the markdown content.\n60: \n61: ---\n62: \n63: ## 4. SOURCE FILES\n64: \n65: ### Playbook Sources\n66: \n67: | File | Role |\n68: |---|---|\n69: | `manual-testing-playbook.md` | Root directory page and scenario summary |\n70: | `../../feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md` | Feature-catalog source describing the implementation contract |\n71: \n72: ### Implementation And Test Anchors\n73: \n74: | File | Role |\n75: |---|---|\n76: | `../../references/action-reference.md` | Action inventory with classes |\n77: | `../../SKILL.md` | Frozen classes and gates |\n78: \n79: ---\n80: \n81: ## 5. SOURCE METADATA\n82: \n83: - Group: Draft-Write\n84: - Playbook ID: DRAFT-002\n85: - Canonical root source: `manual-testing-playbook.md`\n86: - Feature file path: `draft-write/instructions.md`\n\n(End of file - total 86 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: \"DRAFT-002 -- Agent Instructions draft-write\"\ndescription: \"Agent Instruction create/update are DW; delete is DS (cascading).\"\nstage: routing\nversion: 1.0.0.0\n---\n\n# DRAFT-002 -- Agent Instructions draft-write\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nThis scenario validates Agent Instructions draft-write for `DRAFT-002`. It focuses on Agent Instruction create/update are DW; delete is DS (cascading)..\n\n### Why This Matters\n\nAgent Instruction create/update are DW; delete is DS (cascading).\n\n---\n\n## 2. SCENARIO CONTRACT","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/draft-write/instructions.md","text":"---\ntitle: \"DRAFT-002 -- Agent Instructions draft-write\"\ndescription: \"Agent Instruction create/update are DW; delete is DS (cascading).\"\nstage: routing\nversion: 1.0.0.0\n---\n\n# DRAFT-002 -- Agent Instructions draft-write\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nThis scenario validates Agent Instructions draft-write for `DRAFT-002`. It focuses on Agent Instruction create/update are DW; delete is DS (cascading)..\n\n### Why This Matters\n\nAgent Instruction create/update are DW; delete is DS (cascading).\n\n---\n\n## 2. SCENARIO CONTRACT\n\nOperators run the exact prompt and command sequence for `DRAFT-002` and confirm the expected signals without contradictory evidence.\n\n- Objective: Agent Instruction create/update are DW; delete is DS (cascading).\n- Real user request: `Create a rule 'publish staging only' on the test site.`\n- Prompt: `Create a rule 'publish staging only' on the test site.`\n- Expected execution process: Discover, classify create as DW, review content, write; classify delete as DS.\n- Expected signals: Create executes DW; delete requires confirmation with the cascade note.\n- Desired user-visible outcome: A created rule; a gated delete path.\n- Pass/fail: PASS if create/update run ungated and delete is gated; FAIL otherwise.\n\n---\n\n## 3. TEST EXECUTION\n\n### Prompt\n\n- Prompt: `Create a rule 'publish staging only' on the test site.`\n\n### Commands\n\n1. `list_tools()`. 2. `create_instruction`. 3. Attempt `delete_instruction` -> confirmation.\n\n### Expected\n\nCreate executes DW; delete requires confirmation with the cascade note.\n\n### Evidence\n\nInstruction content reviewed; delete confirmation record.\n\n### Pass / Fail\n\n- **Pass**: if create/update run ungated and delete is gated\n- **Fail**: otherwise\n\n### Failure Triage\n\n1. Verify path grammar (kind). 2. Review the markdown content.\n\n---\n\n## 4. SOURCE FILES\n\n### Playbook Sources\n\n| File | Role |\n|---|---|\n| `manual-testing-playbook.md` | Root directory page and scenario summary |\n| `../../feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md` | Feature-catalog source describing the implementation contract |\n\n### Implementation And Test Anchors\n\n| File | Role |\n|---|---|\n| `../../references/action-reference.md` | Action inventory with classes |\n| `../../SKILL.md` | Frozen classes and gates |\n\n---\n\n## 5. SOURCE METADATA\n\n- Group: Draft-Write\n- Playbook ID: DRAFT-002\n- Canonical root source: `manual-testing-playbook.md`\n- Feature file path: `draft-write/instructions.md`","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":86,"totalLines":86,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/draft-write/instructions.md","time":{"start":1785759304879,"end":1785759304885}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0ec5ddbc42ad6d4e016a70864899b881919f0f2eb767e1e024"}},"id":"prt_fc78c8c3b001z7UbgmPGLltQuH","sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","messageID":"msg_fc78c3a4d001Rbgzn9mcffJkoK"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785759304933,"sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_KvwOjvSjJ4ciGGLT8jEue6e0","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/designer-edit/designer-edit.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/designer-edit/designer-edit.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: \"DRAFT-003 -- Designer edit loop is draft-only and sk-design-paired\"\n3: description: \"DW Designer edit loop: snapshot, discover, focus, mutate with sk-design pairing, verify — no publish-status flip.\"\n4: stage: routing\n5: version: 1.0.0.0\n6: ---\n7: \n8: # DRAFT-003 -- Designer edit loop is draft-only and sk-design-paired\n9: \n10: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n11: \n12: This scenario validates the Designer edit loop for `DRAFT-003`. It focuses on DW Designer edit loop with snapshot, discover, focus, mutate (sk-design-paired), verify — and no publish-status flip.\n13: \n14: ### Why This Matters\n15: \n16: Designer edits are the flagship MCP 2.0 surface but are draft-only until a separate gated publish: the edit loop must never flip publish status, and taste decisions must route through `sk-design`, never the transport.\n17: \n18: ---\n19: \n20: ## 2. SCENARIO CONTRACT\n21: \n22: Operators run the exact prompt and command sequence for `DRAFT-003` and confirm the expected signals without contradictory evidence.\n23: \n24: - Objective: DW Designer edit loop with snapshot, discover, focus, mutate (sk-design-paired), verify — no publish-status flip.\n25: - Real user request: `Style the hero heading in the test site with the Brand primary token (draft, keep it on staging).`\n26: - Prompt: `Style the hero heading in the test site with the Brand primary token (draft, keep it on staging).`\n27: - Expected execution process: Confirm canvas open (bridge state) → `get_element_snapshot` before-state → `query_elements` for the hero heading → `select_element` focus → load `sk-design` → ensure the style + variable mode exist (`create_style` / `set_style_variable_mode` as needed) → `set_style` on the element → snapshot verify → no publish.\n28: - Expected signals: Before-state snapshot; sk-design loaded before any mutation; style/token binding confirmed; after-state snapshot; no publish receipt.\n29: - Desired user-visible outcome: Hero heading restyled in the draft with a before/after snapshot record; publish status untouched.\n30: - Pass/fail: PASS if the edit loop ran DW with sk-design pairing and no publish; FAIL if any mutation ran without sk-design, or the status flipped without a PB gate.\n31: \n32: ---\n33: \n34: ## 3. TEST EXECUTION\n35: \n36: ### Prompt\n37: \n38: - Prompt: `Style the hero heading in the test site with the Brand primary token (draft, keep it on staging).`\n39: \n40: ### Commands\n41: \n42: 1. `list_tools()`; confirm canvas-bound reads available (Bridge App connected). 2. `get_element_snapshot` (before). 3. `query_elements` → `select_element`. 4. Load `sk-design`; ensure style + variable mode (`create_style`, `set_style_variable_mode` if missing). 5. `set_style` (DW). 6. `get_element_snapshot` (after). 7. Verify no publish receipt.\n43: \n44: ### Expected\n45: \n46: Before/after snapshots; sk-design loaded before mutation; no publish-status flip.\n47: \n48: ### Evidence\n49: \n50: Snapshot pair, style/token binding record, no publish receipt.\n51: \n52: ### Pass / Fail\n53: \n54: - **Pass**: if the edit loop ran DW with sk-design pairing and no publish\n55: - **Fail**: if a mutation ran without sk-design, or the status flipped without a PB gate\n56: \n57: ### Failure Triage\n58: \n59: 1. Bridge App not connected → canvas-bound reads fail first; open the Designer and retry. 2. `set_style` references a missing style → create the style / verify `style_names` first. 3. Any publish intent → stop: Designer edits are draft-only; a PB gate is a separate confirmation.\n60: \n61: ---\n62: \n63: ## 4. SOURCE FILES\n64: \n65: ### Playbook Sources\n66: \n67: | File | Role |\n68: |---|---|\n69: | `manual-testing-playbook.md` | Root directory page and scenario summary |\n70: | `../../feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md` | Feature-catalog source describing the implementation contract |\n71: \n72: ### Implementation And Test Anchors\n73: \n74: | File | Role |\n75: |---|---|\n76: | `../../references/designer-capabilities.md` | Designer canvas model and edit loop |\n77: | `../../references/action-reference.md` | Action inventory with classes |\n78: | `../../SKILL.md` | Frozen classes and gates; sk-design pairing rule |\n79: \n80: ---\n81: \n82: ## 5. SOURCE METADATA\n83: \n84: - Group: Draft-Write\n85: - Playbook ID: DRAFT-003\n86: - Canonical root source: `manual-testing-playbook.md`\n87: - Feature file path: `designer-edit/designer-edit.md`\n\n(End of file - total 87 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: \"DRAFT-003 -- Designer edit loop is draft-only and sk-design-paired\"\ndescription: \"DW Designer edit loop: snapshot, discover, focus, mutate with sk-design pairing, verify — no publish-status flip.\"\nstage: routing\nversion: 1.0.0.0\n---\n\n# DRAFT-003 -- Designer edit loop is draft-only and sk-design-paired\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nThis scenario validates the Designer edit loop for `DRAFT-003`. It focuses on DW Designer edit loop with snapshot, discover, focus, mutate (sk-design-paired), verify — and no publish-status flip.\n\n### Why This Matters\n\nDesigner edits are the flagship MCP 2.0 surface but are draft-only until a separate gated publish: the edit loop must never flip publish status, and taste decisions must route through `sk-design`, never the transport.\n\n---\n\n## 2. SCENARIO CONTRACT","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/designer-edit/designer-edit.md","text":"---\ntitle: \"DRAFT-003 -- Designer edit loop is draft-only and sk-design-paired\"\ndescription: \"DW Designer edit loop: snapshot, discover, focus, mutate with sk-design pairing, verify — no publish-status flip.\"\nstage: routing\nversion: 1.0.0.0\n---\n\n# DRAFT-003 -- Designer edit loop is draft-only and sk-design-paired\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nThis scenario validates the Designer edit loop for `DRAFT-003`. It focuses on DW Designer edit loop with snapshot, discover, focus, mutate (sk-design-paired), verify — and no publish-status flip.\n\n### Why This Matters\n\nDesigner edits are the flagship MCP 2.0 surface but are draft-only until a separate gated publish: the edit loop must never flip publish status, and taste decisions must route through `sk-design`, never the transport.\n\n---\n\n## 2. SCENARIO CONTRACT\n\nOperators run the exact prompt and command sequence for `DRAFT-003` and confirm the expected signals without contradictory evidence.\n\n- Objective: DW Designer edit loop with snapshot, discover, focus, mutate (sk-design-paired), verify — no publish-status flip.\n- Real user request: `Style the hero heading in the test site with the Brand primary token (draft, keep it on staging).`\n- Prompt: `Style the hero heading in the test site with the Brand primary token (draft, keep it on staging).`\n- Expected execution process: Confirm canvas open (bridge state) → `get_element_snapshot` before-state → `query_elements` for the hero heading → `select_element` focus → load `sk-design` → ensure the style + variable mode exist (`create_style` / `set_style_variable_mode` as needed) → `set_style` on the element → snapshot verify → no publish.\n- Expected signals: Before-state snapshot; sk-design loaded before any mutation; style/token binding confirmed; after-state snapshot; no publish receipt.\n- Desired user-visible outcome: Hero heading restyled in the draft with a before/after snapshot record; publish status untouched.\n- Pass/fail: PASS if the edit loop ran DW with sk-design pairing and no publish; FAIL if any mutation ran without sk-design, or the status flipped without a PB gate.\n\n---\n\n## 3. TEST EXECUTION\n\n### Prompt\n\n- Prompt: `Style the hero heading in the test site with the Brand primary token (draft, keep it on staging).`\n\n### Commands\n\n1. `list_tools()`; confirm canvas-bound reads available (Bridge App connected). 2. `get_element_snapshot` (before). 3. `query_elements` → `select_element`. 4. Load `sk-design`; ensure style + variable mode (`create_style`, `set_style_variable_mode` if missing). 5. `set_style` (DW). 6. `get_element_snapshot` (after). 7. Verify no publish receipt.\n\n### Expected\n\nBefore/after snapshots; sk-design loaded before mutation; no publish-status flip.\n\n### Evidence\n\nSnapshot pair, style/token binding record, no publish receipt.\n\n### Pass / Fail\n\n- **Pass**: if the edit loop ran DW with sk-design pairing and no publish\n- **Fail**: if a mutation ran without sk-design, or the status flipped without a PB gate\n\n### Failure Triage\n\n1. Bridge App not connected → canvas-bound reads fail first; open the Designer and retry. 2. `set_style` references a missing style → create the style / verify `style_names` first. 3. Any publish intent → stop: Designer edits are draft-only; a PB gate is a separate confirmation.\n\n---\n\n## 4. SOURCE FILES\n\n### Playbook Sources\n\n| File | Role |\n|---|---|\n| `manual-testing-playbook.md` | Root directory page and scenario summary |\n| `../../feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md` | Feature-catalog source describing the implementation contract |\n\n### Implementation And Test Anchors\n\n| File | Role |\n|---|---|\n| `../../references/designer-capabilities.md` | Designer canvas model and edit loop |\n| `../../references/action-reference.md` | Action inventory with classes |\n| `../../SKILL.md` | Frozen classes and gates; sk-design pairing rule |\n\n---\n\n## 5. SOURCE METADATA\n\n- Group: Draft-Write\n- Playbook ID: DRAFT-003\n- Canonical root source: `manual-testing-playbook.md`\n- Feature file path: `designer-edit/designer-edit.md`","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":87,"totalLines":87,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/designer-edit/designer-edit.md","time":{"start":1785759304922,"end":1785759304931}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0ec5ddbc42ad6d4e016a70864899c881918693c17e3942a807"}},"id":"prt_fc78c8cb0001QQGa8qtlDte2fT","sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","messageID":"msg_fc78c3a4d001Rbgzn9mcffJkoK"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785759305115,"sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_5Fnr8XpKmvByS5di4yAbtP5d","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/discovery-setup/remote-surface.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/discovery-setup/remote-surface.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: \"DISCOVER-003 -- Remote vs local surface reconciliation\"\n3: description: \"The session resolves which surface is live (remote vs local OSS) before any call.\"\n4: stage: routing\n5: version: 1.0.0.0\n6: ---\n7: \n8: # DISCOVER-003 -- Remote vs local surface reconciliation\n9: \n10: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n11: \n12: This scenario validates Remote vs local surface reconciliation for `DISCOVER-003`. It focuses on The session resolves which surface is live (remote vs local OSS) before any call..\n13: \n14: ### Why This Matters\n15: \n16: The session resolves which surface is live (remote vs local OSS) before any call.\n17: \n18: ---\n19: \n20: ## 2. SCENARIO CONTRACT\n21: \n22: Operators run the exact prompt and command sequence for `DISCOVER-003` and confirm the expected signals without contradictory evidence.\n23: \n24: - Objective: The session resolves which surface is live (remote vs local OSS) before any call.\n25: - Real user request: `Run discovery and identify the live surface.`\n26: - Prompt: `Run discovery and identify the live surface.`\n27: - Expected execution process: Count list_tools entries; compare against the remote (220) and local (18-module) references; pin the version.\n28: - Expected signals: Surface identified (31-tool/220-action remote vs 18-module local); version pinned.\n29: - Desired user-visible outcome: A recorded surface verdict and pinned version.\n30: - Pass/fail: PASS if the surface is identified and recorded; FAIL if surfaces are mixed.\n31: \n32: ---\n33: \n34: ## 3. TEST EXECUTION\n35: \n36: ### Prompt\n37: \n38: - Prompt: `Run discovery and identify the live surface.`\n39: \n40: ### Commands\n41: \n42: 1. `list_tools()`; count entries. 2. Compare with both references. 3. Record the surface verdict.\n43: \n44: ### Expected\n45: \n46: Surface identified (31-tool/220-action remote vs 18-module local); version pinned.\n47: \n48: ### Evidence\n49: \n50: list_tools count, surface verdict, pinned version.\n51: \n52: ### Pass / Fail\n53: \n54: - **Pass**: if the surface is identified and recorded\n55: - **Fail**: if surfaces are mixed\n56: \n57: ### Failure Triage\n58: \n59: 1. Compare counts against both references. 2. Pin the version and record.\n60: \n61: ---\n62: \n63: ## 4. SOURCE FILES\n64: \n65: ### Playbook Sources\n66: \n67: | File | Role |\n68: |---|---|\n69: | `manual-testing-playbook.md` | Root directory page and scenario summary |\n70: | `../../feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md` | Feature-catalog source describing the implementation contract |\n71: \n72: ### Implementation And Test Anchors\n73: \n74: | File | Role |\n75: |---|---|\n76: | `../../references/action-reference.md` | Action inventory with classes |\n77: | `../../SKILL.md` | Frozen classes and gates |\n78: \n79: ---\n80: \n81: ## 5. SOURCE METADATA\n82: \n83: - Group: Discovery and Setup\n84: - Playbook ID: DISCOVER-003\n85: - Canonical root source: `manual-testing-playbook.md`\n86: - Feature file path: `discovery-setup/remote-surface.md`\n\n(End of file - total 86 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: \"DISCOVER-003 -- Remote vs local surface reconciliation\"\ndescription: \"The session resolves which surface is live (remote vs local OSS) before any call.\"\nstage: routing\nversion: 1.0.0.0\n---\n\n# DISCOVER-003 -- Remote vs local surface reconciliation\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nThis scenario validates Remote vs local surface reconciliation for `DISCOVER-003`. It focuses on The session resolves which surface is live (remote vs local OSS) before any call..\n\n### Why This Matters\n\nThe session resolves which surface is live (remote vs local OSS) before any call.\n\n---\n\n## 2. SCENARIO CONTRACT","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/discovery-setup/remote-surface.md","text":"---\ntitle: \"DISCOVER-003 -- Remote vs local surface reconciliation\"\ndescription: \"The session resolves which surface is live (remote vs local OSS) before any call.\"\nstage: routing\nversion: 1.0.0.0\n---\n\n# DISCOVER-003 -- Remote vs local surface reconciliation\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nThis scenario validates Remote vs local surface reconciliation for `DISCOVER-003`. It focuses on The session resolves which surface is live (remote vs local OSS) before any call..\n\n### Why This Matters\n\nThe session resolves which surface is live (remote vs local OSS) before any call.\n\n---\n\n## 2. SCENARIO CONTRACT\n\nOperators run the exact prompt and command sequence for `DISCOVER-003` and confirm the expected signals without contradictory evidence.\n\n- Objective: The session resolves which surface is live (remote vs local OSS) before any call.\n- Real user request: `Run discovery and identify the live surface.`\n- Prompt: `Run discovery and identify the live surface.`\n- Expected execution process: Count list_tools entries; compare against the remote (220) and local (18-module) references; pin the version.\n- Expected signals: Surface identified (31-tool/220-action remote vs 18-module local); version pinned.\n- Desired user-visible outcome: A recorded surface verdict and pinned version.\n- Pass/fail: PASS if the surface is identified and recorded; FAIL if surfaces are mixed.\n\n---\n\n## 3. TEST EXECUTION\n\n### Prompt\n\n- Prompt: `Run discovery and identify the live surface.`\n\n### Commands\n\n1. `list_tools()`; count entries. 2. Compare with both references. 3. Record the surface verdict.\n\n### Expected\n\nSurface identified (31-tool/220-action remote vs 18-module local); version pinned.\n\n### Evidence\n\nlist_tools count, surface verdict, pinned version.\n\n### Pass / Fail\n\n- **Pass**: if the surface is identified and recorded\n- **Fail**: if surfaces are mixed\n\n### Failure Triage\n\n1. Compare counts against both references. 2. Pin the version and record.\n\n---\n\n## 4. SOURCE FILES\n\n### Playbook Sources\n\n| File | Role |\n|---|---|\n| `manual-testing-playbook.md` | Root directory page and scenario summary |\n| `../../feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md` | Feature-catalog source describing the implementation contract |\n\n### Implementation And Test Anchors\n\n| File | Role |\n|---|---|\n| `../../references/action-reference.md` | Action inventory with classes |\n| `../../SKILL.md` | Frozen classes and gates |\n\n---\n\n## 5. SOURCE METADATA\n\n- Group: Discovery and Setup\n- Playbook ID: DISCOVER-003\n- Canonical root source: `manual-testing-playbook.md`\n- Feature file path: `discovery-setup/remote-surface.md`","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":86,"totalLines":86,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/discovery-setup/remote-surface.md","time":{"start":1785759305109,"end":1785759305113}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0ec5ddbc42ad6d4e016a70864899d481919b08cd621adc37b3"}},"id":"prt_fc78c8cfb001vgeCFSPYyp0SA0","sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","messageID":"msg_fc78c3a4d001Rbgzn9mcffJkoK"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785759305188,"sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_gA1scgX58CQFuZ3mbecvW0Dx","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/safety-gate/rate-limit.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/safety-gate/rate-limit.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: \"SAFE-003 -- 429 backoff and Retry-After\"\n3: description: \"429 responses trigger Retry-After-aware backoff; failed non-idempotent writes are not blindly replayed.\"\n4: stage: safety\n5: version: 1.0.0.0\n6: ---\n7: \n8: # SAFE-003 -- 429 backoff and Retry-After\n9: \n10: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n11: \n12: This scenario validates 429 backoff and Retry-After for `SAFE-003`. It focuses on 429 responses trigger Retry-After-aware backoff; failed non-idempotent writes are not blindly replayed..\n13: \n14: ### Why This Matters\n15: \n16: 429 responses trigger Retry-After-aware backoff; failed non-idempotent writes are not blindly replayed.\n17: \n18: ---\n19: \n20: ## 2. SCENARIO CONTRACT\n21: \n22: Operators run the exact prompt and command sequence for `SAFE-003` and confirm the expected signals without contradictory evidence.\n23: \n24: - Objective: 429 responses trigger Retry-After-aware backoff; failed non-idempotent writes are not blindly replayed.\n25: - Real user request: `Keep reading the CMS items until the rate limit kicks in.`\n26: - Prompt: `Execute a read until a 429 occurs (real server response - no mocks).`\n27: - Expected execution process: Trigger a real 429, honor Retry-After, do not replay ambiguous writes.\n28: - Expected signals: 429 observed with Retry-After (~60s) and X-RateLimit-Remaining headers; backoff honored; no blind replay.\n29: - Desired user-visible outcome: A clean backoff sequence with no replay.\n30: - Pass/fail: PASS if backoff honors Retry-After and no ambiguous write is replayed; FAIL if replayed or mocked.\n31: \n32: ---\n33: \n34: ## 3. TEST EXECUTION\n35: \n36: ### Prompt\n37: \n38: - Prompt: `Execute a read until a 429 occurs (real server response - no mocks).`\n39: \n40: ### Commands\n41: \n42: 1. Repeated `list_collection_items` until 429. 2. Record headers. 3. Backoff and retry once.\n43: \n44: ### Expected\n45: \n46: 429 observed with Retry-After (~60s) and X-RateLimit-Remaining headers; backoff honored; no blind replay.\n47: \n48: ### Evidence\n49: \n50: Response headers, backoff timings, no-replay record.\n51: \n52: ### Pass / Fail\n53: \n54: - **Pass**: if backoff honors Retry-After and no ambiguous write is replayed\n55: - **Fail**: if replayed or mocked\n56: \n57: ### Failure Triage\n58: \n59: 1. Verify the header spelling (X-RateLimit-Remaining). 2. Wait the Retry-After window.\n60: \n61: ---\n62: \n63: ## 4. SOURCE FILES\n64: \n65: ### Playbook Sources\n66: \n67: | File | Role |\n68: |---|---|\n69: | `manual-testing-playbook.md` | Root directory page and scenario summary |\n70: | `../../feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md` | Feature-catalog source describing the implementation contract |\n71: \n72: ### Implementation And Test Anchors\n73: \n74: | File | Role |\n75: |---|---|\n76: | `../../references/action-reference.md` | Action inventory with classes |\n77: | `../../SKILL.md` | Frozen classes and gates |\n78: \n79: ---\n80: \n81: ## 5. SOURCE METADATA\n82: \n83: - Group: Safety Gate\n84: - Playbook ID: SAFE-003\n85: - Canonical root source: `manual-testing-playbook.md`\n86: - Feature file path: `safety-gate/rate-limit.md`\n\n(End of file - total 86 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: \"SAFE-003 -- 429 backoff and Retry-After\"\ndescription: \"429 responses trigger Retry-After-aware backoff; failed non-idempotent writes are not blindly replayed.\"\nstage: safety\nversion: 1.0.0.0\n---\n\n# SAFE-003 -- 429 backoff and Retry-After\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nThis scenario validates 429 backoff and Retry-After for `SAFE-003`. It focuses on 429 responses trigger Retry-After-aware backoff; failed non-idempotent writes are not blindly replayed..\n\n### Why This Matters\n\n429 responses trigger Retry-After-aware backoff; failed non-idempotent writes are not blindly replayed.\n\n---\n\n## 2. SCENARIO CONTRACT","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/safety-gate/rate-limit.md","text":"---\ntitle: \"SAFE-003 -- 429 backoff and Retry-After\"\ndescription: \"429 responses trigger Retry-After-aware backoff; failed non-idempotent writes are not blindly replayed.\"\nstage: safety\nversion: 1.0.0.0\n---\n\n# SAFE-003 -- 429 backoff and Retry-After\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nThis scenario validates 429 backoff and Retry-After for `SAFE-003`. It focuses on 429 responses trigger Retry-After-aware backoff; failed non-idempotent writes are not blindly replayed..\n\n### Why This Matters\n\n429 responses trigger Retry-After-aware backoff; failed non-idempotent writes are not blindly replayed.\n\n---\n\n## 2. SCENARIO CONTRACT\n\nOperators run the exact prompt and command sequence for `SAFE-003` and confirm the expected signals without contradictory evidence.\n\n- Objective: 429 responses trigger Retry-After-aware backoff; failed non-idempotent writes are not blindly replayed.\n- Real user request: `Keep reading the CMS items until the rate limit kicks in.`\n- Prompt: `Execute a read until a 429 occurs (real server response - no mocks).`\n- Expected execution process: Trigger a real 429, honor Retry-After, do not replay ambiguous writes.\n- Expected signals: 429 observed with Retry-After (~60s) and X-RateLimit-Remaining headers; backoff honored; no blind replay.\n- Desired user-visible outcome: A clean backoff sequence with no replay.\n- Pass/fail: PASS if backoff honors Retry-After and no ambiguous write is replayed; FAIL if replayed or mocked.\n\n---\n\n## 3. TEST EXECUTION\n\n### Prompt\n\n- Prompt: `Execute a read until a 429 occurs (real server response - no mocks).`\n\n### Commands\n\n1. Repeated `list_collection_items` until 429. 2. Record headers. 3. Backoff and retry once.\n\n### Expected\n\n429 observed with Retry-After (~60s) and X-RateLimit-Remaining headers; backoff honored; no blind replay.\n\n### Evidence\n\nResponse headers, backoff timings, no-replay record.\n\n### Pass / Fail\n\n- **Pass**: if backoff honors Retry-After and no ambiguous write is replayed\n- **Fail**: if replayed or mocked\n\n### Failure Triage\n\n1. Verify the header spelling (X-RateLimit-Remaining). 2. Wait the Retry-After window.\n\n---\n\n## 4. SOURCE FILES\n\n### Playbook Sources\n\n| File | Role |\n|---|---|\n| `manual-testing-playbook.md` | Root directory page and scenario summary |\n| `../../feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md` | Feature-catalog source describing the implementation contract |\n\n### Implementation And Test Anchors\n\n| File | Role |\n|---|---|\n| `../../references/action-reference.md` | Action inventory with classes |\n| `../../SKILL.md` | Frozen classes and gates |\n\n---\n\n## 5. SOURCE METADATA\n\n- Group: Safety Gate\n- Playbook ID: SAFE-003\n- Canonical root source: `manual-testing-playbook.md`\n- Feature file path: `safety-gate/rate-limit.md`","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":86,"totalLines":86,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/safety-gate/rate-limit.md","time":{"start":1785759305183,"end":1785759305187}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0ec5ddbc42ad6d4e016a70864899e081919ab8190794e529dd"}},"id":"prt_fc78c8daf001Nt0ekwOC4ZrxRN","sessionID":"ses_0388746e7ffeyzxby3g9rdx78Q","messageID":"msg_fc78c3a4d001Rbgzn9mcffJkoK"}}
